is_a: HP:0030680 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0001645
name: Sudden cardiac death
def: "The heart suddenly and unexpectedly stops beating resulting in death within a short time period (generally within 1 h of symptom onset)." []
is_a: HP:0001695 ! Cardiac arrest
is_a: HP:0001699 ! Sudden death

[Term]
id: HP:0001646
name: Abnormal aortic valve morphology
def: "Any abnormality of the aortic valve." []
xref: Fyler:1400
xref: Fyler:1408
is_a: HP:0001654 ! Abnormal heart valve morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0001647
name: Bicuspid aortic valve
def: "The presence of an aortic valve with two instead of the normal three cusps (flaps). Bicuspid aortic valvue is a malformation of a commissure (small space between the attachment of each cusp to the aortic wall) and the adjacent parts of the two corresponding cusps forming a raphe (the fused area of the two underdeveloped cusps turning into a malformed commissure between both cusps; the raphe is a fibrous ridge that extends from the commissure to the free edge of the two underdeveloped, conjoint cusps)." []
is_a: HP:0031567 ! Abnormal aortic valve cusp morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0001649
name: Tachycardia
def: "A rapid heartrate that exceeds the range of the normal resting heartrate for age." []
synonym: "Elevated heart rate" RELATED layperson []
synonym: "Increased heart rate" RELATED layperson []
synonym: "Rapid heart beat" RELATED layperson []
