[Term]
id: HP:0012727
name: Thoracic aortic aneurysm
def: "An abnormal localized widening (dilatation) of the thoracic aorta." []
is_a: HP:0004942 ! Aortic aneurysm

[Term]
id: HP:0020114
name: Persistent human papillomavirus infection
def: "Human papillomaviruses (HPVs) are small oncogenic viruses. HPV has been shown to cause a variety of lesions and malignancies, which predominantly affect the anogenital region. Low-risk, non-oncogenic HPV types are associated with anogenital warts and recurrent respiratory papillomatosis while high-risk, oncogenic types are associated with cervical, penile, anal, vaginal, vulvar, and oropharyngeal cancers. Infection with anogenital HPV is usually asymptomatic and resolves spontaneously without consequences in the immunocompetent host. When disease does occur, the most common manifestation is genital warts, which may be small papules, or flat, smooth or pedunculated lesions. This resolution of HPV lesions is not generally seen in the immunosuppressed, resulting in severe, persistent and extensive manifestations of HPV disease." []
is_a: HP:0032169 ! Severe infection

[Term]
id: HP:0020129
name: Abnormal urine protein level
def: "Any deviation of the concentration of one or more proteins in the urine." []
is_a: HP:0033354 ! Abnormal urine metabolite level

[Term]
id: HP:0020169
name: Abnormal drug response
def: "An anomalous response to a medication related to individual variation in metabolic or immune response to drugs varying from potentially from potentially life-threatening adverse drug reactions to alteration of therapeutic efficacy." []
is_a: HP:0001939 ! Abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis

[Term]
id: HP:0020172
name: Adverse drug response
def: "An unpleasant or harmful reaction resulting from treatment with a drug." []
is_a: HP:0020169 ! Abnormal drug response

[Term]
id: HP:0020347
name: Abnormal circulating monosaccharide concentration
def: "A deviation from the normal concentration of a monosaccharide in the blood circulation." []
is_a: HP:0011013 ! Abnormal circulating carbohydrate concentration

[Term]
id: HP:0025015
name: Abnormal vascular morphology
is_a: HP:0002597 ! Abnormality of the vasculature
is_a: HP:0030680 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0025031
name: Abnormality of the digestive system
is_a: HP:0000118 ! Phenotypic abnormality

[Term]
id: HP:0025142
name: Constitutional symptom
def: "A symptom or manifestation indicating a systemic or general effect of a disease and that may affect the general well-being or status of an individual." []
is_a: HP:0000118 ! Phenotypic abnormality

[Term]
id: HP:0025169
name: Left ventricular systolic dysfunction
def: "Abnormality of left ventricular contraction, often defined operationally as an ejection fraction of less than 40 percent." []
is_a: HP:0005162 ! Abnormal left ventricular function

[Term]
id: HP:0025323
name: Abnormal arterial physiology
def: "An anomaly of arterial function." []
is_a: HP:0030163 ! Abnormal vascular physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0025423
name: Abnormal larynx morphology
def: "Any anomaly of the structure of the larynx." []
is_a: HP:0001600 ! Abnormality of the larynx

[Term]
id: HP:0025502
name: Overweight
def: "Increased body weight with a body mass index of 25-29.9 kg per square meter." []
is_a: HP:0004324 ! Increased body weight

[Term]
id: HP:0025722
name: Cerebral infarct
def: "A necrotic lesion in the cerebrum resulting from a sudden insufficiency of arterial or venous blood supply due to emboli, thrombi or mechanical factors." []
is_a: HP:0002060 ! Abnormal cerebral morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0025766
name: Abnormal affect
def: "An anomaly in intensity, frequency, or duration of the verbal or behavioral expression of emotions, feelings, or thoughts." []
is_a: HP:0011446 ! Abnormality of mental function

[Term]
id: HP:0025780
name: Abnormal volitional state
def: "An abnormality of internal states of motivation or drive that compromise, or interfere with, the ability of the person to attend to basic personal, social, or vocational activities." []
synonym: "Abnormal energy" RELATED []
synonym: "Abnormal motivation" RELATED []
is_a: HP:0025766 ! Abnormal affect

[Term]
id: HP:0030163
name: Abnormal vascular physiology
def: "Abnormality of vascular function." []
is_a: HP:0002597 ! Abnormality of the vasculature
is_a: HP:0011025 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0030680
name: Abnormal cardiovascular system morphology
def: "Any structural anomaly of the heart and blood vessels." []
is_a: HP:0001626 ! Abnormality of the cardiovascular system

[Term]
id: HP:0030828
name: Wheezing
def: "A high-pitched whistling sound associated with labored breathing." []
is_a: HP:0030829 ! Abnormal breath sound

[Term]
id: HP:0030829
name: Abnormal breath sound
def: "An anomalous (adventitious) sound produced by the breathing process." []
is_a: HP:0002795 ! Abnormal respiratory system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0030858
name: Addictive behavior
def: "When an activity, substance, object, or behavior becomes a major focus of a person's life, excluding other activities, or has begun to harm the individual or others physically, mentally, or socially, it can be considered addictive behavior. A person can become addicted or compulsively engaged with anything." []
is_a: HP:5200241 ! Recurrent maladaptive behavior

[Term]
id: HP:0030872
name: Abnormal cardiac ventricular function
def: "An abnormality of the cardiac ventricular function." []
is_a: HP:0011025 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0030956
name: Abnormality of cardiovascular system electrophysiology
def: "An anomaly of the electrical conduction physiology of the heart." []
is_a: HP:0011025 ! Abnormal cardiovascular system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0030962
name: Abnormal morphology of the great vessels
def: "A structural anomaly affecting a blood vessel involved in the circulation of the heart, i.e., the superior or inferior vena cava, the pulmonary arteries, the pulmonary veins, and the aorta." []
is_a: HP:0033353 ! Abnormal blood vessel morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0031501
name: Pelvic mass
def: "An abnormal enlargement or swelling in the pelvic region." []
is_a: HP:0001438 ! Abnormal abdomen morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0031567
name: Abnormal aortic valve cusp morphology
def: "Any structural anomaly of the aortic valve leaflets." []
xref: Fyler:1480
is_a: HP:0001646 ! Abnormal aortic valve morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0032101
name: Unusual infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to infection, as manifested by recurrent infection, severe or invasive infection, infection occurring in an unusual anatomical location, or infection with opportunistic organisms, that is unusual for a healthy individual of the same age." []
is_a: HP:0010978 ! Abnormality of immune system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0032169
name: Severe infection
def: "A type of infection that is regarded as a sign of a pathological susceptibility to infection because of unusual severity or intensity of the infection." []
is_a: HP:0032101 ! Unusual infection

[Term]
id: HP:0032180
name: Abnormal circulating metabolite concentration
def: "An abnormal level of an analyte measured in the blood." []
is_a: HP:0001939 ! Abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis

[Term]
id: HP:0032325
name: Lacunar stroke
def: "A stroke related to a small infarct (2-20 mm in diameter) in the deep cerebral white matter, basal ganglia, or pons, that is presumed to result from the occlusion of a single small perforating artery supplying the subcortical areas of the brain." []
is_a: HP:0002140 ! Ischemic stroke

[Term]
id: HP:0033127
name: Abnormality of the musculoskeletal system
def: "An anomaly of the musculoskeletal system, which consists of the bones of the skeleton, muscles, cartilage, tendons, ligaments, joints, and other connective tissue. The musculoskeletal system supports the weight of the body, maintains body position and produces movements of the body or of parts of the body." []
is_a: HP:0000118 ! Phenotypic abnormality

[Term]
id: HP:0033353
name: Abnormal blood vessel morphology
def: "Any structural anomaly of a blood vessel (artery, arteriole, capillary, venule, or vein)." []
is_a: HP:0025015 ! Abnormal vascular morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0033354
name: Abnormal urine metabolite level
def: "Any deviation from the normal amount of a metabolite in urine." []
is_a: HP:0003110 ! Abnormality of urine homeostasis

[Term]
id: HP:0033401
name: Tissue ischemia
def: "Ischemia is defined as a restriction of arterial blood supply to a tissue associated with insufficient oxygenation to support the metabolis requirements of the tissue. Depending on the involved tissues, clinical manifestations may include pain, pallor, lack of pulse, coldness, paresthesia, and paralysis. Additional associated manifestations include hemodynamic parameters (reduced blood pressure distal to the site of restricted arterial supply) and angiographic evidence of arterial occclusion." []
is_a: HP:0025323 ! Abnormal arterial physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0034267
name: Pelvic pain
def: "Pain perceived in the area of the pelvis, the lower part of the abdomen located between the hip bones." []
is_a: HP:0012531 ! Pain

[Term]
id: HP:0040195
name: Decreased head circumference
def: "An abnormally reduced head circumference in a growing child. Head circumference is measured with a nonelastic tape and comprises the distance from above the eyebrows and ears and around the back of the head. The measured HC is then plotted on an appropriate growth chart. Microcephaly is defined as a head circumference (HC) that is great than two standard deviations below the mean of age- and gender-matched population based samples. Severe microcephaly is defined with an HC that is three standard deviations below the mean." []
is_a: HP:0000240 ! Abnormality of skull size

[Term]
id: HP:0100326
name: Immunologic hypersensitivity
def: "Immunological states where the immune system produces harmful responses upon reexposure to sensitizing antigens." []
is_a: HP:0010978 ! Abnormality of immune system physiology

[Term]
id: HP:0100543
name: Cognitive impairment
def: "Abnormal cognition is characterized by deficits in thinking, reasoning, or remembering." []
is_a: HP:0011446 ! Abnormality of mental function

[Term]
id: HP:0100545
name: Arterial stenosis
def: "Narrowing or constriction of the inner surface (lumen) of an artery." []
is_a: HP:0011004 ! Abnormal systemic arterial morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0100547
name: Abnormal forebrain morphology
def: "An abnormality of the forebrain, which has as its parts the telencephalon, diencephalon, lateral ventricles and third ventricle." []
is_a: HP:0012443 ! Abnormal brain morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0100659
name: Abnormal cerebral vascular morphology
def: "An anomaly of the cerebral blood vessels." []
is_a: HP:0012443 ! Abnormal brain morphology
is_a: HP:0025015 ! Abnormal vascular morphology

[Term]
id: HP:0100716
name: Self-injurious behavior
def: "Self-aggression." []
is_a: HP:5200241 ! Recurrent maladaptive behavior

[Term]
id: HP:0100851
name: Abnormal emotional state
def: "A disturbance in the experience or expression of emotion, characterized by alterations in valence, intensity, frequency, or duration. It may also involve emotional responses that are mismatched, exaggerated, or incongruent relative to internal expectations or external contextual stimuli, such as experiencing negative affect in response to neutral or positive events." []
is_a: HP:0025766 ! Abnormal affect

[Term]
id: HP:0200134
name: Epileptic encephalopathy
def: "A condition in which epileptiform abnormalities are believed to contribute to the progressive disturbance in cerebral function. Epileptic encephalaopathy is characterized by (1) electrographic EEG paroxysmal activity that is often aggressive, (2) seizures that are usually multiform and intractable, (3) cognitive, behavioral and neurological deficits that may be relentless, and (4) sometimes early death." []
is_a: HP:0001298 ! Encephalopathy

[Term]
id: HP:0410324
name: Dust mite allergy
def: "Hypersensitivity in form of an adverse immune reaction against dust mites." []
is_a: HP:0012393 ! Allergy

[Term]
id: HP:0430071
name: Abnormal circulating organic compound concentration
def: "Any deviation of the concentration of an orrganic compound from the normal range. An organic compound is defined as any compound that contains a carbon atom." []
is_a: HP:0032180 ! Abnormal circulating metabolite concentration

[Term]
id: HP:5200241
name: Recurrent maladaptive behavior
def: "A repeating behavior that is either immediately unproductive or has negative long-term consequences. This includes harmful coping mechanisms such as addictive behavior and failure to control impulses and compulsions." []
is_a: HP:0000708 ! Atypical behavior

[Term]
id: HP:5200283
name: Sleep-related breathing disorders
def: "Conditions of abnormal and difficult respiration during sleep, including chronic snoring and sleep apnea." []
is_a: HP:0002360 ! Sleep disturbance

[Term]
id: HP:5200330
name: Suicide behaviors
def: "Suicide attempts or preparations" []
is_a: HP:0100716 ! Self-injurious behavior

[Term]
id: HP:5200423
name: Abnormal experience of reality
def: "Subjective phenomena or perceptions that deviate from what is considered correct or are outside the range of normal human experiences." []
is_a: HP:0011446 ! Abnormality of mental function

[Term]
id: HP:5200430
name: Abnormal psychotic pattern
def: "Any abnormal pattern of psychotic experiences, where an individual has significant disturbances in their thoughts, perceptions, emotions, and behavior, resulting in a loss of touch with reality." []
is_a: HP:5200423 ! Abnormal experience of reality

[Term]
id: HP:5210000
name: Unusual bacterial infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to bacterial infections as manifested by recurrent or severe/invasive bacterial infection, or by bacterial infection in an unusual anatomical location." []
is_a: HP:0032101 ! Unusual infection

[Term]
id: HP:5210001
name: Unusual gram-positive bacterial infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to gram-positive bacterial infections as manifested by recurrent or severe/invasive infection with gram-positive organisms." []
is_a: HP:5210000 ! Unusual bacterial infection

[Term]
id: HP:5210009
name: Unusual Streptococcus infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to Streptococcus infections as manifested by recurrent or severe/invasive infection with Streptococcus, or by Streptococcus infection occurring in an unusual anatomical location." []
is_a: HP:5210001 ! Unusual gram-positive bacterial infection

[Term]
id: HP:5210013
name: Unusual Streptococcus pyogenes infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to Streptococcus pyogenes infections as manifested by recurrent or severe/invasive infection with Streptococcus pyogenes, or by Streptococcus pyogenes infection occurring in an unusual anatomical location." []
is_a: HP:5210009 ! Unusual Streptococcus infection

[Term]
id: HP:5210014
name: Severe Streptococcus pyogenes infection
def: "Increased susceptibility to Streptococcus pyogenes infections as manifested by a severe or invasive infection with Streptococcus pyogenes." []
is_a: HP:5210013 ! Unusual Streptococcus pyogenes infection

