[Instance]
id: IAO:0000224
name: obsolete_core
def: "Core is an instance of a grouping of terms from an ontology or ontologies. It is used by the ontology to identify main classes." []
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000231 IAO:0000226
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000226
name: placeholder removed
def: "The term was created to temporarily stand in for a semantic purpose, but is no longer needed, typically due to another permanent term being defined." []
instance_of: IAO:0000225 ! obsolescence reason specification
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6875-5360
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
property_value: IAO:0000111 "placeholder removed" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "This reason is appropriate for a temporary term even if no permanent term is defined; for example if the need for the term no longer exists. If a permanent (replacement) term is defined, the deprecated term should reference the replacement with IAO:0100001. If no replacement is defined, it may be appropriate to reference alternative terms with oboInOwl:consider." xsd:string

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000227
name: terms merged
def: "The term has been combined with one or more other terms to create a more encompassing (merged) term." []
instance_of: IAO:0000225 ! obsolescence reason specification
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6875-5360
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
property_value: IAO:0000111 "terms merged" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "The deprecated term should reference the merged term with obo:IAO_0100001. The replacement term should reference the original terms as sources using obo:RO_0001000 (derives_from). An editor note should explain what were the merged terms and the reason for the merge." xsd:string

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000228
name: term imported
def: "The term has been replaced by a term imported from another ontology." []
instance_of: IAO:0000225 ! obsolescence reason specification
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6875-5360
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
property_value: IAO:0000111 "term imported" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "This is to be used when the original term has been replaced by a term imported from an other ontology. The deprecated term should reference the imported term with obo:IAO_0100001." xsd:string

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000229
name: term split
def: "The term has been split into two or more new terms." []
instance_of: IAO:0000225 ! obsolescence reason specification
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6875-5360
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
property_value: IAO:0000111 "term split" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "This is to be used when a term has been split in two or more new terms. An editor note should indicate the reason for the split. The deprecated term should reference the replacement terms with obo:IAO_0100001." xsd:string

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000410
name: universal
instance_of: IAO:0000409 ! denotator type
property_value: IAO:0000111 "universal" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "Hard to give a definition for. Intuitively a \"natural kind\" rather than a collection of any old things, which a class is able to be, formally. At the meta level, universals are defined as positives, are disjoint with their siblings, have single asserted parents." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "A Formal Theory of Substances, Qualities, and Universals, http://ontology.buffalo.edu/bfo/SQU.pdf" xsd:string

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000420
name: defined class
def: "A defined class is a class that is defined by a set of logically necessary and sufficient conditions but is not a universal" []
instance_of: IAO:0000409 ! denotator type
property_value: IAO:0000111 "defined class" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "\"definitions\", in some readings, always are given by necessary and sufficient conditions. So one must be careful (and this is difficult sometimes) to distinguish between defined classes and universal." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000421
name: named class expression
def: "A named class expression is a logical expression that is given a name. The name can be used in place of the expression." []
instance_of: IAO:0000409 ! denotator type
property_value: IAO:0000111 "named class expression" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "named class expressions are used in order to have more concise logical definition but their extensions may not be interesting classes on their own. In languages such as OWL, with no provisions for macros, these show up as actuall classes. Tools may with to not show them as such, and to replace uses of the macros with their expansions" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000423
name: to be replaced with external ontology term
def: "Terms with this status should eventually replaced with a term from another ontology." []
instance_of: IAO:0000078 ! curation status specification
property_value: IAO:0000111 "to be replaced with external ontology term" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "group:OBI" xsd:string

[Instance]
id: IAO:0000428
name: requires discussion
def: "A term that is metadata complete, has been reviewed, and problems have been identified that require discussion before release. Such a term requires editor note(s) to identify the outstanding issues." []
instance_of: IAO:0000078 ! curation status specification
property_value: IAO:0000111 "requires discussion" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000114 IAO:0000125
property_value: IAO:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "group:OBI" xsd:string

[Instance]
id: OMO:0001000
name: out of scope
def: "The term was added to the ontology on the assumption it was in scope, but it turned out later that it was not." []
instance_of: IAO:0000225 ! obsolescence reason specification
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6875-5360
property_value: dce:contributor https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7356-1779
property_value: IAO:0000116 "This obsolesence reason should be used conservatively. Typical valid examples in disease ontologies are: unnecessary class grouping; mistaked creation of a disease associated to a phenotype." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 http://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/ontology-metadata/issues/77" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000234 "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432" xsd:string

[Instance]
id: OMO:0001002
name: domain entity does not exist
def: "The term was added to the ontology on the assumption it was a valid domain entity, but it turns out the entity does not exist in reality." []
instance_of: IAO:0000225 ! obsolescence reason specification
property_value: IAO:0000116 "This obsolesence reason should be used conservatively. For example: Obsoleting class that describes a breed of cow based on a record in an existing database, that was later retracted as faulty (breed does not exist). Do not use this term to obsolete a historic concept (that was once valid, but not anymore). " xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 http://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153
property_value: IAO:0000233 "https://github.com/information-artifact-ontology/ontology-metadata/issues/136" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000234 "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153" xsd:string

