[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000377
name: BioBank Japan
def: "A patient-based biobank established in 2003 at the Institute of Medical Science, the University of Tokyo, by the BioBank Japan Project, with a first cohort of about 200,000 patients diagnosed with any of 47 common diseases, enrolled at 12 cooperative medical institutes across Japan from June 2003 to March 2008, whose DNA was collected at baseline and serum and clinical information annually until 2013, and a second cohort of about 67,000 new patients with 38 diseases enrolled in fiscal years 2013–2017, together about 267,000 patients with 51 diseases, built as infrastructure for genomic research and the implementation of personalized medicine." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28189464", IAO:0000119="https://biobankjp.org/en/about/1990"}
