[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000385
name: Framingham Heart Study
def: "A community-based, multi-generational cohort begun in 1948 with the Original Cohort of 5,209 men and women aged 30–62, a random sample of the adult population of Framingham, Massachusetts, and extended by the Offspring Cohort of 5,124 of their children and the children's spouses (1971), the Third Generation Cohort of 4,095 grandchildren (2002–2005), the New Offspring Spouse Cohort (2003–2005) and the ethnically diverse Omni cohorts, begun in 1994 among residents of Framingham and surrounding towns and extended in 2003–2005, all examined approximately every 2–4 years to define cardiovascular disease risk factors and, increasingly, the genetic and molecular epidemiology of cardiovascular and other diseases." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.framinghamheartstudy.org/fhs-about/", IAO:0000119="PMID:26705418", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
