[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000388
name: Hispanic Community Health Study/Study of Latinos
def: "A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20609343", IAO:0000119="PMID:39644095"}
