[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000396
name: Simons Foundation Powering Autism Research for Knowledge
def: "A US cohort, launched by the Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative (SFARI), of individuals living in the United States with a professional diagnosis of autism spectrum disorder together with their parents and an unaffected sibling, recruited nationwide through 21 clinical sites and social media and taking part remotely online, with questionnaires and saliva samples for genetic analysis (exome sequencing and genome-wide genotyping, later also whole-genome sequencing). It collects genomic, environmental and longitudinal behavioural and medical data, returns genetic results to participants, and recontacts them and connects them with researchers for new studies; it enrolled 18,089 individuals with autism and 28,515 of their family members in its first 12 months of recruitment, to May 2017." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29420931", IAO:0000119="PMID:41606319"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "Simons Foundation Powering Autism Research" RELATED []
synonym: "SPARK" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
