[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000414
name: Wisconsin Alzheimer's Disease Research Center
def: "A longitudinal cohort, the Clinical Core study of the Wisconsin Alzheimer's Disease Research Center, a National Institute on Aging-funded centre established in 2009 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, in which adults aged 45 and over, recruited into subgroups with mild late-onset Alzheimer disease, mild cognitive impairment, healthy older controls, and middle-aged adults with a positive, negative or indeterminate parental history of Alzheimer disease, attend annual or every-other-year visits with a study partner for memory and thinking evaluations, blood draws and biomarker visits with MRI, lumbar puncture and PET, to study memory, ageing and Alzheimer disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://adrc.wisc.edu/history-and-mission", IAO:0000119="https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core", IAO:0000119="PMID:33437055", IAO:0000119="https://adrc.wisc.edu/structure-and-cores"}
