[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000417
name: BioVU
def: "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:18500243", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/"}
