[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000433
name: Generation Scotland: Scottish Family Health Study
def: "A family-based population cohort of 24,084 adults, including 5,501 families, recruited in Scotland between 2006 and 2011 by Generation Scotland, a collaboration of the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and NHS Scotland. It comprises 6,665 probands aged 35–65, selected from lists of collaborating general practices in the Glasgow and Tayside areas (extended to Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010), and 17,419 of their adult relatives. Participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or took part by post, gave DNA for genome-wide genotyping and consented to record linkage and recontact, for the study of the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of common diseases such as heart disease, stroke and depression." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38908846", IAO:0000119="PMID:29040551"}
