[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000444
name: Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium
def: "A consortium of large prospective population-based cohort studies from the United States and Europe, founded with the Age, Gene/Environment Susceptibility-Reykjavik Study, the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Heart Study and the Rotterdam Study, formed to facilitate genome-wide association meta-analyses and replication across cohorts with similarly measured phenotypes." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20031568"}
