[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000451
name: Red Blood Cell-Omics Study
def: "A cohort of 13,403 racially and ethnically diverse volunteer blood donors aged 18 or older, enrolled from December 2013 to October 2015 at four large blood centres across the United States (in Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and California) by the NHLBI Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III (REDS-III), who completed a questionnaire and gave blood for blood counts, ferritin and DNA and a sample of their red cells for haemolysis testing at the end of storage, with donors of extreme haemolysis recalled for a second donation, to study the genetic and biological determinants of donor iron metabolism, pica, restless legs syndrome and red cell storage haemolysis, and to link donors to the outcomes of the patients transfused with their red cells." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:30267427", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:36395887"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
