[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000459
name: Ludwigshafen Risk and Cardiovascular Health Study
def: "A prospective cohort of 3,808 patients from the Ludwigshafen, Mannheim and Heidelberg area of south-west Germany, enrolled between July 1997 and March 2002 when they underwent coronary angiography at the municipal hospital of Ludwigshafen, with and without coronary artery disease, examined at baseline (medical history, physical examination, glucose tolerance test and blood sampling) and followed up from 2004, to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular diseases. Most analyses use its 3,316 participants of German ancestry recruited between July 1997 and January 2000." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:32915819", IAO:0000119="https://www.luric.online", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:39003598"}
