id: coho:COHO_0000472
name: Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III
def: "A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24188564"}
