id: coho:COHO_0000480
name: National Alzheimer's Coordinating Center
def: "A US data resource, founded in 1999 and funded by the National Institute on Aging, that combines the standardized longitudinal clinical (Uniform Data Set), neuropathology, imaging, biomarker and genetic data of participants of the NIA-funded Alzheimer's Disease Research Centers, more than 56,000 people from over 42 centers, for research on Alzheimer disease and related dementias." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41122833", IAO:0000119="https://naccdata.org/"}
