def: "A family study of the NHLBI Family Blood Pressure Program that from 1995 to 2000 recruited African American and white sibships with two or more members with hypertension diagnosed before age 60, with their untreated adult offspring and random population samples, at centres in Birmingham (Alabama), Forsyth County (North Carolina), Framingham (Massachusetts), Minneapolis (Minnesota) and Salt Lake City (Utah), to identify genes promoting hypertension." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="PMID:10964005", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7933688/fullTextXML"}
