[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000488
name: Bandim Health Project
def: "A health and demographic surveillance and research platform in Guinea-Bissau, run by the Bandim Health Project with Statens Serum Institut, that has followed women and children in an urban surveillance system in the capital, Bissau, since 1978 and in a nationally representative rural surveillance system of 182 clusters since 1989-1990, to study health interventions, child mortality and the non-specific effects of vaccines. Randomised trials are run within it, such as the 2008-2013 trial of early BCG vaccination in low-birth-weight newborns in Bissau." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29579158", IAO:0000119="PMID:31189684", IAO:0000119="PMID:25210141", IAO:0000119="PMID:32114478"}
