[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000498
name: Munich Antidepressant Response Signature
def: "A naturalistic, open-label longitudinal treatment study of inpatients admitted with a moderate to severe unipolar or bipolar depressive episode to the hospital of the Max Planck Institute of Psychiatry in Munich and collaborating hospitals in Southern Bavaria and Switzerland, characterised clinically, neuroendocrinologically (dex/CRH test) and genetically and followed weekly during treatment, to identify predictors of antidepressant treatment response." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:18586274", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30678080"}
