[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000523
name: Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study
def: "A prospective cohort of 41,513 middle-aged and older adults of white European origin, almost all aged 40–69, recruited in Melbourne, Australia, in 1990–1994 by Cancer Council Victoria and followed up face to face in 2003–2007 and by record linkage to cancer and death registries, collecting socio-demographic, lifestyle and health data to study risk factors for cancer and other chronic diseases." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML"}
