id: coho:COHO_0000526
name: Finnish Cardiovascular Study
def: "A clinical cohort of about 4,500 patients scheduled for an exercise stress test at Tampere University Hospital, Finland, recruited between October 2001 and December 2007 with continuous high-resolution ECG, haemodynamic measurements, genotyping and follow-up of clinical events and deaths, to construct risk profiles for cardiovascular disease, events and death." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16515696", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles"}
