id: coho:COHO_0000538
name: Raine Study
def: "A pregnancy cohort in Western Australia for which 2,900 pregnant women were recruited between 1989 and 1991 at King Edward Memorial Hospital, Perth, and nearby private clinics, with the mothers (Generation 1) and their 2,868 offspring (Generation 2) followed from 18 weeks' gestation through childhood and adolescence into adulthood, to study how early life shapes later health and behaviour." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28064197", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12873190/fullTextXML"}
