[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000540
name: Genetic Epidemiology Network of Salt Sensitivity
def: "A family feeding study in rural northern China that recruited 3,153 Han Chinese participants from 658 families, each ascertained through a proband with untreated prehypertension or stage-1 hypertension, of whom 1,906 eligible probands and their siblings, spouses and offspring underwent seven-day low-sodium, high-sodium and high-sodium with potassium supplementation dietary interventions, to localise and identify genes influencing blood pressure responses to dietary sodium and potassium." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:28993450", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4873465/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="PMID:17443206"}
