[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000553
name: Shanghai Women's Health Study
def: "A population-based prospective cohort of 74,942 Chinese women aged 40–70 recruited in 1996–2000 from selected urban communities of Shanghai, most of whom gave blood, urine or buccal-cell samples, followed by biennial in-person recontact and linkage to cancer and vital statistics registries, to study environmental exposures, biomarkers and the risk of cancer and other chronic diseases." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:22073174", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16236996"}
