[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000556
name: Darmkrebs: Chancen der Verhütung durch Screening
def: "A multicentre population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the Rhine-Neckar region of south-west Germany, led from the German Cancer Research Center in Heidelberg, which from 2003 recruited patients aged 30 or over with a first colorectal cancer diagnosis from the 22 hospitals treating the disease in the region, and actively follows the cases to study colorectal cancer risk, prevention by screening and survival." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
