id: coho:COHO_0000559
name: Hong Kong Degenerative Disc Disease Population Cohort
def: "A population-based cohort of about 2,900 volunteers of Southern Chinese origin aged 15–55 in Hong Kong, openly recruited through newspaper advertisements, posters and e-mails regardless of back symptoms, who underwent lumbar spine MRI, questionnaires and genome-wide genotyping, to study the genetic and environmental determinants of intervertebral disc degeneration." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:34450027", IAO:0000119="PMID:27157501"}
