[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000561
name: Alzheimer's Disease Sequencing Project
def: "A US National Institutes of Health initiative, started in 2012, that sequences the exomes and whole genomes of well-characterized participants of many Alzheimer disease cohorts, first from the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium and CHARGE consortium and later from ancestrally diverse cohorts, and integrates them with harmonized phenotypes to identify genetic risk and protective variants for Alzheimer disease and related dementias. Its fourth release comprised 36,361 whole genomes from 17 cohorts in 14 countries, 45% of its unique participants of non-European ancestry, and its fifth 58,507 genomes from 57 cohorts." [] {IAO:0000119="https://dss.niagads.org/studies/sa000001/", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:40407102", IAO:0000119="https://adsp.niagads.org/"}
