[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000562
name: Cebu Longitudinal Health and Nutrition Survey
def: "A community-based birth cohort of about 3,000 singletons born in 1983-1984 in Cebu, Philippines, and their mothers, enrolled in pregnancy and followed with bimonthly surveys for two years and repeated follow-up surveys to age 35, run by the Office of Population Studies of the University of San Carlos and the University of North Carolina to study the long-term effects of early nutrition and life conditions on health." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33865193", IAO:0000119="PMID:18426866"}
