[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000571
name: Japan Multi-Institutional Collaborative Cohort Study
def: "A Japanese multi-institutional genome cohort, launched in 2005, of 92,610 adults aged 35–69 years from 14 study regions in 12 prefectures (respondents to study announcements, people attending local-government health checkups or health checkup centres, and first-visit patients at a cancer hospital), who gave baseline questionnaire data and blood samples in 2005–2014 and are followed until 2025, to examine gene–environment interactions in lifestyle-related diseases, mainly cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17696755", IAO:0000119="PMID:32963210"}
