[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000572
name: Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study
def: "A case-control study of urinary bladder cancer run from Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, in which patients diagnosed from 1995 to 2010 under the age of 76 and living in the catchment area of seven hospitals in the east of the country were identified through the Netherlands Cancer Registry and invited in batches, with controls drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, to study genetic and lifestyle risk factors and outcomes of bladder cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4453642/fullTextXML"}
