id: coho:COHO_0000578
name: Shanghai Men's Health Study
def: "A population-based prospective cohort of 61,480 men aged 40–74 living in urban Shanghai, recruited from 2002 with detailed lifestyle, dietary and medical data and blood, urine and DNA samples, and followed by in-person surveys every 3–4 years and linkage with cancer and vital statistics registries, to study lifestyle, environmental and genetic contributions to cancer and other non-communicable diseases." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25733578", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
