[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000582
name: NHLBI Family Heart Study
def: "A family study of the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute that recruited families, about half at high risk of coronary heart disease and half selected randomly, from existing study populations at four centres in Forsyth County (North Carolina), Framingham (Massachusetts), Minneapolis (Minnesota) and Salt Lake City (Utah), examining 5,710 participants in 1993–1995, to identify genetic and non-genetic determinants of coronary heart disease, atherosclerosis and their risk factors. Its follow-up, the Family Heart SCAN study, re-examined about a third of the participants with cardiac CT in 2002–2003 and added 622 African Americans from 211 families of hypertensive sibships previously examined by the Hypertension Genetic Epidemiology Network (HyperGEN)." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:8651220", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8224703/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4417236/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2409301/fullTextXML"}
