[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000583
name: Hyperglycemia and Adverse Pregnancy Outcome Study
def: "A multinational, multi-ancestry observational cohort of more than 25,000 pregnant women enrolled in 2000-2006 at 15 field centres in Asia, Australia, the Caribbean, Europe, North America and the Middle East, who had a standardised 75 g oral glucose tolerance test at 24-32 weeks of gestation, to study the association of maternal glycaemia with adverse pregnancy and newborn outcomes; mothers were later genotyped and their children followed up." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:39849370", IAO:0000119="PMID:37110162"}
