id: coho:COHO_0000586
name: Italian Network of Genetic Isolates - Carlantino
def: "A population-based cohort of about 1,000 people from Carlantino, a small isolated village in Apulia (Foggia province), southern Italy, who underwent clinical and instrumental evaluations between 1998 and 2005; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8394865/fullTextXML", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4997959/fullTextXML"}
