[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000597
name: North Carolina Colon Cancer Study
def: "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in African Americans and whites in 33 counties of central and eastern North Carolina, United States, in which cases aged 40–80 were identified by rapid ascertainment through the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry, African Americans were oversampled, and controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Health Care Financing Administration records. Phase I enrolled colon cancer cases from October 1996 to September 2000 and phase II (NCCCS-II) cases of sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer from May 2001 to September 2006, both collecting interview data on diet, medication use and other risk factors." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19336553", IAO:0000119="PMID:19842051", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013500/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode"}
