id: coho:COHO_0000607
name: International Multicentre ADHD Genetics project
def: "A European multi-site family sample of children aged 5 to 17 with DSM-IV combined-type ADHD, their siblings and parents, all of white European Caucasian descent, recruited in 2003-2007 at specialist ADHD clinics in eight countries for molecular genetic studies of ADHD, including candidate-gene, linkage and genome-wide association analyses; a second phase (IMAGE II) combined ADHD cases from the original project and from further clinics in Germany, the Netherlands and the UK with population controls for genome-wide association." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16887023", IAO:0000119="PMID:20732625", IAO:0000119="PMID:21473745"}
