id: coho:COHO_0000608
name: Family Blood Pressure Program
def: "An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of over 11,000 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:11799070", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML"}
