[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000616
name: Exeter Family Study of Childhood Health
def: "A prospective family study of 1,017 families (both parents and their children) from a postcode-defined area of central Exeter, United Kingdom, with anthropometry and fasting biochemistry at 28 weeks of gestation, cord blood at delivery and child follow-up to age 2 years, set up to test the fetal insulin hypothesis and identify genetic variants influencing birthweight and early postnatal growth." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16466435"}
