id: coho:COHO_0000652
name: SubPopulations and InteRmediate Outcome Measures in COPD Study
def: "A multicentre observational cohort of current and former smokers aged 40–80 with or without airflow obstruction, and never-smoking controls, recruited at clinical sites across the United States with baseline and annual follow-up visits, to find subgroups of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and biomarkers usable as intermediate outcomes in therapeutic trials." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24029743"}
