id: coho:COHO_0000657
name: Population Assessment for Tomorrow's Health Study
def: "A research registry of community volunteers aged 18 to 65 living in the Greater Hamilton area, with or without addiction problems, run by the Peter Boris Centre for Addictions Research at St. Joseph's Healthcare Hamilton, whose participants completed questionnaires, simple physical measurements and an in-person assessment and gave saliva for DNA genotyping through 23andMe, to build a cohort for research on the causes, consequences and treatment of addiction." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35080193", IAO:0000119="PMID:37060189", IAO:0000119="https://pbcar.healthsci.mcmaster.ca/research/projects/population-assessment-for-tomorrows-health-study-path/"}
