[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000672
name: Australian Genetics of Depression Study
def: "A cohort of 20,689 adults in Australia who had been diagnosed with depression, recruited through the Australian Department of Human Services and a media campaign, who completed online questionnaires on psychiatric history and antidepressant response and provided saliva DNA, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for depression and antidepressant response." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:32461290"}
