id: coho:COHO_0000684
name: Hisayama-FSR study
def: "A case-control study of ischaemic stroke in Japan combining 1,113 patients with ischaemic stroke recruited in 2004 from seven hospitals in Fukuoka Prefecture (the Fukuoka Stroke Registry) with 901 controls free of stroke and coronary heart disease drawn from the population-based Hisayama Study, used in genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes." [] {IAO:0000119="https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29531354"}
