id: coho:COHO_0000696
name: Wisconsin Longitudinal Study
def: "A longitudinal study of men and women who graduated from Wisconsin high schools in 1957, most born in 1939, and one of their randomly selected siblings, followed for almost 60 years to link family background, adolescent characteristics, education, work and family life to later-life physical and mental health, cognition and mortality, with saliva samples for genetic studies." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24585852"}
