[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000708
name: German Infant Study on the Influence of Nutrition Intervention plus Air pollution and Genetics on Allergy Development
def: "A prospective population-based German birth cohort of 5,991 healthy term newborns recruited in obstetric hospitals in Munich and Wesel in 1995–1998, comprising a double-blind randomised trial of hydrolysed infant formula in children with a family history of allergy (the German Infant Nutritional Intervention study, GINI) and a non-interventional arm, about 55% of whom were followed for the first 10 years to study the natural course of atopic diseases and their determinants." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30402607"}
