property_value: IAO:0000112 "GCST90435154" xsd:string {dcterms:title="Comprehensive Association Analyses of Extraintestinal Manifestations in Inflammatory Bowel Disease.", xref="PMID:38490347", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38490347+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core", comment="We assembled the largest multicohort data set to date to investigate the clinical, serologic, and genetic factors associated with EIM complications in IBD.MethodsData were available in 12,083 unrelated European ancestry IBD cases with presence or absence of EIMs (eg, ankylosing spondylitis [ankylosing spondylitis and sacroiliitis], primary sclerosing cholangitis [PSC], peripheral arthritis, and skin and ocular manifestations) across 4 cohorts (Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, National Institute for Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases IBD Genetics Consortium, Sinai Helmsley Alliance for Research Excellence Consortium, and Risk Stratification and Identification of Immunogenetic and Microbial Markers of Rapid Disease Progression in Children with Crohn's Disease cohort)."}
