id: coho:COHO_0000747
name: Diabetes Control and Complications Trial/Epidemiology of Diabetes Interventions and Complications Study
def: "A cohort of 1,441 people aged 13–39 years with type 1 diabetes from 29 centres in the United States and Canada, enrolled in the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial (1983–1993), a randomised trial comparing intensive with conventional therapy to test whether glycaemic control prevents or delays the complications of type 1 diabetes, and followed since 1994 in the observational Epidemiology of Diabetes Interventions and Complications (EDIC) study of the durability of the treatment effects on advanced microvascular complications and cardiovascular disease." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9727532/fullTextXML", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24356592"}
