[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000748
name: Danish National Birth Cohort
def: "A nationwide Danish cohort of about 100,000 pregnant women recruited early in pregnancy between 1996 and 2002, run by Statens Serum Institut, with telephone interviews during pregnancy and after birth, biological samples from mother and umbilical cord, and long-term follow-up of the children through questionnaires and national registry linkage, established to study the causal links between early-life exposures and later disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.dnbc.dk/about-the-dnbc"}
