id: coho:COHO_0000756
name: Heinz Nixdorf Recall Study
def: "A population-based cohort of 4,814 adults aged 45–75 randomly selected from the resident registries of Bochum, Essen and Mülheim an der Ruhr in the Ruhr area of Germany, examined in 2000–2003 and followed up repeatedly, set up to evaluate coronary artery calcification measured by electron-beam CT for predicting myocardial infarction and cardiac death beyond traditional risk factors." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12458722/fullTextXML", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
