[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000757
name: INflammation, Health, Ancestry and Lung Epidemiology study
def: "A case-control study of lung cancer in African American and non-Hispanic White adults from the Detroit metropolitan area, in which patients were enrolled within 12 months of diagnosis at the Karmanos Cancer Institute or Henry Ford Health System between 2012 and 2018, together with controls without lung cancer, to study inflammation, ancestry and other risk factors for lung cancer and racial disparities in the disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9307937/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="PMID:35024781", IAO:0000119="PMID:39854657"}
