[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000766
name: University of Southern California Hormone Replacement Therapy Colorectal Cancer Study
def: "A population-based case-control study of colon cancer in women in Los Angeles County, United States, comprising 831 English-speaking women aged 55–74 years diagnosed with primary colon cancer from 1998 to 2002, identified through the Los Angeles County Cancer Surveillance Program (a SEER registry), and 755 race/ethnicity- and age-matched neighbourhood control women, with in-person interviews on hormone use, reproductive history and lifestyle and blood samples, set up to study menopausal hormone therapy and colon cancer risk." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35512400", IAO:0000119="PMID:38561434"}
