id: coho:COHO_0000772
name: Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism
def: "A multi-site, multi-generational family study in which probands recruited through alcohol treatment centres and their relatives, together with community comparison families, have been assessed over more than 30 years (nearly 18,000 individuals from over 2200 families) with psychiatric interviews, questionnaires, electrophysiology and DNA to identify genetic factors in alcohol use disorder and related outcomes." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37581339"}
