[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000796
name: Singapore Malay Eye Study
def: "A population-based study of Malay adults aged 40–79 years living in south-western Singapore, selected by age-stratified random sampling and examined with standardised interviews, ocular and systemic assessments and stored blood and urine samples, to measure the prevalence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17365815"}
