id: coho:COHO_0000834
name: Microisolates in South Tyrol Study
def: "A population-based family study of about 1,300 adults from Stelvio, Vallelunga and Martello, three small, historically isolated villages of the Val Venosta (Vinschgau) in South Tyrol, Italy, surveyed by the European Academy of Bozen/Bolzano (EURAC) in 2002–2003 and 2007, with reconstructed genealogies, to study the genetic epidemiology of Mendelian and complex diseases." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17550581", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12119133/fullTextXML"}
