[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000849
name: South London Ethnicity and Stroke Study
def: "A stroke study in which 1,200 black and 1,200 white stroke patients were prospectively recruited between 1999 and 2010 from three hospitals covering a contiguous area of South London, United Kingdom, with black African and African Caribbean community controls from general practice lists in the same catchment area (1999–2012), to study stroke subtypes and the genetic and other risk factors for stroke in African and African Caribbean people." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:28349126", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:27197724"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
