def: "An international consortium of gout genetics research groups, named as a collective author of a genome-wide association analysis of gout in 2.6 million people, whose own case-control sample set (New Zealand/Ardea Biosciences/EuroGout: 4,713 people with self-reported clinically diagnosed gout or gout meeting the 1977 ARA classification criteria and 2,151 controls, of self-reported European ancestry) was genotyped for that study on the Illumina CoreExome array." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2022/11/29/2022.11.26.22281768/DC1/embed/media-1.xlsx", IAO:0000119="PMID:39406924"}
