id: coho:COHO_0000922
name: KOALA Birth Cohort Study
def: "A prospective Dutch birth cohort of healthy pregnant women enrolled from October 2000 to 2002, recruited from a cohort study on pregnancy-related pelvic girdle pain ('conventional lifestyles') and, for contrast, through organic food shops, anthroposophic doctors and midwives, Steiner schools and dedicated magazines ('alternative lifestyles'), and their children, set up to identify lifestyle and other early-life factors that influence atopic disease and followed into young adulthood." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:42116128", IAO:0000119="PMID:16343090"}
