id: coho:COHO_0000927
name: Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study
def: "A population-based prospective cohort of more than 140,000 participants in Norrbotten and Västerbotten, the two northernmost regions of Sweden, initiated in the mid-1980s and managed by Umeå University, combining three sub-cohorts (the Västerbotten Intervention Programme, the expanded Northern Sweden MONICA study and the Mammography Screening Project) with over 240,000 stored blood samples, for research on the aetiology, prevention and early detection of cancer, cardiovascular and other diseases." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11790227/fullTextXML"}
