[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000929
name: Prolonged Anticoagulation During eighteen months vs placebo after Initial Six-month treatment for a first episode of idiopathic Pulmonary Embolism
def: "A randomised, double-blind trial in which 371 adults with a first unprovoked pulmonary embolism, after six months of vitamin K antagonist treatment, were randomised to a further 18 months of warfarin or placebo and followed between 2007 and 2014 at 14 French centres, comparing recurrent venous thromboembolism and major bleeding." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26151264"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "PADIS-PE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "PADIS-PE randomized clinical trial" RELATED []
synonym: "PADIS-PE trial" RELATED []
synonym: "Prolonged Anticoagulant During Eighteen Months vs Placebo After Initial Six-month Treatment for a First Episode of Idiopathic Pulmonary Embolism" RELATED []
