id: coho:COHO_0000945
name: ProHealth Kaiser GWAS
def: "A multiethnic genome-wide association study sample of prostate cancer from Kaiser Permanente health plan members in California, combining prostate cancer cases from three Kaiser Permanente studies (the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health, the ProHealth Study and the California Men's Health Study) with men of the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging cohort without a prostate cancer diagnosis as controls (7,783 cases and 38,595 controls; 80.3% non-Hispanic white, 4.9% African American, 7.0% East Asian and 7.8% Latino)." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26034056"}
