[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000958
name: Army Study to Assess Risk and Resilience in Servicemembers
def: "A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS)." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:30104726", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
