[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000960
name: CECILE Breast Cancer Study
def: "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in two French départements, Côte d'Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, in which women under 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007 and population controls frequency-matched to them by age, recruited over the same period, were interviewed in person by trained nurses, most also giving a blood sample; it has been used to study occupational, environmental and genetic risk factors for breast cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30669331"}
