[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000962
name: GENetic and clinical Predictors Of treatment response in Depression
def: "A multicentre randomised controlled trial in primary care in Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle, United Kingdom, in which adults aged 18–74 with a new episode of depression (an ICD-10 depressive episode and a Beck Depression Inventory score of at least 15), recruited from September 2005, were randomly allocated to citalopram or reboxetine to identify genetic and clinical predictors of response to antidepressant treatment." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18498636"}
