[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000964
name: Indianapolis-Ibadan Dementia Project
def: "A longitudinal, prospective, population-based study of two elderly community-dwelling populations, African Americans in Indianapolis, Indiana, and Yoruba in Ibadan, Nigeria, aged 65 years or older and free of dementia when enrolled in 1992 and 2001, who were re-evaluated every 2-3 years by in-home screening followed by clinical diagnostic assessment, to compare the incidence of dementia and Alzheimer disease between the two sites using identical methods." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26218444", IAO:0000119="PMID:11176911"}
