id: coho:COHO_0000985
name: Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine Program
def: "A programme of the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (NHLBI) that adds whole-genome sequencing and other omics data to existing, deeply phenotyped studies of ethnically and ancestrally diverse participants, to elucidate the genetic architecture and biology of heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders and improve their diagnosis, treatment and prevention." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33568819"}
