[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000994
name: Ashford study
def: "An unselected birth cohort of children born in 1992–1993 in Ashford, Kent, England, whose mothers were recruited in pregnancy from 1991 as the UK cohort of the Asthma Multicentre Infant Cohort Study, with house-dust allergen measured in infancy and follow-up by questionnaire, lung function and skin prick tests to age 14 years and a questionnaire at about age 20, to study how early-life allergen exposure and other factors relate to the development of atopy, wheeze and asthma." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:15454651", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:10232430", IAO:0000119="PMID:37227431", IAO:0000119="PMID:16950296"}
