[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0000996
name: Bonn Study of COVID Genetics
def: "A study run by the Institute of Human Genetics, University of Bonn, Germany, that continuously recruits adults with SARS-CoV-2 infection confirmed by PCR or antibody testing from the general population through public announcements, collecting questionnaires on demographics, pre-existing conditions and the course of infection (and, from September 2021, on long COVID) and DNA for genotyping, to study host genetic factors in COVID-19." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:40399555"}
