id: coho:COHO_0000998
name: Childhood Asthma Management Program
def: "A multicentre, randomized, double-masked clinical trial of long-term inhaled treatment for mild to moderate asthma (budesonide, nedocromil or placebo, each with albuterol as needed) in children aged 5–12 years, who were enrolled in 1993–1995 at eight clinical centres in the United States and Canada and followed after the trial into adulthood, with a genetic ancillary study of the children and their parents." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:34212545", IAO:0000119="PMID:10027502", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001726"}
