[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001005
name: Fangshan Family-based Ischemic Stroke Study in China
def: "A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:42259975", IAO:0000119="PMID:31823830", IAO:0000119="PMID:36551856", IAO:0000119="PMID:17825112"}
