[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001007
name: Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium
def: "A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29924316", IAO:0000119="PMID:41390056", IAO:0000119="https://www.gelcc.org/node/3", IAO:0000119="PMID:15272417"}
