[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001012
name: Genes, Reading and Dyslexia Study
def: "A multisite case-control study of reading disability (developmental dyslexia) in Hispanic American and African American children aged 8 to 15, led by Yale University at sites in the United States, Puerto Rico and Canada, in which the children were assessed with reading and reading-related measures and gave DNA for genetic studies of reading ability and dyslexia." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38702345", IAO:0000119="PMID:30995994", IAO:0000119="PMID:30631481"}
