[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001014
name: Hypertrophic Cardiomyopathy Registry
def: "An international prospective observational registry and natural history study of hypertrophic cardiomyopathy funded by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, which enrolled patients aged 18 to 65 with hypertrophic cardiomyopathy (unexplained left ventricular hypertrophy) at centres in the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, Italy, Germany and the Netherlands in 2014–2017. Participants underwent clinical evaluation, cardiac magnetic resonance imaging and blood sampling for genetic and biomarker analysis, and are followed for cardiovascular events to improve risk prediction." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26299218", IAO:0000119="PMID:31699273"}
