[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001019
name: Indian Migration Study
def: "A cross-sectional sib-pair study at four factories in Lucknow, Nagpur, Hyderabad and Bangalore in north, central and south India, which in 2005–2007 examined factory workers and their spouses who had migrated from rural areas together with a rural-dwelling sibling of each, and a random sample of urban non-migrant workers and spouses together with an urban-dwelling sibling, to study the effect of rural-to-urban migration on obesity, diabetes and other cardiovascular risk factors." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20436961"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "IMS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
