[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001024
name: NIMH Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Initiative
def: "A family study of Alzheimer's disease in the United States in which three academic medical centres (Massachusetts General Hospital, Johns Hopkins University and the University of Alabama at Birmingham) ascertained families with two or more members affected by Alzheimer's disease (mostly affected sibling pairs), together with unaffected relatives, from 1991 through memory disorder clinics, nursing homes and the community, using uniform procedures. It is the Alzheimer's disease collection of the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative, whose data and DNA are shared through the NIMH repository for genetic linkage and association studies." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup", IAO:0000119="PMID:9008509", IAO:0000119="PMID:18189239"}
