[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001026
name: MRC National Survey of Health and Development
def: "A birth cohort of people born in one week in March 1946 in England, Scotland and Wales, selected as a social-class-stratified sample of the singleton births to married mothers that week and followed up repeatedly from birth into old age through home visits, questionnaires and clinic assessments. The oldest of the British national birth cohort studies, it is core-funded by the UK Medical Research Council and has been developed since 2008 by the MRC Unit for Lifelong Health and Ageing at UCL into an interdisciplinary study of ageing." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:27995394", IAO:0000119="PMID:21345808", IAO:0000119="PMID:23637643"}
