[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001029
name: PROCAM-2 Study
def: "An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38839884", IAO:0000119="PMID:39112778"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
