id: coho:COHO_0001033
name: Genome-Wide Association Study of Breast Cancer in the African Diaspora
def: "A consortium for a genome-wide association study of breast cancer in women of African ancestry in Nigeria, Barbados and the United States, pooling the cases and controls of six epidemiological studies (the Nigerian Breast Cancer Study, the Barbados National Cancer Study, the Racial Variability in Genotypic Determinants of Breast Cancer Risk Study, the Chicago Cancer Prone Study, the Baltimore Breast Cancer Study and the Southern Community Cohort Study), genotyped together on the Illumina HumanOmni2.5 array." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28171663", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:29302764"}
