[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001038
name: Vitamin Intervention for Stroke Prevention
def: "A double-blind, randomised, multicentre trial run from 1996 to 2003 at 56 hospitals and neurology practices in the United States, Canada and Scotland, in which adults aged 35 or older with a recent nondisabling ischaemic stroke and a screening plasma homocysteine above the 25th percentile received high-dose or low-dose folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12, to test whether lowering homocysteine prevents recurrent stroke." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:14762035", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:11174041"}
