[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001049
name: Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium
def: "A consortium, initiated in 2010, that pools genome-wide genotype data on colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls of East Asian ancestry from studies in China, Japan and South Korea, among them the Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies and colorectal cancer studies from Shanghai, Guangzhou, Aichi, BioBank Japan and several Korean centres, to identify genetic risk factors for colorectal cancer." [] {IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30529582"}
