[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001050
name: AIDS Clinical Trials Group
def: "A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://actgnetwork.org/about/", IAO:0000119="PMID:14583845", IAO:0000119="PMID:21051598", IAO:0000119="PMID:2671281"}
