[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001051
name: genetic Association study in individuals from Diverse Ancestral backgrounds with Multiple Sclerosis
def: "A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37197821"}
