id: coho:COHO_0001052
name: ADVANCE trial
def: "A randomised, open-label, investigator-led phase 3 non-inferiority trial of first-line antiretroviral therapy, run by the University of the Witwatersrand (study WRHI 060) at sites in Johannesburg, South Africa, which from February 2017 randomised people aged 12 years or older with HIV-1 who had not received antiretroviral therapy in the previous 6 months to dolutegravir and emtricitabine with either tenofovir alafenamide or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, or to efavirenz, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate and emtricitabine, and followed them for 96 weeks, later extended to 192 weeks." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:31339677", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03122262"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "ADVANCE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "ADVANCE Study of DTG + TAF + FTC vs DTG + TDF + FTC and EFV + TDF+FTC in First-line Antiretroviral Therapy" RELATED []
synonym: "WRHI 060" RELATED []
