[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001053
name: Atherosclerotic Disease, Vascular Function, and Genetic Epidemiology Study
def: "A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18443000", IAO:0000119="PMID:21917174", IAO:0000119="PMID:18413559", IAO:0000119="PMID:27030599"}
