[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001055
name: Autopsy-Confirmed Parkinson Disease GWAS Consortium
def: "A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson's disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients' spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease with less diagnostic misclassification." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25663231", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1"}
