[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001060
name: BiDirect Study
def: "A prospective observational study run by the University of Münster, Germany, of three cohorts of adults aged 35–65 examined in parallel with identical methods: patients treated for an acute depressive episode and patients after an acute myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, recruited through psychiatric and cardiological hospitals and clinics in and around Münster, and reference participants randomly sampled from the city's population register, with a baseline examination in 2010–2013 and repeated follow-ups, to investigate the bidirectional relationship between depression and subclinical arteriosclerosis." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:22736162", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24924233"}
