[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001071
name: Columbia University COVID-19 Biobank
def: "A biobank set up at Columbia University Irving Medical Center in New York City, United States, in response to the city's COVID-19 surge in March 2020, which kept residual blood and urine samples left over from clinical testing of consecutive patients with PCR-confirmed COVID-19, of any age, sex or ancestry, treated at the medical center." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:36062073", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:34642645"}
