[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001072
name: FIN-D2D 2007
def: "A population-based health examination survey of a random sample of people aged 45–74, drawn from the National Population Register and stratified by sex, age group and area, in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, South Ostrobothnia and Central Finland, Finland, examined in October–December 2007 at the end of FIN-D2D, the implementation project of Finland's national type 2 diabetes prevention programme, to measure the prevalence of diabetes, cardiovascular disease and their risk factors and to evaluate the programme." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20459722", IAO:0000119="PMID:23555291", IAO:0000119="PMID:21595955"}
