[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001075
name: Finnish Diabetes Prevention Study
def: "A randomised controlled trial at five centres in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Turku, Tampere and Oulu) that from 1993 to 1998 randomised overweight men and women aged 40–64 with impaired glucose tolerance to intensive individual diet and exercise counselling or to a control group, to test whether lifestyle change prevents type 2 diabetes, and whose participants continued to be followed with yearly visits after the trial." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:20980412", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23555291", IAO:0000119="PMID:40583490"}
