[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001076
name: Duke study of Functional Endpoints for Age-related Macular Degeneration
def: "A single-centre, prospective, longitudinal observational natural-history study at the Duke Eye Center in Durham, North Carolina, United States, which from 2013 enrolled people aged 50 or over with early or intermediate (dry) age-related macular degeneration from the centre's patients, together with controls from Duke optometry and comprehensive eye clinics or the patients' family and friends, and assessed them with retinal imaging and with visual function tests repeated about every six months over 24 months, to find functional end points for clinical trials." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:42560005", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01822873", IAO:0000119="PMID:36245764"}
