id: coho:COHO_0001079
name: Early-Onset Venous Thrombosis
def: "A French case-control study of venous thrombosis whose cases, from medical centres in Grenoble, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, had a documented idiopathic deep vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism before the age of 50 without acquired risk factors or major thrombophilia defects, and whose controls were healthy French participants of the SU.VI.MAX study. It was genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of venous thrombosis." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37399490", IAO:0000119="PMID:21980494", IAO:0000119="PMID:23509962"}
