id: coho:COHO_0001082
name: Greater Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky Stroke Study
def: "A population-based study of stroke incidence, risk factors, treatment and outcomes in the biracial population of a five-county region of southwestern Ohio and northern Kentucky, United States, around Cincinnati, which ascertains all hospitalized and autopsied strokes and transient ischaemic attacks among residents during one-year study periods held since 1993 (July 1993 to June 1994, 1999, 2005, 2010 and 2015), to measure temporal trends in stroke incidence and outcome." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38700029", IAO:0000119="PMID:28645938", IAO:0000119="PMID:38533959", IAO:0000119="PMID:9472883"}
