[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001087
name: International Agency for Research on Cancer Central Europe Study
def: "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract (oral cavity, pharynx, larynx and oesophagus), coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banská Bystrica (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic) to investigate genetic susceptibility to these cancers and its interaction with alcohol and tobacco use. It is the upper aerodigestive tract arm of IARC's central European multicentre case–control study of lung, head and neck and kidney cancers, and part of its controls are shared with the lung cancer arm." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22655231", IAO:0000119="PMID:21437268", IAO:0000119="PMID:16614111"}
