[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001088
name: Institute for Behavioral Genetics
def: "A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:35378236", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23092589", IAO:0000119="PMID:23158098"}
