[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001091
name: INGI-Val Borbera
def: "A population-based cohort of adults descended from the inhabitants of the upper Val Borbera, a genetically isolated valley in the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, north-west Italy, recruited on the basis of their ancestry in the valley's villages and nearby areas, with clinical and anthropometric data collected by physicians of San Raffaele Hospital, Milan, to identify genes and variants underlying common disorders and quantitative traits; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19847309", IAO:0000119="PMID:37174278"}
