[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001095
name: Krakow stroke genetics study
def: "An ongoing, prospective, single-centre, hospital-based study of consecutive consenting patients of European origin with first-ever or recurrent ischaemic stroke admitted since 2002 to the Stroke Unit of the Jagiellonian University in Krakow, Poland, with stroke subtypes assigned by TOAST and CCS criteria, together with unrelated stroke-free controls from the population of southern Poland; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24021684", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
