[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001096
name: Leuven Stroke Genetics Study
def: "A prospective hospital-based study of patients of European descent with cerebral ischaemia (a clinical stroke with imaging confirmation, or a transient ischaemic attack with a new ischaemic lesion on diffusion-weighted imaging) admitted to the Stroke Unit of the University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, from 2005 to 2009, with standardised diagnostic work-up and TOAST subtyping, together with controls recruited from the same population; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24021684", IAO:0000119="PMID:29867722", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
