[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001097
name: Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate
def: "A multicentre, clinic-based case-control study of prostate cancer run since 2016 by the Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate (MADCaP) Network at seven accrual centres in Ghana, Nigeria, Senegal and South Africa, with partner institutions in the United States, which under common eligibility criteria, instruments and biosample protocols enrols men over 30 who self-identify as black African: incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer cases from urology and oncology clinics, and cancer-free controls frequency-matched by age from other clinics in the same catchment areas, to study the genetics and epidemiology of prostate cancer in sub-Saharan Africa." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30260755"}
