id: coho:COHO_0001098
name: Maywood Cohort
def: "A cohort of African-American families in Maywood, Illinois, United States, recruited from 1995 by Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine from a representative random sample of residents aged 18 to 74 for its family studies of blood pressure and the genetics of hypertension in populations of West African origin, in which Maywood was the United States site alongside Nigeria and Jamaica." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28430825", IAO:0000119="PMID:18433493", IAO:0000119="PMID:20400458"}
