[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001101
name: HARMONISATION study
def: "A prospective observational cohort of older multi-ethnic Asian patients aged 50 or over with no cognitive impairment, mild cognitive impairment or dementia due to Alzheimer's disease and/or cerebrovascular disease, recruited from 2010 at the memory clinics of the National University Hospital and St Luke's Hospital in Singapore and assessed by the Memory Aging and Cognition Centre, National University of Singapore, with annual clinical and neuropsychological follow-up for up to five years and brain MRI, retinal and blood biomarker data, to study vascular cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41160443", IAO:0000119="PMID:40796328", IAO:0000119="PMID:41988974", IAO:0000119="PMID:38038215"}
