[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001109
name: Genetics of Hypertension in Blacks
def: "A Loyola University Chicago project on the genetics of hypertension in people of West African origin, whose genome-wide association sample consists of unrelated Yoruba-speaking adults with normal or raised blood pressure from Igbo-Ora, a rural town, and Idikan, a low-income neighbourhood of Ibadan, in southwest Nigeria, recruited as part of a long-term study of the environmental and genetic factors underlying hypertension; the Idikan participants were controls of the Africa America Diabetes Mellitus study." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21573225", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22615923", IAO:0000119="PMID:20400458", IAO:0000119="PMID:21998595"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
