[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001114
name: Severe Asthma Research Program
def: "A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI's Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:34536413", IAO:0000119="PMID:17208583", IAO:0000119="PMID:28866107"}
