[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001115
name: Sickle Cell Clinical Research and Intervention Program
def: "A lifespan cohort study of people with sickle cell disease in the United States, established in 2014 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, that prospectively enrols patients at St. Jude (the coordinating site), two other sickle cell centres and St. Jude affiliate sites, collects retrospective and longitudinal clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial and health-outcome data and banks biological samples, to study disease progression from childhood into adulthood and the long-term effects of therapies." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41870384", IAO:0000119="PMID:29797644", IAO:0000119="PMID:39373640"}
