[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001119
name: Sisters in Breast Screening Study
def: "A family study in the United Kingdom that from October 2002 recruited women attending the Cambridge and Huntingdon NHS breast screening services who had one or more female blood relatives (sisters, half-sisters, first cousins, aunts or nieces) who had also had screening mammograms, with further families found through newspaper and radio advertisements, to map genes underlying quantitative phenotypes related to breast cancer, in particular mammographic breast density and sex steroid hormone levels." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35414113", IAO:0000119="PMID:22266113", IAO:0000119="PMID:20570912"}
