[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001120
name: St. Jude Lifetime Cohort Study
def: "A retrospective cohort with prospective follow-up, established in 2007 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital in Memphis, Tennessee, of survivors of paediatric cancer diagnosed and treated there between 1962 and 2012 who have survived at least five years from diagnosis (until 2015, only adults who had survived ten years), with frequency-matched community controls, who are invited back to the hospital at least every five years for protocol-based medical assessments, patient-reported outcomes and biospecimen collection, to study late health outcomes of childhood cancer and its treatment." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21370418", IAO:0000119="PMID:33374007"}
