[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001125
name: ThyroidOmics Consortium
def: "An international consortium of large, well-phenotyped cohort studies, mostly population-based, formed to study the determinants and effects of thyroid diseases and thyroid function with genomic, epigenomic, transcriptomic, proteomic and metabolomic data, which meta-analyses genome-wide association data from its member cohorts on thyroid-stimulating hormone, free thyroxine, triiodothyronine, thyroid dysfunction and related traits and makes the summary statistics available." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38291025", IAO:0000119="https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/", IAO:0000119="PMID:30367059"}
