id: coho:COHO_0001131
name: Washington University St. Louis Stroke Study
def: "A hospital-based collection of ischaemic stroke patients admitted from August 2008 to Barnes-Jewish Hospital/Washington University Medical Center in St. Louis, Missouri, identified by screening emergency department and inpatient stroke service admissions regardless of age, race or ethnicity and followed up at 90 days, whose DNA came from an acute tPA pharmacogenomics study, the Recovery Genomics after Ischemic Stroke (ReGenesIS) study and the Cognitive Rehabilitation and Recovery Group (CRRG) stroke registry; one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24021684", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
