relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/China {xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8648780/fullTextXML", comment="The 4D-SZ cohort (multi-omics, with more data to come, from Shenzhen, China) at present have high-depth whole-genome sequencing data from 2984 individuals"}
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Eastern_Asia
property_value: coho:numberOfParticipants "2984" xsd:integer {IAO:0000116="Shenzhen participants with high-depth whole-genome sequencing (as of 2021)", xref="PMID:34873157", comment="The 4D-SZ cohort (multi-omics, with more data to come, from Shenzhen, China) at present have high-depth whole-genome sequencing data from 2984 individuals (mean depth of 33×, ranging from 15× to 78×, Supplementary Table S1 and Fig."}
property_value: IAO:0000112 "GCST90255364" xsd:string {dcterms:title="Sex differences in the oral microbiome, host traits, and their causal relationships.", xref="PMID:36660475", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9843272/fullTextXML", comment="The 4D-SZ cohort is a well-designed multi-omics cohort,15,16,17,18 with shotgun data for the metagenome across multiple body sites and the host genome, as well as metabolic traits, detailed questionnaires, and clinical information."}

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001141
name: obsolete Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. The Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study is the same cohort as the Sikh Diabetes Study, which its investigators write as AIDHS/SDS ('the AIDHS (also named the SDS)', PMID:23300278); it was minted twice, once from each of the catalog tags AIDHS and SDS. COHO:0001116 (Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study/Sikh Diabetes Study) replaces it and carries all its names.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0001116

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001142
name: Age-Related Eye Disease Study
def: "A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:39826679", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000001.v3.p1", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:10588299", IAO:0000119="PMID:11594942"}
