[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001143
name: Age-Related Eye Disease Study 2
def: "A multicentre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial sponsored by the US National Eye Institute and run from 2006 to 2012 at 82 clinical centres in the United States. It enrolled people aged 50 to 85 at risk of progressing to advanced age-related macular degeneration to test whether adding lutein plus zeaxanthin or omega-3 fatty acids to the AREDS supplement formulation, or removing beta carotene or lowering zinc, changes that risk." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:23644932", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22840421"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
