[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001147
name: Brain Development and Air Pollution Ultrafine Particles in School Children
def: "A prospective cohort of children aged 7–10 years in grades 2 to 4 at 39 primary schools in Barcelona, Spain, selected as pairs with high and low traffic-related air pollution, whose working memory and attention were tested four times, every three months, from January 2012 to March 2013, with brain MRI in a subsample, to study the effects of traffic-related air pollution on cognitive and brain development." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25734425", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:31539824"}
