[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001150
name: Black Women's Health Study
def: "A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses' Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/", IAO:0000119="PMID:40050615"}
