[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001151
name: Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes Study
def: "A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:23340891", IAO:0000119="PMID:14578303", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24130360", IAO:0000119="PMID:30943964"}
