[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001152
name: Collaborative Association Study of Psoriasis
def: "A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19169254", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1"}
