[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001156
name: Collaborative European NeuroTrauma Effectiveness Research in Traumatic Brain Injury
def: "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25525693", IAO:0000119="PMID:31526754", IAO:0000119="PMID:34351445"}
