id: coho:COHO_0001162
name: Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Study
def: "A longitudinal study of the health and behaviour of a complete birth cohort: children born at Queen Mary Maternity Hospital, Dunedin, New Zealand, between April 1972 and March 1973 and still living in the greater Dunedin area at age 3. They were assessed in day-long multidisciplinary phases from age 3 through childhood and adolescence into midlife, by the Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Research Unit of the University of Otago." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:42101744", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25835958"}
