[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001163
name: European Community Respiratory Health Survey
def: "A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28974648", IAO:0000119="PMID:30723731", IAO:0000119="PMID:30764884", IAO:0000119="https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-ii", IAO:0000119="https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-i", IAO:0000119="https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iii", IAO:0000119="https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv"}
