[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001165
name: Echinococcus Multilocularis and Internal Diseases in Leutkirch
def: "A population-based study of the residents of the town of Leutkirch in Baden-Württemberg, south-western Germany, designed by the State Health Department of Baden-Württemberg and the University of Ulm, for which inhabitants aged 10 to 65 years were selected at random from the municipal population register and examined in November and December 2002 (EMIL-I) with a questionnaire, anthropometry, abdominal ultrasound and blood sampling. Its original aim, the prevalence of infection with the fox tapeworm Echinococcus multilocularis, was extended to internal diseases and public health, and a subsample was re-examined in 2013 (EMIL-II)." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:30885181", IAO:0000119="PMID:16981990", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
