[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001166
name: Early Pseudomonas Infection Control Observational Study
def: "A prospective, multicentre observational cohort of children with cystic fibrosis aged 12 years or younger who were free of Pseudomonas aeruginosa at enrolment (no earlier positive respiratory culture, or at least two years of negative cultures) or were taking part in the companion Early Pseudomonas Infection Control clinical trial, enrolled in 2004-2006 at 59 cystic fibrosis care centres in the United States and led from the University of Washington and Seattle Children's Hospital. Participants were followed through encounter-based data collection built on the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry, annual family surveys, respiratory cultures and banked serum, bacterial isolates and DNA, to identify risk factors for early acquisition of P. aeruginosa and to describe its clinical consequences." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19470318", IAO:0000119="PMID:26061914", IAO:0000119="PMID:22554417", IAO:0000119="PMID:39260370"}
