[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001167
name: Environmental Risk Longitudinal Twin Study
def: "A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King's College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:40350583", IAO:0000119="https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "E-Risk" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
