[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001168
name: Gabapentin for chronic pelvic pain in women
def: "The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:39258169", IAO:0000119="PMID:32979978"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
