id: coho:COHO_0001172
name: Genetic and Environmental Risk Factors for Alzheimer's Disease Among African Americans Study
def: "A case-control study of Alzheimer's disease in community-dwelling African Americans aged 65 or older, led from Johns Hopkins University, whose participants were identified through the electronic claims database of the Henry Ford Health System in Detroit, Michigan, and had a proxy informant; cases met NINCDS-ADRDA criteria for possible or probable Alzheimer's disease at a consensus conference, and controls were cognitively normal." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22159054", IAO:0000119="https://dss.niagads.org/cohorts/genetic-and-environmental-risk-factors-for-alzheimers-disease-among-african-americans-generaations/", IAO:0000119="PMID:20697030"}
