[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001180
name: Genetic Modifier Study of Severe CF Liver Disease
def: "A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19738092", IAO:0000119="PMID:30307979", IAO:0000119="PMID:27062904"}
