[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001181
name: GSK
def: "A pharmacogenetic sample of adult outpatients of white European ancestry with moderate to severe major depressive disorder who completed escitalopram treatment in two identically designed randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled GlaxoSmithKline trials run in the United States in 2003–2004 to compare bupropion XL with escitalopram for antidepressant efficacy and effects on sexual functioning; GlaxoSmithKline contributed their DNA to the NEWMEDS consortium for genetic studies of antidepressant response." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23091423", IAO:0000119="PMID:35712048", IAO:0000119="PMID:16841623"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "Glaxo Smith Kline" RELATED []
synonym: "Glaxo-Smith Kline" RELATED []
instance_of: coho:COHO_0000000 ! cohort
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States {xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9117153/supplementaryFiles", comment="The studies were parallel groups and identically designed, conducted between January 2003 and June 2004 in the United States."}
property_value: coho:numberOfParticipants "191" xsd:integer {IAO:0000116="escitalopram-arm participants contributed by GlaxoSmithKline to NEWMEDS", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3472989/fullTextXML", comment="As part of the NEWMEDS consortium (http://www.newmeds-europe.com) [13], three studies conducted by academic institutions (GENDEP, a part-randomized open study of two active antidepressants, n = 868; GENPOD, a randomized controlled trial of two active antidepressants, n = 601; and GODS, a treatment cohort of severe depression, n = 131) [14]–[16] and two studies by pharmaceutical industry members of the European Federation of Pharmaceutical Industries and Associations (active comparator arms from randomized controlled trials by Pfizer, n = 355, and GlaxoSmithKline, n = 191) were combined to obtain a sample of 2,146 adult individuals (1,205 women and 941 men; see Table 1 in Text S1 for description by contributing study) diagnosed with unipolar MDD according to the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders–IV and the International Classification of Diseases–10, with prospective data on outcome of treatment with SRI or NRI antidepressants."}
property_value: IAO:0000112 "GCST90244577" xsd:string {dcterms:title="Identifying the Common Genetic Basis of Antidepressant Response.", xref="PMID:35712048", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9117153/supplementaryFiles", comment="The samples from GSK derived from two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled comparisons of the antidepressant efficacy and the effects on sexual functioning of Bupropion XL and escitalopram in outpatients with moderate to severe depression (22)."}
property_value: IAO:0000116 "GSK is GlaxoSmithKline, a company. The GWAS Catalog uses the cohort tag GSK for the pharmacogenetic sample from two GlaxoSmithKline escitalopram trials pooled in the antidepressant-response GWAS (GCST90244577, GCST90244578), which is what this term denotes; the GSK Munich recurrent major depression case-control study (COHO:0001182) is a different GlaxoSmithKline sample, and studies that name GlaxoSmithKline only as a funder or sponsor are not this cohort." xsd:string

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001182
name: GSK Munich recurrent major depression case-control study
def: "A case-control sample for recurrent major depressive disorder, collected with GlaxoSmithKline, of German patients with recurrent moderate or severe major depression recruited at the Max Planck Institute of Psychiatry in Munich and two satellite hospitals in the Munich area (BKH Augsburg and Klinikum Ingolstadt), and age- and sex-matched controls from a Munich community sample screened free of lifetime mood and anxiety disorders, genotyped genome-wide for studies of the genetics of depression." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19107115", IAO:0000119="PMID:16822851", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2012.21/MediaObjects/41380_2013_BFmp201221_MOESM194_ESM.doc"}
