[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001183
name: Great Smoky Mountains Study
def: "A longitudinal, population-based study of children from 11 predominantly rural counties of western North Carolina, United States, recruited in 1993 as three cohorts aged 9, 11 and 13 through a two-phase design that screened a random sample of children for behavioural problems and oversampled those with high scores, together with all age-eligible American Indian children of the area. The participants were interviewed annually to age 16 and then repeatedly into adulthood, to study the development of psychiatric and substance use disorders and the need for and use of mental health services." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:8956679", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24342383", IAO:0000119="PMID:23461817"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
