[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001186
name: Health2008 Study
def: "A cross-sectional population-based study of the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Denmark, conducted in 2008–2009 on a random sample of men and women aged 30–60, drawn from the Danish Central Personal Register, living in the western part of the Copenhagen area; pregnant women and people with known diabetes, cardiovascular disease, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, hypertension or a history of blood clots, or unable to do physical activities such as climbing stairs, were excluded. The examination included questionnaires, clinical and biochemical measurements, an oral glucose tolerance test and two tests estimating maximal oxygen uptake." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26372449", IAO:0000119="PMID:23022702", IAO:0000119="PMID:22587629"}
