[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001190
name: Hvidoere Remission Phase Study
def: "A multinational longitudinal cohort of children and adolescents under 16 with newly diagnosed type 1 diabetes, recruited from August 1999 to December 2000 at 18 paediatric departments in 15 countries of Europe and Japan by the Hvidoere Study Group on Childhood Diabetes, an international group of paediatric diabetes centres, and followed through the first 12 months after diagnosis with meal-stimulated C-peptide tests, HbA1c, insulin doses, islet autoantibodies and HLA typing, to study residual beta-cell function and the partial remission period." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21429197", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19435955", IAO:0000119="PMID:33203694", IAO:0000119="PMID:19708904"}
