[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001197
name: Japan Prospective Studies Collaboration for Aging and Dementia
def: "A multisite, population-based prospective cohort study of dementia, coordinated from Kyushu University. Community-dwelling residents aged 65 years or older at eight research sites across Japan (Hirosaki, Yahaba, Nakajima, Arakawa, Ama, Nakayama, Hisayama and Arao) were examined in 2016–2018 under a common standardized protocol, including questionnaires, cognitive assessment, blood tests, brain MRI and DNA samples, and are followed up for incident dementia, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for dementia and their interaction." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:33129280", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "JPSC-AD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
