[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001201
name: Luxembourg Parkinson's Study
def: "A nation-wide, monocentric, observational, longitudinal-prospective cohort of people with Parkinson's disease or atypical parkinsonism at any disease stage, and of control subjects without a neurodegenerative disorder, recruited since 2015 in Luxembourg and the surrounding Greater Region of Germany, France and Belgium within the National Centre of Excellence in Research on Parkinson's Disease (NCER-PD). Patients are followed up annually with deep clinical phenotyping and biosampling, to find markers for early diagnosis and progression." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30420802", IAO:0000119="PMID:38174101"}
