[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001203
name: Mammary Carcinoma Risk Factor Investigation
def: "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal breast cancer in two regions of Germany, Hamburg and Rhine-Neckar-Karlsruhe, which from 2002 to 2005 enrolled women aged 50–74 with incident invasive or in situ breast cancer and population controls frequency-matched to them, interviewed face to face to investigate risk factors, notably menopausal hormone therapy. Its cases were re-interviewed in 2009 and followed for survival and recurrence until 2015 as the MARIE patient cohort." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:31694687", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37964298", IAO:0000119="PMID:18506692"}
