[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001204
name: Mayo Clinic Study of Aging
def: "A prospective population-based cohort of residents of Olmsted County, Minnesota, United States, randomly sampled with age and sex stratification from the population enumerated by the Rochester Epidemiology Project medical records-linkage system: people aged 70–89 from 2004, extended in 2012 to ages 50–69 and later to younger adults. Participants have in-person clinical, neurological and neuropsychological evaluations with a consensus diagnosis of normal cognition, mild cognitive impairment or dementia, repeated about every 15 months together with neuroimaging and biomarkers, to study the prevalence, incidence, risk factors and biomarkers of mild cognitive impairment and dementia." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:41001249", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:42690834", IAO:0000119="PMID:40830522", IAO:0000119="PMID:18259084"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
