[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001207
name: Michigan State University Twin Registry
def: "A twin registry at Michigan State University, begun as a university-based registry of undergraduate twins and since 2004 recruiting twins identified from birth records by the Michigan Department of Health and Human Services. Its population-based mail-in registry enrols child and adolescent twins aged 3–17 with their families and adult twins aged 18–55 living in lower Michigan, United States, and in-depth in-person twin family studies are drawn from it, to examine developmental differences in genetic, environmental, neural and neurobiological influences on psychopathology and resilience, particularly in childhood and adolescence." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23101567", IAO:0000119="PMID:31466551"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
