[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001210
name: Carolina Breast Cancer Study
def: "A population-based study of breast cancer among women aged 20–74 in central and eastern North Carolina, United States, run from the University of North Carolina, which identifies newly diagnosed cases through rapid case ascertainment with the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry and oversamples Black and younger women. Phases I (1993–1996) and II (1996–2001) in 24 counties were a case-control study with controls drawn from Department of Motor Vehicles and Medicare enrolment records; phase III (2008–2013) enrolled invasive cases in 44 counties and followed them for recurrence, to study the biology, risk factors and outcomes of breast cancer and their differences by race and age." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33479248", IAO:0000119="PMID:36968228", IAO:0000119="PMID:27492244"}
