[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001211
name: North Carolina Bladder Cancer Study
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer in North Carolina, United States, which enrolled patients with transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder and control patients without cancer (mainly presenting with benign prostatic hypertrophy or impotence), frequency-matched on race, sex and age, at the urology clinics of Duke University Medical Center and the University of North Carolina Hospitals, to study inherited variation in carcinogen-metabolism and DNA-repair genes, smoking and bladder cancer risk." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19706757", IAO:0000119="PMID:11219769", IAO:0000119="PMID:8320745"}
