[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001223
name: Parkinson Research Examination of CEP-1347 Trial
def: "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial run by the Parkinson Study Group, which enrolled people with early Parkinson's disease not yet requiring dopaminergic therapy at 65 sites in the United States and Canada between April 2002 and April 2004 to test whether the mixed lineage kinase inhibitor CEP-1347 could slow disease progression; the trial was stopped early for futility in 2005, and its participants were then followed in the observational PostCEPT study." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:18413464", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17881719", IAO:0000119="PMID:27717005"}
