[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001236
name: Study of Osteoporotic Fractures
def: "A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:37402774", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37619450", IAO:0000119="PMID:28465840"}
