[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001240
name: Swedish Twin study of CHild and Adolescent Development
def: "A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:37289452", IAO:0000119="PMID:28638965", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://ki.se/en/meb/twin-study-of-child-and-adolescent-development-tchad", IAO:0000119="PMID:17539366", IAO:0000119="PMID:29845340"}
