[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001241
name: Transforming Research and Clinical Knowledge in Traumatic Brain Injury
def: "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:36939699", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02119182", IAO:0000119="PMID:35301180"}
