[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001244
name: U.S. Radiologic Technologists Study
def: "A cohort of current and former radiologic technologists in the United States, women and men certified by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists for at least two years between 1926 and 1982, assembled in 1982 by the US National Cancer Institute with the University of Minnesota and the Registry and followed through four mailed questionnaires (1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005 and 2012–2014), to assess risks of cancer and other diseases from protracted low-dose occupational and personal medical ionising radiation and other exposures." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists", IAO:0000119="PMID:29992993"}
