[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001249
name: Vanderbilt Atrial Fibrillation Registry
def: "A clinical and genetic registry at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, founded in 2001, that prospectively enrols patients with atrial fibrillation together with affected and unaffected family members, recording a detailed medical and drug history, an atrial fibrillation symptom severity assessment and a blood sample for DNA, and follows them with serial symptom assessments; its early-onset cases were whole-genome sequenced by the NHLBI TOPMed programme." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30271950", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001032.v7.p2"}
