[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001251
name: Wisconsin Sleep Cohort Study
def: "A population-based longitudinal cohort study of the University of Wisconsin-Madison in which Wisconsin state employees aged 30 to 60, sampled from state payroll files, answered a mailed sleep and health survey in 1988, after which all respondents at high risk of sleep-disordered breathing by self-reported snoring, with an age- and sex-matched random sample of the others, were invited to overnight in-laboratory polysomnography repeated at about 4-year intervals, to study the natural history and health consequences of sleep-disordered breathing and other sleep disorders." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35670608", IAO:0000119="PMID:19743755"}
