[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001254
name: Project Viva
def: "A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24639442", IAO:0000119="PMID:37012456"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
