[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001255
name: GERO cohort
def: "A population-based cohort of community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over without dementia but with a subjective cognitive complaint. They were recruited door to door from 2017 in three districts of Santiago, Chile (Macul, Peñalolén and La Reina), by the Geroscience Center for Brain Health and Metabolism (GERO), and are followed at 18 and 36 months with clinical, neuropsychological, neuroimaging, blood and stool assessments to study the rate of functional decline and progression to dementia and their risk factors." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33238908"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
