[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001257
name: STORK study
def: "A prospective cohort of healthy pregnant women of Scandinavian heritage with singleton pregnancies who registered for obstetric care and gave birth at Oslo University Hospital, Rikshospitalet, Norway, in 2001–2008. The women had four antenatal visits (weeks 14–16, 22–24, 30–32 and 36–38) with fasting blood samples and ultrasound, and oral glucose tolerance tests at weeks 14–16 and 30–32, to study the determinants of fetal growth and birthweight in healthy pregnancies." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22723995", IAO:0000119="PMID:23460863"}
