[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001258
name: San Antonio Longitudinal Study of Aging
def: "A community-based longitudinal study of the disablement process in older Mexican Americans and European Americans in San Antonio, Texas. Its participants, the oldest members (aged 65 and over) of the San Antonio Heart Study cohort, had been randomly sampled from low-, middle- and high-income (barrio, transitional and suburban) neighbourhoods. They had a baseline examination in 1992–1996, combining a home-based assessment with a performance-based assessment at a clinical research center, and three follow-up examinations 18 months apart in 2000–2005." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21216857", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21054295", IAO:0000119="PMID:25597562"}
