[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001271
name: Die Deutsche Diabetes Dialyse Studie
def: "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37806305", IAO:0000119="PMID:37779851", IAO:0000119="PMID:10412782"}
