id: coho:COHO_0001278
name: Anxiety NeuroGenetics STudy
def: "A consortium of seven independent studies of people of European ancestry in the United States, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Germany and Australia (the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia control sample, PsyCoLaus, the Rotterdam Study, the Study of Health in Pomerania, the QIMR twin sample, TRAILS and NESDA/NTR), with interview-based DSM diagnoses of anxiety disorders, formed to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of generalized anxiety disorder, panic disorder, social phobia, agoraphobia and specific phobia." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26754954"}
