[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001282
name: Anglo-Scandinavian Cardiac Outcomes Trial
def: "A multicentre randomised controlled trial that recruited hypertensive men and women aged 40–79 with at least three other cardiovascular risk factors, mostly through family practices in the United Kingdom, Ireland and the Nordic countries between February 1998 and May 2000, to compare an amlodipine-based with an atenolol-based antihypertensive regimen for preventing coronary and other cardiovascular events (the Blood Pressure-Lowering Arm), those with total cholesterol of 6.5 mmol/L or less being also randomised to atorvastatin or placebo in a factorial Lipid-Lowering Arm." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38291599", IAO:0000119="PMID:40139683"}
