[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001291
name: Barbados National Cancer Study
def: "A nationwide population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents of Barbados. It was run by Stony Brook University with the Barbados Ministry of Health and the University of the West Indies and funded by the US National Human Genome Research Institute. Its breast cancer arm enrolled every histologically confirmed incident breast cancer identified by the island's only pathology department, at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, from July 2002 to March 2006, with controls randomly selected from a national database and frequency-matched by age. The aim was to study environmental and genetic risk factors in this predominantly African-origin population." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18814239", IAO:0000119="PMID:22357627"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
