[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001295
name: Canadian Spontaneous Coronary Artery Dissection Study
def: "A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30698711", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04906356", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02188069", IAO:0000119="PMID:32887874"}
