[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001296
name: Copenhagen City Heart Study
def: "A prospective cardiovascular population study of an age-stratified random sample of adults aged 20 years or older living in the Østerbro district and part of Nørrebro around Rigshospitalet in Copenhagen, Denmark, launched in 1975 with a first examination in 1976–1978 and re-examinations in 1981–1983, 1991–1994, 2001–2003 and 2011–2013, whose participants are followed through the Danish national registers. Its original purpose was the prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke; lung disease, dementia, ageing, genetics and other topics were added later." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:26779513", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35379992"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
