[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001302
name: Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology
def: "A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:20041166", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20205591", IAO:0000119="PMID:21160409", IAO:0000119="PMID:24910414", IAO:0000119="PMID:23935489"}
