[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001304
name: Chronic Kidney Disease in Children Study
def: "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of children with chronic kidney disease in the United States and Canada, funded since 2003 by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and coordinated from Children's Mercy Hospital in Kansas City and Johns Hopkins (later the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia), which since 2005 has enrolled children aged 6 months to 16 years at paediatric nephrology centres and later also young adults. Participants have annual visits with measured glomerular filtration rate, questionnaires on cognition, behaviour and quality of life, cardiovascular assessments and stored biosamples and DNA, to identify risk factors for the decline of kidney function and its effects on cardiovascular risk, neurocognitive function and behaviour, and growth." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35518833", IAO:0000119="PMID:17699320", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00327860"}
