[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001305
name: UCLA Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics
def: "A sample of adults aged 21–50 studied at the University of California, Los Angeles, by the Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics, one of the NIH Roadmap interdisciplinary research consortia of 2007–2012: mainly healthy White non-Hispanic or Hispanic adults recruited by community advertisement in the Los Angeles area, with smaller groups with schizophrenia, bipolar disorder or ADHD recruited through local clinics and online portals. Participants had diagnostic interviews, neurocognitive testing and blood sampling for genotyping, and a subset had structural, diffusion and functional MRI, to study memory and response-inhibition phenotypes dimensionally from genome to syndrome." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37582857", IAO:0000119="PMID:27922632"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "CNP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics" RELATED []
