[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001311
name: Drakenstein Child Health Study
def: "A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks' gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25228292", IAO:0000119="PMID:38177345"}
