[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001315
name: Detroit Neighborhood Health Study
def: "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 18 or older living in the city of Detroit, Michigan, most of them African American, drawn from a random probability sample of the city's households and interviewed by telephone in annual waves from 2008 to 2013, with blood specimens collected from a subset, to study how biological variation, stressful and traumatic experiences and environmental factors contribute to post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and other psychopathology." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41821625", IAO:0000119="PMID:22745713", IAO:0000119="PMID:38177345"}
