[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001321
name: Epidemiology of Burkitt Lymphoma in East African Children and Minors
def: "A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute's intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:40646133", IAO:0000119="https://emblem.cancer.gov/"}
