id: coho:COHO_0001324
name: European/International Fibromuscular Dysplasia Registry and Initiative
def: "A registry of patients with fibromuscular dysplasia, launched in December 2015 at the First Brussels National Meeting on FMD and endorsed by the European Society of Hypertension in 2016, that enrols prevalent and incident adult patients whose multifocal or focal FMD lesions in at least one arterial bed were shown by CT angiography, MR angiography or catheter angiography, at centres in Europe and a few other countries, recording their clinical characteristics, imaging, visits and vascular interventions on an online platform with an associated DNA and RNA biobank, to characterise the clinical profiles, complications and management of the disease. It also takes in data from existing national registries such as the French NOMADE and Polish ARCADIA-POL registries." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://orbi.uliege.be/bitstream/2268/250361/1/2020%20Cardiovas%20Res_Pappaccogli-FEIRI-1000%20FMD.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:32282921"}
