[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001327
name: FinnTwin12 Cohort
def: "A population-based longitudinal cohort of the twins born in Finland in 1983–1987, the youngest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts, identified through Finland's Central Population Registry and enrolled with their biological parents in the year they reached age 11, with twin, parent and teacher questionnaires and ratings at baseline and follow-up surveys at ages 14, 17, about 22 and about 37; a subset was studied intensively with in-school assessments and peer nominations at age 12, psychiatric interviews at ages 14 and 22, and neurocognitive tests and DNA collection in early adulthood. It was designed to identify individual, familial and school and neighbourhood risks for substance use before its onset and to follow trajectories of use, abuse and their consequences into adulthood." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:31640839", IAO:0000119="https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0890856722001794-mmc2.docx", IAO:0000119="PMID:39920525"}
