[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001331
name: Genes and Blood Clotting Study
def: "A family-based study of healthy young people aged 14–35, recruited at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, United States, between June 2006 and January 2009 from the university's undergraduate and graduate students together with their biological siblings, with blood samples for measuring plasma haemostatic proteins (such as von Willebrand factor and plasminogen), genome-wide genotyping and a survey of common morphological traits, to identify the genetic factors behind variation in blood clotting in healthy people, using its sibling structure for linkage as well as association analysis." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:23267103", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25208887", IAO:0000119="PMID:40756183", IAO:0000119="PMID:40071514"}
