[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001333
name: Ghana Breast Health Study
def: "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer, a collaboration of the US National Cancer Institute with three major hospitals in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital, Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and Peace and Love Hospital), that in 2013–2015 enrolled women aged 18–74 recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy, or treated for breast cancer, at these hospitals, and population controls sampled by household enumeration of the surrounding districts and frequency-matched on age and district, collecting interviews and tumour tissue, blood, saliva and faecal samples to study breast cancer risk factors in a West African population." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:30990841", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38082317", IAO:0000119="PMID:28295287"}
