[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001334
name: GenomALC
def: "A multicentre international case–control study of alcohol-related cirrhosis, run by the GenomALC Consortium of researchers in Australia, France, Germany, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and the United States with funding from the US National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, that from September 2012 recruited, at liver and alcohol treatment clinics and from existing repositories of the participating centres, people who had drunk heavily (at least 80 g of alcohol a day for men or 50 g for women) for at least ten years, with alcoholic cirrhosis (cases) or without significant liver disease (controls), with interviews, clinical records and blood samples, to find genetic factors that predispose drinkers to cirrhosis. A second sample, GenomALC-2, added DNA and data that research groups in these countries and Belgium had collected for earlier genetic studies of alcohol-related liver disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38727677", IAO:0000119="PMID:25872595"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "Genetics of alcoholic liver cirrhosis consortium" RELATED []
synonym: "GenomALC Multinational Study" RELATED []
