id: coho:COHO_0001339
name: Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment
def: "A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:36699085"}
