[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001341
name: Genetics of Impulsivity project
def: "A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site's undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29120849", IAO:0000119="PMID:37582857", IAO:0000119="PMID:27449350"}
