[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001345
name: Genomic Research in Alpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency and Sarcoidosis Study
def: "A multicentre observational study in the United States, solicited by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute and run by a genomics and informatics centre with several clinical centres, that enrolled adults with sarcoidosis across defined clinical phenotypes and adults over 35 with the PiZZ or PiMZ alpha-1 antitrypsin genotypes, with questionnaires, chest CT, lung function tests, bronchoalveolar lavage and blood samples, to study the role of the lung microbiome and genome-wide gene expression in the two diseases." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26153726", IAO:0000119="PMID:26193069", IAO:0000119="PMID:35806883"}
