[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001346
name: Genomics of Resistance to Immunodeficiency Virus
def: "A collection of DNA samples, established in France in 1995, from HIV-1-infected people of European descent living in France with extreme courses of infection: long-term non-progressors (infected for more than eight years with CD4 T-cell counts above 500/mm3 and no symptoms) and rapid progressors. It is used to identify host genes associated with slow and rapid progression to AIDS, with genetic analyses comparing its members with seronegative French controls from another study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21750674", IAO:0000119="PMID:38146367", IAO:0000119="PMID:26367535"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "Genetics of Resistance to Immunodeficiency Virus" RELATED []
