[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001347
name: Guangzhou Twin Eye Study
def: "A longitudinal twin study in Guangzhou, China, that from 2006 enrolled twin pairs aged 7 to 15 years from the population-based Guangzhou Twin Registry, living near the Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center, together with some of their parents or siblings. It collected DNA and baseline eye measurements, then examined the twins annually until 2018 for progressive traits such as cycloplegic refraction, axial length, height and weight, to study the genetic and environmental causes of common eye diseases, particularly myopia." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:41117591", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:32014069", IAO:0000119="PMID:23186635", IAO:0000119="PMID:17254403"}
