[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001350
name: Hemophilia Growth and Development Study
def: "A multicentre longitudinal study, established in 1988 at 14 hemophilia treatment centres in the United States, of boys and young men aged 6 to 19 years with moderate to severe hemophilia, HIV-infected through clotting factor concentrates or HIV-uninfected, with their non-hemophiliac, HIV-uninfected male siblings as a comparison group, followed until 1996/97 to study the impact of HIV on physical growth and sexual maturation, immune function, and neurological and neuropsychological functioning." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:11075607", IAO:0000119="PMID:37532928", IAO:0000119="PMID:8498644"}
