[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001352
name: Hong Kong Children Eye Study
def: "A population-based cohort study of eye conditions, run by the Chinese University of Hong Kong since 2015, that recruits ethnic Chinese children aged 6 to 8 years from randomly selected primary schools across Hong Kong, together with their parents, and follows the children up, to determine the occurrence and development of refractive errors, strabismus, amblyopia and other eye disorders and their environmental and genetic determinants." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:36542383", IAO:0000119="PMID:31981300", IAO:0000119="PMID:34226578", IAO:0000119="PMID:40410244"}
