id: coho:COHO_0001358
name: INTERHEART study
def: "A standardised case-control study of first acute myocardial infarction, which from February 1999 to March 2003 enrolled patients presenting to hospital with a first myocardial infarction and age- and sex-matched hospital- or community-based controls without heart disease at 262 centres in 52 countries on every inhabited continent, to establish the importance of modifiable and psychosocial risk factors for myocardial infarction in all regions of the world." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:15364186", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:15364185", IAO:0000119="PMID:23202125", IAO:0000119="PMID:37414411"}
