[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001361
name: International Warfarin Pharmacogenetics Consortium
def: "A consortium of research groups in North and South America, Europe and Asia, formed with the Pharmacogenomics Knowledge Base (PharmGKB) as its data broker, that pools and curates the clinical and genetic data of warfarin-treated patients from its members' centres, to develop and evaluate pharmacogenetic algorithms for estimating the stable warfarin dose and to study the genetic determinants of warfarin dose across populations, including a genome-wide association study of African Americans from its US sites." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19228618", IAO:0000119="PMID:20203262", IAO:0000119="PMID:18330919", IAO:0000119="PMID:23755828"}
