[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001365
name: Low Concentration Atropine for Myopia Progression Study
def: "A randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial at the Chinese University of Hong Kong Eye Centre that from 2016 to 2017 enrolled children aged 4 to 12 with myopia in both eyes, limited astigmatism and documented myopic progression in the previous year, assigned them to nightly 0.05%, 0.025% or 0.01% atropine eye drops or placebo, and followed them in later phases (placebo switched to atropine, re-randomisation to continued treatment or washout, and longer-term follow-up), to evaluate the efficacy and safety of low-concentration atropine for slowing myopia progression." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:40410244", IAO:0000119="PMID:41732593", IAO:0000119="PMID:30514630"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
