[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001368
name: Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study
def: "A prospective multicentre cohort study of gay and bisexual men with and without HIV-1 infection, first enrolled in 1984–1985 at sites in Baltimore/Washington DC, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles in the United States, with later enrolment waves, and followed with interviews, physical examinations, laboratory testing and specimen banking every six months, to study the natural and treated history of HIV infection and AIDS and its risk factors; in 2019 it was combined with the Women's Interagency HIV Study into the MACS/WIHS Combined Cohort Study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37532928", IAO:0000119="PMID:33675224", IAO:0000119="PMID:3300281"}
