[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001371
name: Manchester Cancer Research Centre Biobank
def: "A research tissue bank of the Manchester Cancer Research Centre, established in 2008 and run from The Christie NHS Foundation Trust, that collects tissue, blood and other samples, with consent to use them and data about the donors for research, from patients at four NHS trusts in Greater Manchester, mainly people undergoing surgery where cancer is a possible diagnosis, to supply samples for cancer research." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/", IAO:0000119="https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/"}
