[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001372
name: MELARISK study
def: "A French study of genetic susceptibility to cutaneous melanoma that recruited histologically confirmed melanoma patients of European ancestry, enrolled for a family history of melanoma, multiple primary melanomas or diagnosis before age 40, through a nationwide network of French dermatology departments and oncogenetic clinics between 1992 and 2011, with interview, clinical examination and questionnaire data on melanoma risk factors; in genome-wide association studies its cases were compared with population-based French controls." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25892537", IAO:0000119="PMID:27347659", IAO:0000119="PMID:32341527"}
