[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001375
name: MRC Myeloma IX trial
def: "A UK Medical Research Council open-label randomised trial that enrolled adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed symptomatic multiple myeloma at 120 UK centres between May 2003 and November 2007, allocating them to an intensive pathway (induction followed by high-dose melphalan and autologous stem-cell transplantation) or a non-intensive pathway, and randomising first-line bisphosphonate (zoledronic versus clodronic acid) with induction chemotherapy and, later, maintenance treatment." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21131037"}
