[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001376
name: Mexican Genomic Database for Addiction Research
def: "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:32390825"}
