[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001379
name: UK Nephropathy Family Study and Oxford Regional Prospective Study
def: "A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:27647854", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19918004", IAO:0000119="PMID:21335371"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "NFS-ORPS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "NFS-ORPS/Cambridge" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
