[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001382
name: National Joint Registry
def: "A national registry of joint replacement surgery, set up by the Department of Health and the Welsh Government, that has recorded hip and knee replacements since April 2003 (ankle, elbow and shoulder replacements since 2010–2012) in NHS and independent hospitals in England and Wales, joined by Northern Ireland in 2013, the Isle of Man in 2015, Guernsey in 2019 and Jersey in 2025. Each procedure is recorded with the implant used and, with the patient's consent, the patient's details, to monitor the outcomes of implants, hospitals and surgeons." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.njrcentre.org.uk/about-the-njr/"}
