[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001383
name: National Psoriasis Victor Henschel BioBank
def: "A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:26626624", IAO:0000119="https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:32725812"}
