[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001385
name: New York Genome Center ALS Consortium
def: "A consortium formed in 2015 around the New York Genome Center, through which 41 ALS clinics and research institutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Greece and Israel contribute blood and post-mortem brain and spinal cord tissue from people with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, other neurological diseases and non-neurological controls. The samples are whole-genome and RNA sequenced at the New York Genome Center and their clinical data harmonised into an openly accessible genomic resource for ALS research." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text"}
