[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001389
name: Phenotype, Genotype & Biomarkers in ALS and Related Disorders
def: "A prospective, longitudinal observational study of the CReATe Consortium (Clinical Research in ALS and Related Disorders for Therapeutic Development), led from the University of Miami, that from 2014 enrolled patients with familial or sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis or a related disorder (primary lateral sclerosis, progressive muscular atrophy, hereditary spastic paraplegia, frontotemporal dementia or multisystem proteinopathy), and some of their family members, at clinical sites in the United States, South Africa and Germany, with repeated motor, cognitive and functional assessments and collection of blood, urine and cerebrospinal fluid, to study phenotype-genotype relationships and develop biomarkers for therapy development." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:39270623", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02327845", IAO:0000119="https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001"}
