[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001400
name: Genome-Wide Association Study of Adiposity in Samoans
def: "A population-based cross-sectional study of adults with four Samoan grandparents, recruited from February to July 2010 in 33 villages across all four census regions of the independent nation of Samoa (Apia Urban Area, Northwest Upolu, the rest of Upolu and Savai'i), with anthropometry, fasting blood biomarkers, dietary, physical activity, health and socio-demographic data and genome-wide genotyping, to identify genetic variation that increases susceptibility to obesity and cardiometabolic traits in Samoans." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24799123", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000914"}
