[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001402
name: Salvador-SCAALA study
def: "A cohort of children from 24 low-income areas of Salvador, Bahia, in north-eastern Brazil, first enrolled aged 0–3 years in 1997, 2001 and 2003 to evaluate the health effects of the city's sanitation programme and followed from 2005, at ages 4–11, with further surveys (questionnaires, anthropometry, stool, blood and house-dust samples, skin prick tests and, later, genome-wide genotyping), to study social, environmental, infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergic diseases; it is the Brazilian study of the Social Changes, Asthma and Allergy in Latin America (SCAALA) programme." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37497783", IAO:0000119="PMID:16796729"}
