[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001404
name: Silent Cerebral Infarct Multi-Center Clinical Trial
def: "A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25140956", IAO:0000119="PMID:39293085"}
