[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001406
name: SLOVENIA study
def: "A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28639505", IAO:0000119="PMID:34442380"}
