[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001413
name: Singapore Preconception Study of Long-Term Maternal and Child Outcomes
def: "A preconception, longitudinal cohort of Chinese, Malay or Indian women aged 18–45 who intended to conceive and deliver in Singapore, recruited in February 2015–October 2017 through a preconception clinic at KK Women's and Children's Hospital and through public outreach, and followed with their children from before conception through pregnancy into early childhood. Its aim is to study how nutrition, lifestyle and maternal mood before and during pregnancy affect the offspring's epigenome, duration of gestation, fetal growth, and metabolic and neural phenotypes." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33222050"}
subset: coho1:GWAS_subset
synonym: "S-PRESTO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
