[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001440
name: Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia cohort 1
def: "A cross-sectional, family-based study, the first cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, that from 2003 recruited households with at least one biological parent–child pair (the child aged 1–18 years), together with all other household members, mainly in rural counties of central West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, United States, and assessed them by interviews, questionnaires, oral health and microbiological examinations and DNA collection to study how individual, family and community factors contribute to oral disease in Appalachia." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18522740", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000095.v3.p1", IAO:0000119="PMID:26106416"}
