[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001444
name: Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia cohort 2
def: "A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:26089906", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38404680"}
