[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001467
name: Alcoholic Cirrhosis GWAS
def: "A genome-wide association study of alcohol-related cirrhosis in people of European descent that meta-analysed two case–control data sets, one from Germany and one from the United Kingdom, comparing patients with alcohol-related cirrhosis with drinking controls to find genetic risk loci for the disease; its discovery results were published in 2015 and its summary statistics have been reused by later studies of cirrhosis." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38727677", IAO:0000119="PMID:33310085", IAO:0000119="PMID:26482880", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3417/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="http://gengastro.med.tu-dresden.de/suppl/alc_cirrhosis/"}
