[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001468
name: University of Manchester Longitudinal Study of Cognition in Normal Healthy Old Age
def: "A longitudinal cohort of healthy community-dwelling volunteers in middle and old age, recruited in Greater Manchester and Newcastle upon Tyne, England, between 1983 and the early 1990s by the University of Manchester's Age and Cognitive Performance Research Centre to chart trajectories of cognitive function in normal old age; participants took alternating batteries of cognitive tests every two years until 2003, with questionnaires on health and behaviour repeated until 2017. Blood was collected for DNA extraction, a Manchester subsample was physically examined and gave saliva, serum and plasma in 2003, and some participants donated their brains to the Manchester Brain Bank." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:31796669", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21826061", IAO:0000119="PMID:34113784", IAO:0000119="PMID:30075734", IAO:0000119="PMID:40908294"}
