[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001473
name: ADHD-VHIR study
def: "A case–control collection of the Psychiatric Genetics Unit of the Vall d'Hebron Research Institute (VHIR) in Barcelona, Spain, of adults of European origin with attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, recruited and evaluated at the Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, and of unrelated blood donors screened for lifetime ADHD symptoms, genotyped genome-wide to identify loci conferring susceptibility to persistent ADHD." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25284319", IAO:0000119="PMID:29531354"}
