[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001474
name: Action in Diabetes and Vascular disease: Preterax and Diamicron-MR Controlled Evaluation
def: "A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:11596665", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16075030", IAO:0000119="PMID:21972410", IAO:0000119="PMID:31967344"}
