[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001477
name: Early Treatment of Atrial Fibrillation for Stroke Prevention Trial
def: "An investigator-initiated, multicentre, parallel-group, open, blinded-outcome-assessment randomised trial sponsored by the Atrial Fibrillation Network (AFNET), which from July 2011 to December 2016 randomised patients with atrial fibrillation diagnosed within the previous year and cardiovascular risk factors, at 135 sites in 11 European countries, to early rhythm control therapy or usual care, to test whether early rhythm control prevents cardiovascular complications; its biosample substudy took blood at enrolment from consenting patients." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:40737012", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37264683", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01288352", IAO:0000119="PMID:34473249"}
