[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001481
name: San Francisco Bay Area Adult Glioma Study
def: "A case-control study of adult glioma run by the University of California, San Francisco since 1991, whose cases are adults with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma: population-based cases living in six San Francisco Bay Area counties (Alameda, Contra Costa, Marin, San Francisco, San Mateo and Santa Clara), identified through the regional cancer registry's rapid case ascertainment, and, from 2002, clinic-based cases recruited at the UCSF Neuro-oncology Clinic. Its controls were found by random-digit dialling in the same counties and frequency-matched to cases on age, sex and ethnicity, and later drawn from UCSF clinics; it studies environmental, immunological and genetic risk factors for glioma." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28346443", IAO:0000119="PMID:16749939"}
