[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001482
name: Aichi Colorectal Cancer Study
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at Aichi Cancer Center in Nagoya, Japan, part of the centre's Hospital-based Epidemiologic Research Program (HERPACC): its first collection (Aichi-1) took colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls, frequency-matched on age and sex, from the first-visit outpatients enrolled in HERPACC-II in 2000–2005, and its second (Aichi-2) recruited further cases and matched controls at the same hospital. Both collections were genotyped for the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf"}
