[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001484
name: Acute Myocardial Infarction Gene Study
def: "A German case-control study of myocardial infarction whose cases were enrolled in 2004–2006 in a prospective multicentre registry at 4 heart centres and 6 cardiology departments in North Rhine-Westphalia, Lower Saxony and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania: consecutive men younger than 65 admitted with ST- or non-ST-segment elevation acute myocardial infarction, all of whom underwent cardiac catheterisation and revascularisation. Its controls are participants of the population-based Dortmund Health Study, and the case-control sample served as a replication study for the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium's genome-wide association study of early-onset myocardial infarction." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.327/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng327_MOESM15_ESM.pdf"}
