[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001497
name: Arsenic Health Risk Assessment and Molecular Epidemiology
def: "A hospital-based case–control study of basal cell carcinoma of the skin and of bladder and kidney cancers in relation to low-level inorganic arsenic in drinking water, funded by the European Commission and conducted in 2002–2004 in counties of Hungary, Romania and Slovakia with arsenic in groundwater. Its incident cases, and its controls drawn from general surgery, orthopaedic and trauma in-patients of hospitals across the same areas and frequency matched to the cases by age, sex and county, all aged 30–79, were assessed for lifetime arsenic exposure, urinary arsenic metabolites and genetic susceptibility." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20401490", IAO:0000119="PMID:22436128", IAO:0000119="PMID:21131975"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
