[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001512
name: British Columbia Non-Hodgkin Lymphoma study
def: "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in British Columbia, Canada, which invited residents of Greater Vancouver and Greater Victoria aged 20–79 with non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from March 2000 to February 2004, identified through the BC Cancer Registry (excluding HIV-positive and post-transplant cases), together with population controls from the Client Registry of the British Columbia Ministry of Health frequency-matched to the cases on sex, age and area of residence, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26956414", IAO:0000119="PMID:17722095", IAO:0000119="PMID:19917125"}
