[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001517
name: Barry Caerphilly Growth Study
def: "A cohort of children born consecutively from March 1972 to October 1974 in the towns of Barry and Caerphilly, South Wales, whose mothers were recruited early in pregnancy through general practitioners into a randomised controlled trial, set up in 1972 by the Medical Research Council Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) and the Welsh National School of Medicine in Cardiff, of milk tokens for pregnant women and their children up to five years of age, with the children examined by trained nurses at intervals from birth to five years. The children who completed the trial were traced and re-examined at 23–27 years of age in 1997–1999 to study how birth size, infant feeding, early growth and childhood illness relate to adult blood pressure, adiposity, insulin resistance, haemostatic factors and lung function." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:12791629", IAO:0000119="PMID:17921364", IAO:0000119="PMID:22479550", IAO:0000119="PMID:23790346", IAO:0000119="PMID:7030223"}
synonym: "Barry Caerphilly Growth study" RELATED []
synonym: "Barry-Caerphilly Growth Study" RELATED []
synonym: "BCG" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
