[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001521
name: Belfast Elderly Longitudinal Free-living Ageing Study
def: "A longitudinal study of ageing by the Belfast Longevity Group of Queen's University Belfast, Northern Ireland, of 'elite' octogenarians and nonagenarians, and some centenarians: community-living, apparently well, independently mobile and mentally competent people recruited through their general practitioners in the Greater Belfast area and seen at home by a research nurse, who took their medical history, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and blood samples for DNA and laboratory tests, with nutrition and lifestyle questionnaires, to study the immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors of healthy ageing and longevity." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20507630", IAO:0000119="PMID:20388089", IAO:0000119="PMID:19496022", IAO:0000119="PMID:25773008"}
