[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001523
name: Boston Early-Onset COPD Study
def: "A family study begun in 1994 at Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston, to find genetic determinants of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease other than alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, which enrols extended pedigrees, mainly in New England, ascertained through probands with severe COPD (FEV1 at most 40% predicted) before age 53 and without severe alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, recruited from lung transplant and general pulmonary clinics, together with their first- and second-degree relatives aged 10 years or older." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1", IAO:0000119="PMID:15539711"}
