[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001524
name: Bangladesh Vitamin E and Selenium Trial
def: "A population-based, 2×2 factorial, double-blind randomised controlled chemoprevention trial in Bangladesh that enrolled adults with manifest arsenical skin lesions from the Narayanganj, Comilla, Noakhali and Chandpur districts, through field offices in Araihazar and Matlab, between April 2006 and August 2009, and gave them vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol), selenium (L-selenomethionine), both or placebo for six years to test the prevention of non-melanoma skin cancer, with all-cause and cancer mortality, diabetes and oxidative stress biomarkers as secondary endpoints." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23590571"}
synonym: "BEST" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
instance_of: coho:COHO_0000000 ! cohort
