[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001527
name: Brains for Dementia Research
def: "A longitudinal brain-donation cohort in the United Kingdom, established in 2008 with funding from Alzheimer's Research UK and the Alzheimer's Society, of volunteers with dementia and volunteers without cognitive impairment (the latter aged 65 or over, apart from spouses or partners of participants with dementia), recruited through a network of six dementia research centres (King's College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and their university brain banks, who undergo standardised clinical and psychometric assessments during life and have consented to donate their brains for dementia research after death." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30452415"}
synonym: "BDR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "BfDR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
