[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001533
name: Biological pathways of risk and resilience in Syrian refugee children
def: "A longitudinal cohort of Syrian refugee children aged 8–16 and their primary caregivers, from families who had fled the war in Syria within the previous four years and were living in informal tented settlements in the West and Central Beqaa regions of Lebanon, recruited by purposive cluster sampling from October 2017 to January 2018 and followed up once a year later, with interviews of children and caregivers and children's saliva (for genotyping and DNA methylation) and hair (for cortisol, DHEA and testosterone), to study how psychosocial and biological factors shape resilience and mental health problems; it was funded by the US National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and sponsored by Queen Mary University of London." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37933522", IAO:0000119="PMID:35041012"}
synonym: "Biological Pathways of Risk and Resilience in Syrian Refugee Children" RELATED []
synonym: "BIOPATH" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
