[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001534
name: Biological Determinants of Peritoneal Dialysis
def: "An international observational cohort study, led from the University of Washington, of adults with kidney failure treated with peritoneal dialysis who had a peritoneal equilibration test soon after starting it, set up to find common genetic variants that influence peritoneal solute transfer rate and ultrafiltration. Participants were enrolled prospectively at centres in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States from 2013 to 2018, and DNA and clinical data were added from earlier peritoneal dialysis studies in the United Kingdom (PD-CRAFT), Belgium, Sweden and Hong Kong." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02694068", IAO:0000119="PMID:34197840", IAO:0000119="PMID:40669005"}
synonym: "Bio-PD" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Biological Determinants of PD" RELATED []
synonym: "Biological Determinants of Peritoneal Dialysis (Bio-PD) study" RELATED []
