[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001535
name: A systems BIOlogy Study to TAilored Treatment in Chronic Heart Failure
def: "A multicentre, prospective, observational European study of adults with new-onset or worsening heart failure who were treated with loop diuretics but received no more than half the target doses of ACE inhibitors or angiotensin receptor blockers and/or beta-blockers, and whose physicians intended to start or up-titrate these drugs. Its index cohort was enrolled at 69 centres in 11 European countries between December 2010 and December 2012 and its validation cohort at six centres in Scotland between October 2010 and April 2014; funded by the European Commission's Seventh Framework Programme, it combined clinical data, biomarkers, genome-wide genotyping and proteomics to find patient profiles that predict response to guideline-recommended therapy." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:32825781", IAO:0000119="PMID:33998162", IAO:0000119="PMID:27126231", IAO:0000119="PMID:32002631", IAO:0000119="PMID:31919934"}
