[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001542
name: Bonn-Mannheim MDD study
def: "A German case-control study of major depressive disorder whose cases were consecutive admissions with a DSM-IV lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder to the psychiatric inpatient units of the University of Bonn and of the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, diagnosed by best-estimate consensus from a structured interview (SCID-I or SADS), medical records and family history and excluding bipolar disorder, non-affective psychosis and substance-related depression, and whose controls came from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the cohorts of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's major depressive disorder working group (cohort code boma)." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:29700475", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:32231276", IAO:0000119="PMID:22472876"}
synonym: "BOMA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
