[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001543
name: BOMA-Bipolar Study
def: "A German case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder, from the University of Bonn and the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, whose cases, nearly all with bipolar I disorder diagnosed by DSM-IV best-estimate consensus from structured interviews (SADS-L or SCID), were recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatric inpatient units, and whose controls were drawn from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's bipolar disorder working group." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21353194", IAO:0000119="PMID:21926972"}
