[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001544
name: Genetic determinants of COVID-19 complications in the Brazilian population
def: "A genetic study of COVID-19 severity in Brazil, based at the University of São Paulo Medical School, which enrolled people infected with SARS-CoV-2 in the São Paulo metropolitan area: patients hospitalised with COVID-19 at the Instituto do Coração (InCor) and the Instituto Central do Hospital das Clínicas, and people with a previous infection who were not hospitalised, found through serological surveys or SARS-CoV-2 PCR testing of health professionals and the general population. DNA came from blood samples already taken for clinical tests or serology, with questionnaire or hospital-record data; it was designed to identify genetic risk factors for COVID-19 severity in the Brazilian population and contributes to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:34237774", IAO:0000119="https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:35368071"}
