[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001545
name: Biologics in Rheumatoid Arthritis Genetics and Genomics Study Syndicate
def: "A multicentre observational study of patients with rheumatoid arthritis treated with biologic drugs at rheumatology centres across the United Kingdom, which collects their blood samples for DNA, RNA and cellular studies together with clinical, laboratory and adherence data, to study genetic and other predictors of response to biologic therapy. Its first patients, starting anti-TNF therapy, were identified through the British Society for Rheumatology Biologics Register; from November 2008 patients were recruited before starting a biologic and followed up prospectively for 12 months." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25213131", IAO:0000119="PMID:40567118", IAO:0000119="PMID:23039402", IAO:0000119="PMID:30166627"}
synonym: "BRAGGSS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
