[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001550
name: Brisbane Twin Nevus Study
def: "A study of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) in Brisbane, Australia, that from 1992 to 2016 examined annual new samples of 12-year-old twins from south-east Queensland, with their siblings nearest in age, counting their naevi and recording their sun behaviour, and re-examined them two years later; set up to investigate genetic factors in naevus development and other risk factors for melanoma, it also includes the twins' parents and is the twin mole study of the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28764680", IAO:0000119="PMID:41807453", IAO:0000119="PMID:40576277", IAO:0000119="PMID:24949998"}
synonym: "Brisbane Twin Naevus Study" RELATED []
synonym: "BTNS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "TWin Mole study" RELATED []
