[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001559
name: Calcium Intake Fracture Outcome Study
def: "A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38477757", IAO:0000119="PMID:41346785"}
