[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001560
name: CALEX-family study
def: "A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:19171028", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24358145", IAO:0000119="PMID:26439744", IAO:0000119="PMID:25279460"}
