[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001562
name: Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital Study
def: "A lung cancer case–control study of ethnic Han Chinese, carried out from 1997 to 2008, in which cases were recruited from Beijing and surrounding provinces at the Cancer Hospital of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences in Beijing, China, and cancer-free controls from the same region and period were drawn from a community nutritional survey, to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer; its never-smoking women take part in the genome-wide association studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20700438", IAO:0000119="PMID:23143601"}
