[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001565
name: Canadian Asthma Primary Prevention Study
def: "A prenatally randomised controlled trial, begun in 1995 at university hospital-based centres in Vancouver and Winnipeg, Canada, of infants at high risk of asthma (with at least one first-degree relative with asthma or two with other IgE-mediated allergic diseases) identified before birth, whose families were assigned either to a multifaceted intervention in the first year of life (avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergens and environmental tobacco smoke, encouragement of breastfeeding with partially hydrolysed formula supplementation, and delayed introduction of solid foods) or to a control group, and whose children were followed as a birth cohort with paediatric allergist assessments to age 15, to test the primary prevention of asthma and allergy." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:10891016", IAO:0000119="PMID:15100668", IAO:0000119="PMID:19566956", IAO:0000119="PMID:35686384"}
synonym: "Canadian Childhood Cohorts: Canadian Asthma Primary Prevention Study" RELATED []
synonym: "CAPPS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
