[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001567
name: Cáncer de Pulmón en Asturias
def: "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28604730", IAO:0000119="PMID:28819433", IAO:0000119="PMID:23013535"}
