[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001568
name: Collaborative Atorvastatin Diabetes Study
def: "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of atorvastatin 10 mg daily for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease in men and women aged 40–75 with type 2 diabetes, no history of cardiovascular disease, LDL cholesterol of 4.14 mmol/l or less and at least one further risk factor (retinopathy, albuminuria, current smoking or hypertension), who were randomised between November 1997 and June 2001 at centres in the United Kingdom and Ireland. It was run as a collaboration of Diabetes UK, the NHS Research and Development Directorate and Pfizer UK, and was stopped early when its prespecified efficacy criterion was met." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25899452", IAO:0000119="PMID:11918622", IAO:0000119="PMID:15325833"}
synonym: "CARDS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
