[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001571
name: Carotene and Retinol Efficacy Trial
def: "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily beta-carotene (30 mg) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU) for the primary prevention of lung cancer in people at high risk of it, namely male and female heavy smokers and former smokers and asbestos-exposed men, recruited at centres in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Irvine, Baltimore and New Haven, United States, in a pilot phase from 1985 and an efficacy phase from 1989. The intervention was stopped in January 1996, 21 months early, because it increased lung cancer incidence and mortality; participants were followed through 2005, and the serum, plasma, whole blood and lung tissue collected during the trial form the CARET Biorepository." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:8137335", IAO:0000119="PMID:8602180", IAO:0000119="PMID:15572756", IAO:0000119="PMID:1844268", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
