[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001575
name: Cambridgeshire Case-Control Study
def: "A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:12045211", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:14551916", IAO:0000119="PMID:22039354"}
