[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001583
name: Central and Eastern European Renal Cell Carcinoma Study
def: "A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC's lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies. Participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region's high kidney cancer rates." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:19034282", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19753122", IAO:0000119="PMID:22113997", IAO:0000119="PMID:21540858"}
