[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001593
name: Copenhagen Ischemic Heart Disease Study
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of ischaemic heart disease in Denmark whose cases are patients from the greater Copenhagen area referred for coronary angiography to Copenhagen University Hospital from 1991 onwards, with ischaemic heart disease documented by coronary stenosis or atherosclerosis on angiography, a positive exercise electrocardiogram or myocardial infarction, and whose controls without ischaemic heart disease are sampled from the Copenhagen General Population Study; with the Copenhagen City Heart Study and the Copenhagen General Population Study it is used in genetic and Mendelian randomization studies of cardiovascular disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22563304", IAO:0000119="PMID:22698489", IAO:0000119="PMID:25406188"}
