[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001595
name: Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism Study
def: "A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00662571", IAO:0000119="PMID:35752286", IAO:0000119="PMID:25290263"}
