[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001601
name: An Epidemiological Study of Periodontal Disease and Diabetes: Cytokine Genes and Inflammation Factors
def: "A cross-sectional genetic and epidemiological study of periodontal disease and caries in Gullah African Americans with type 2 diabetes from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina. The Medical University of South Carolina ran it as the first project funded through its NIH Center of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE) for Oral Health. Participants were recruited in 2004–2006 from Project SuGAR, community health fairs and churches, were examined at MUSC in Charleston or at four off-site centres and gave blood for DNA, so that periodontal disease could be related to diabetes control, cytokine genes and inflammation. Their data form one of the studies of the Sea Islands Genetics Network." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25364473", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19563285", IAO:0000119="PMID:34008864", IAO:0000119="PMID:23966867"}
synonym: "Center of Biomedical Research Excellence for Oral Health pilot project" RELATED []
synonym: "COBRE" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "COBRE for Oral Health" RELATED []
synonym: "COBRE for Oral Health Study" RELATED []
