[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001603
name: Colorectal Cancer Genetic Susceptibility Study
def: "A Scotland-wide study run from Edinburgh from 1999 that approached patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at age 55 or younger. Research nurses visited them at home to take a family pedigree, give genetic counselling and take blood for genetic testing, to evaluate a strategy for finding families with hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer and to study inherited susceptibility to colorectal cancer. Population controls matched by age, sex and area of residence were recruited through the Scottish NHS. Its early-onset cases and controls formed the Scotland1 genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:18372901", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:15931596", IAO:0000119="PMID:22634755", IAO:0000119="PMID:19011631", IAO:0000119="PMID:14562005"}
synonym: "COGS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
