[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001607
name: Consortium for the Investigation of Renal Malignancies
def: "A kidney cancer study run by Cancer Council Victoria with QIMR Berghofer, the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries and hospitals and familial cancer clinics across Australia; its Queensland arm is called the CARE Study. Its population-based case–control family component recruited, through the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries, people diagnosed in 2009–2015, at age 18–74, with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma, with siblings and partners of cases as controls. The study also enrolled people with a strong family history of kidney cancer or a hereditary kidney cancer syndrome. Participants completed questionnaires on health, lifestyle and family and medical history and gave blood, so that lifestyle, environmental and genetic causes of kidney cancer could be investigated." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:39272843", IAO:0000119="PMID:34562747", IAO:0000119="https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html", IAO:0000119="PMID:28598434"}
