[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001609
name: Duke Neurogenetics Study
def: "A study of young adult university students aged 18–22, most of them Duke University undergraduates recruited on campus in Durham, North Carolina, United States, who between 2010 and 2016 completed self-report and behavioural measures, functional and structural brain MRI and genotyping in Duke University's Laboratory of NeuroGenetics. People with psychiatric diagnoses were not excluded, as the study set out to relate variation in behaviour, brain and genes to risk for psychopathology." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28887539", IAO:0000119="PMID:31677585", IAO:0000119="PMID:31629936", IAO:0000119="PMID:38711811"}
