[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001615
name: Assessment of Risk for Colorectal Tumors in Canada
def: "A colorectal cancer genomics project in Ontario, Canada (the ARCTIC Genome Project), hosted by Cancer Care Ontario and funded by Genome Canada through the Ontario Genomics Institute and other agencies, whose case-control sample consists of participants of the Ontario Familial Colorectal Cancer Registry: people aged 20–74 with colorectal cancer diagnosed in 1997–2000 and identified through the population-based Ontario Cancer Registry, and population controls randomly selected and frequency-matched to them by sex and five-year age group. They were genotyped genome-wide to find common variants associated with colorectal cancer, and the sample has since been used for risk-prediction and DNA methylation studies." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:27142380", IAO:0000119="PMID:17618283", IAO:0000119="PMID:20437058"}
