[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001617
name: Bipolar Disorder Research Network
def: "A cohort of adults of European ancestry with bipolar disorder (bipolar I or II disorder, schizoaffective disorder of bipolar type or bipolar disorder not otherwise specified) recruited from across the United Kingdom by the Bipolar Disorder Research Network, an ongoing research programme run from Cardiff and Worcester, systematically through NHS community mental health teams and lithium clinics and non-systematically through media advertising and patient charities such as Bipolar UK. Participants are interviewed by trained psychologists and psychiatrists with the Schedules for Clinical Assessment in Neuropsychiatry and their case notes reviewed, to study the genetic and environmental causes of bipolar and related mood disorders." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:39537796", IAO:0000119="PMID:34002096", IAO:0000119="PMID:38355785"}
