[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001620
name: Cohort of Norway
def: "A Norwegian multipurpose collection of health data and blood samples pooled from ten regional population-based health surveys conducted in 1994–2003, among them the fourth and fifth surveys of the Tromsø Study, the second Nord-Trøndelag Health Study (HUNT II), the Hordaland Health Study, the Oslo Health Study, the Oppland and Hedmark Health Study and the Troms and Finnmark Health Study. Participants, invited through the Population Registry of Norway, answered about 50 common core questions, had standardised examinations and gave non-fasting blood samples, and consented to linkage with national health registries; the collaboration is run by the Norwegian Institute of Public Health with the universities of Bergen, Oslo, Tromsø and Trondheim." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17984119"}
