[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001626
name: COloRectal tumour Gene Identification study
def: "A UK family study that since 1999 has recruited, through Clinical Genetics Departments throughout the United Kingdom, members of families with colorectal tumours who developed colorectal cancer by age 80 or significant colorectal adenomas (three or more, with severe dysplasia or villous histology, or presenting before age 45; adenoma-only cases having a first- or second-degree relative with colorectal cancer), with their unaffected spouses or partners as controls, to identify genes that predispose to colorectal tumours. Its cases and controls formed the first UK genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer (UK1) and later sample sets." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20972440", IAO:0000119="PMID:31089142", IAO:0000119="PMID:23263490", IAO:0000119="PMID:17618284"}
