[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001631
name: Canadian Pharmacogenomics Network for Drug Safety
def: "A pan-Canadian collection of children and adults treated with drugs of interest who have been enrolled since 2005 by trained surveillance clinicians at major Canadian hospitals (first paediatric hospitals, as the Genotype-specific Approaches to Therapy in Childhood network), either as cases of serious adverse drug reactions, such as anthracycline-induced cardiotoxicity or cisplatin-induced hearing loss, or as drug-tolerant controls, and whose clinical data and biological samples are collected for genetic association studies to find genomic predictors of adverse drug reactions. The network is based at the University of British Columbia in Vancouver." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:30452777", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:31083486", IAO:0000119="PMID:20578893", IAO:0000119="PMID:19507171", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4610716/unicode"}
