[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001632
name: Hong Kong Cardiovascular Risk Factor Prevalence Study
def: "A prospective population-based cohort of Hong Kong Chinese adults aged 25–74, recruited in 1995–1996 through randomly generated telephone numbers from the general population of Hong Kong for a baseline survey of the prevalence of cardiovascular risk factors (CRISPS-1), with a comprehensive assessment including a 75-g oral glucose tolerance test, and re-examined with similar protocols in 2000–2004, 2005–2008, 2010–2012 and 2016–2018 (CRISPS-2 to CRISPS-5) to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors such as diabetes and hypertension." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:36335348", IAO:0000119="PMID:38030128", IAO:0000119="PMID:41662368", IAO:0000119="PMID:9406673"}
synonym: "CRISPS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
