[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001638
name: Chennai Urban Rural Epidemiology Study
def: "A population-based epidemiological study of diabetes and its complications in adults aged 20 years or more in Chennai, southern India, run by the Madras Diabetes Research Foundation. A representative sample of the city's residents, from wards chosen by systematic random sampling, was screened for diabetes in a door-to-door survey in 2001–2003; everyone found to have diabetes and every tenth participant then underwent detailed anthropometric, biochemical and complication studies, and they were followed up in 2012–2014." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29985959", IAO:0000119="PMID:14710970"}
synonym: "CURES" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
