[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001640
name: CVPath Institute Sudden Cardiac Death registry
def: "An autopsy registry of people who died suddenly and unexpectedly, whose hearts have been referred since the mid-1990s to CVPath Institute in Gaithersburg, Maryland, by the Office of the Chief Medical Examiner of the State of Maryland through an ongoing cardiovascular pathology consultation service. The cause of death is determined by detailed histopathological examination of the heart and coronary arteries, and DNA extracted from the archived tissue is used to study the genetics of sudden cardiac death and of coronary plaque." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37916415", IAO:0000119="PMID:34039022", IAO:0000119="PMID:34076677"}
