[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001642
name: Czech post-MONICA study
def: "A series of independent cross-sectional surveys of cardiovascular risk factors in the Czech Republic that continued the country's WHO MONICA Project surveys: random 1% samples of residents aged 25–64 years, stratified by age and sex and drawn from health insurance registers, were examined in the same districts in 1997/98, 2000/01, 2007/08 and 2016/17 by investigators in Prague (the Institute for Clinical and Experimental Medicine, and Charles University and Thomayer Hospital). DNA from its participants has also served as general-population controls in genetic studies." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:34226943", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38252350", IAO:0000119="PMID:32392239"}
