[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001643
name: Dutch Asthma GWAS
def: "A genome-wide association sample of asthma from the north of the Netherlands, assembled by the Dutch Asthma Genetics Consortium in two phases that were genotyped separately and meta-analysed: a family-based phase whose asthmatic cases came from a trio and family study, with non-asthmatic spouses or the untransmitted alleles of the trios as controls, and a case–control phase whose asthmatics came from earlier clinical and genetic studies of the investigators' research institute, with controls from COPACETIC, a population-based lung cancer screening study of male smokers. Cases had a physician's diagnosis of asthma, asthma symptoms and bronchial hyperresponsiveness; controls had no asthma, COPD or significant airway obstruction." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29273806"}
synonym: "DAG" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Dutch Asthma GWAS study" RELATED []
