[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001645
name: The Danish study of Functional Disorders
def: "A Danish population-based cohort of men and women aged 18 to 76, drawn at random from the national registers among people born in Denmark and living in the western part of greater Copenhagen and examined at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health, Glostrup, from 2011 to 2015, set up to study the epidemiology of functional somatic syndromes (such as fibromyalgia, irritable bowel syndrome and chronic fatigue syndrome) and bodily distress syndrome. It merges a follow-up examination of the Health2006 cohort (DanFunD part one, 2011-2012) with a new random sample examined from 2012 to 2015 (DanFunD part two)." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28275316"}
