[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001668
name: Drug-Induced Liver Injury Network Prospective Study
def: "The prospective registry study of the US Drug-Induced Liver Injury Network (DILIN), which the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases set up in 2003. Since September 2004 it has enrolled children aged 2 or over and adults referred to the network's clinical sites within 6 months of a suspected liver injury caused by a prescription or over-the-counter drug or a herbal or dietary supplement. Causality is adjudicated by expert review, clinical data and blood (DNA), serum and some tissue samples are collected, and confirmed cases are followed for at least 6 months, in order to study the clinical, genetic, environmental and immunological risk factors and the outcomes of drug-induced liver injury." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19132805", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00345930"}
synonym: "A Multi-Center, Longitudinal Study of Drug-and CAM-Induced Liver Injury" RELATED []
