[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001672
name: obsolete Department of Neurology, Medical University of Vienna
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. DNMUV is the PGS Catalog's id for the Department of Neurology of the Medical University of Vienna (Austria), a hospital department, and the Catalog records no released score or sample set that uses it, so no study sample can be identified behind it. The papers found by name each describe a different unnamed set of the department's patients (E270.1, E270.4, E270.7, E270.10, E270.13; abstracts of PMID:23841974, 25861769, 29987508, 36630660, 34711480). No COHO term matches; the review's MUV ('Medical University of Vienna', COHO:0002100, placeholder) is the parent institution, a CIMBA site label, and not the same thing. Reconsider if a released PGS score ever cites DNMUV. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001673
name: Dutch Renal Cell Cancer Study
def: "A case–control study of renal cell carcinoma in the region of Nijmegen, the Netherlands, run by Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Centre with the Comprehensive Cancer Centre East, whose cases of European descent form a hospital-based series (patients of the hospital's outpatient urology clinic who had given blood and lifestyle data from 1999 onwards for studies of gene–environment interactions in urological disease and were found through the cancer registry to have renal cell carcinoma) and a population-based series recruited in 2009 through the regional cancer registry (patients diagnosed in 1995–2008 before the age of 75). Its controls are participants of the population-based Nijmegen Biomedical Study." [] {IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21131975"}
