[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001678
name: European Collaborative Study
def: "A European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma that genotyped, at the Centre National de Génotypage in France, cases from five European Hodgkin lymphoma studies (the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin's Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study) and compared them with generic controls chosen by country from earlier genome-wide association studies of other cancers in populations of European ancestry, among them ARCAGE, the IARC Central Europe Study, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and the Wellcome Trust Case–Control Consortium. It was the European discovery sample of the 2014 Hodgkin lymphoma GWAS meta-analysis with the University of Southern California and University of Chicago GWAS." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:22286212", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24920014"}
synonym: "ECS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "European Collaborative GWAS" RELATED []
