[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001679
name: Etude Cas-Témoins de l'Infarctus du Myocarde
def: "A multicentre case-control study of myocardial infarction based on the WHO MONICA centres of Belfast (Northern Ireland) and Lille, Strasbourg and Toulouse (France), set up to investigate why coronary heart disease is more than three times as common in middle-aged men in Northern Ireland as in France. Between 1988 and 1991 it recruited men aged 25–64 who had had a myocardial infarction, examined 3 to 9 months after the event, and control men sampled from the general population. Its cases and controls have been used in many candidate-gene studies of myocardial infarction and lipids, and an extension study later recruited men and women in the MONICA areas of Belfast and Glasgow." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:7789377", IAO:0000119="PMID:8633596", IAO:0000119="PMID:1534257", IAO:0000119="PMID:11040019", IAO:0000119="PMID:12081984"}
