[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001684
name: Emory Genebank Study
def: "A study of patients undergoing cardiac catheterization at Emory University hospitals, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia, United States, designed to investigate the relationship of biochemical and genetic factors with coronary artery disease; patients with angiographic coronary artery disease or a history of myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation serve as cases and those without coronary artery disease on catheterization as controls in genetic studies." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21239051", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21270820"}
