[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001687
name: European Male Ageing Study
def: "A multicentre prospective population-based cohort of men aged 40–79 years recruited from population registers in eight European centres (Florence, Leuven, Lodz, Malmö, Manchester, Santiago de Compostela, Szeged and Tartu) with an age-stratified sample at each centre, who completed a detailed questionnaire on personal and medical history, lifestyle and sexual function, designed to examine the prevalence, incidence and geographical distribution of gender-specific and general symptoms of ageing in men and their endocrine, genetic and psychosocial predictors, particularly age-related changes in hormone levels." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18653627", IAO:0000119="PMID:18328041"}
