[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001694
name: EPICOLON
def: "A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20638935", IAO:0000119="PMID:22294762", IAO:0000119="PMID:30510241"}
