[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001708
name: Essen Obesity Study
def: "A German cross-sectional study of early-onset extreme obesity, made up of a case-control study of extremely obese children and adolescents recruited in hospitals specialised in the inpatient treatment of extreme obesity, with healthy lean controls ascertained at the University of Marburg, and a nuclear family study of obese children and adolescents ascertained in the same way together with both their biological parents (the Essen Obesity Trios), whose genotypes have been used in genome-wide association studies of obesity and body mass index." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18159244", IAO:0000119="https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:18454148"}
