[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001717
name: French-Canadian Family Study on Factor V Leiden Thrombophilia
def: "A family study of five extended French-Canadian pedigrees, identified between 2005 and 2006 at the Thrombosis Clinic of the Ottawa Hospital, Canada, through single probands with objectively diagnosed idiopathic venous thromboembolism who carried the factor V Leiden mutation, whose consenting relatives were genotyped genome-wide and measured for plasma haemostatic factors." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:28894120", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21810271", IAO:0000119="PMID:27490645", IAO:0000119="PMID:25265411"}
