relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/France {xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3247254/fullTextXML", comment="Nuclear families, defined as family groups consisting of a father and/or mother and their children who share living quarters, were drawn from the Fleurbaix-Laventie Ville-Santé II (FLVS II) study, a prospective study (1999–2001) aimed at identifying determinants of adiposity and its changes over time in families living in two small towns in Northern France, Fleurbaix and Laventie [16], [17]."}
