[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001749
name: Genetic Association Information Network
def: "A public-private partnership of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health that, through a series of collaborative genome-wide association studies, genotyped samples from case-control studies of bipolar disorder, diabetic nephropathy, major depressive disorder, psoriasis and schizophrenia and a trio study of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, and made the resulting individual genotype and phenotype data available to researchers through dbGaP." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:17898773", IAO:0000119="PMID:17728769", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19065144"}
