[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001752
name: GAIN Major Depressive Disorder Study
def: "A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19065144", IAO:0000119="PMID:18197199"}
