[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001756
name: Genetic Architecture of Smoking and Smoking Cessation
def: "A genome-wide association study of the Gene Environment Association Studies initiative (GENEVA), deposited in dbGaP as phs000404, that genotyped nicotine-dependent smokers and non-dependent smoking controls from two projects, the Collaborative Genetic Study of Nicotine Dependence (recruited in Detroit and St. Louis) and the University of Wisconsin Transdisciplinary Tobacco Use Research Center smoking cessation trials (recruited in Madison and Milwaukee, Wisconsin), with harmonised measures, to identify genetic variants that contribute to nicotine dependence, related smoking behaviours and smoking cessation." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:31033776", IAO:0000119="https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs000404/phs000404.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs000404.v1.p1.xml"}
synonym: "GASSC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "The Genetic Architecture of Smoking and Smoking Cessation" RELATED []
