id: coho:COHO_0001760
name: CBDB/NIMH Genetic Study of Schizophrenia
def: "A family study of schizophrenia in the intramural research programme of the US National Institute of Mental Health, run by its Clinical Brain Disorders Branch and Genes, Cognition and Psychosis Program, that recruited patients with schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, their unaffected full siblings and healthy volunteers from local and national sources and studied them with cognitive testing, brain imaging and genotyping to identify intermediate phenotypes and risk genes for schizophrenia." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17689500", IAO:0000119="PMID:11381111", IAO:0000119="PMID:25951819"}
