[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001763
name: obsolete Genomics Collaborative Initiative
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. GCI is Genomics Collaborative, Inc., a company that held a DNA repository and supplied case-control sets to other researchers; the rheumatoid arthritis papers' 'Genomics Collaborative Initiative' is a misreading of its name. A company, not a cohort. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001764
name: Guangdong Study
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in the Guangdong area of China, whose cases are ethnic Chinese in-patients with incident, histologically confirmed primary lung cancer of any histological type diagnosed at the Guangdong Lung Cancer Institute and Guangdong General Hospital, and whose controls are healthy, cancer-free patients from the health examination clinics of the same hospitals; one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia genotyped for its genome-wide association study of lung cancer in never-smoking women." [] {IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23143601"}
