[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001765
name: Gene-Environment Interaction in Prostate Cancer Study
def: "A case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Henry Ford Health System in Detroit, Michigan, United States, which enrolled men of Caucasian or African American race younger than 75 years with adenocarcinoma of the prostate living in the metropolitan Detroit tri-county area, and controls randomly selected from the same Henry Ford Health System population base, between January 2001 and December 2004, to study gene-environment interaction in prostate cancer risk." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21637779", dcterms:contributor="GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17067754"}
