[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001766
name: Gene-Environment-Development Initiative
def: "A consortium funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse that brought together four existing longitudinal, general-population studies with repeated assessments across childhood, adolescence and young adulthood, the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development, the Great Smoky Mountains Study and the Caring for Children in the Community study in the United States and the Christchurch Health and Development Study in New Zealand, to identify which genes, environments and developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23461817"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
