[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001770
name: Genetic Epidemiology of Migraine Study
def: "A Dutch population-based study of migraine embedded in the MORGEN project, in which adults aged 20 to 65 randomly selected from two Dutch county population registries (Maastricht and Doetinchem) to take part in a general health survey were screened for headache history, screen-positives were given a detailed headache questionnaire and a random subset a semistructured telephone clinical interview, and migraine was diagnosed by International Headache Society criteria, to study the prevalence, characteristics, cardiovascular risk profile and genetics of migraine." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18676988", IAO:0000119="PMID:10449117", IAO:0000119="PMID:19025553"}
