[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001772
name: Genetic Epidemiology of Metabolic Syndrome Study
def: "A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25164947", IAO:0000119="PMID:15642551", IAO:0000119="PMID:19165155"}
