[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001780
name: GenePD Study
def: "An international multicentre study of the genetics of familial Parkinson's disease, designed for genetic linkage analysis of affected relative pairs, that recruits families with at least two members with Parkinson's disease meeting diagnostic criteria, ascertained through a proband with an affected sibling, parent, offspring or more distant relative, at academic centres and clinics in the United States, Canada, Australia, Germany, Italy, the United Kingdom and Denmark." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18649400", IAO:0000119="PMID:18986508", IAO:0000119="PMID:17408493"}
