[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001795
name: obsolete German BP sample
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. German BP sample is how two 2012 papers name the Bonn/Mannheim bipolar disorder GWAS sample (PMID:22384057, PMID:23092984), which COHO holds as the BOMA-Bipolar Study. Replaced by COHO:0001543 (BOMA-Bipolar Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0001543

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001796
name: German Affected-Sib-Pair Study
def: "A family study of asthma in Germany whose families have at least two children with confirmed clinical asthma, ascertained at multiple centres and phenotyped by trained staff to a common protocol for the German Asthma Genetics Group; its families were used for genome-wide linkage scans of asthma and later as a replication sample in genetic association studies of asthma." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:10333435", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:15634351", IAO:0000119="PMID:11793707", IAO:0000119="PMID:19198610"}
