id: coho:COHO_0001800
name: Groningen Genetics of Atrial Fibrillation Study
def: "A collection of individuals with atrial fibrillation and age- and sex-matched controls, assembled at the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, as a genotype and phenotype repository for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation, whose cases come from three hospital-based atrial fibrillation cohorts (the AF-Risk, Young-AF and Biomarker-AF studies) and whose controls come from the GIPS-III trial and the PREVEND community cohort of Groningen." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
