id: coho:COHO_0001803
name: Glioma International Case-Control Study
def: "A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:26656478", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30482874", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode"}
