[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001810
name: Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma Genes and Environment Study
def: "A case-control genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma in the United States, part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative, which assembled cases and controls from three studies: the clinic-based Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma project of the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, and cases and matched controls from the glaucoma-at-risk cohorts of the Nurses' Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, to find genetic loci and gene–environment interactions for the disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML"}
