[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001817
name: Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study
def: "A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37813622"}
synonym: "GNHS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
