[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001840
name: Heart Attack Risk in Puget Sound
def: "A population-based case-control study of early-onset myocardial infarction in King, Pierce and Snohomish counties, Washington, United States, whose cases were men under 50 and women under 60 with a first myocardial infarction diagnosed between 1991 and 2002, ascertained through medical record review at all acute care facilities in those counties, and whose controls, matched on age and sex and free of cardiovascular disease, were identified by random digit dialling in the same counties; it is one of the six studies of the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21239051", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19198609"}
