[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001846
name: obsolete Hospital Clinico San Carlos
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. HCSC is the Hospital Clínico San Carlos, a university hospital in Madrid, Spain. The PGS Catalog uses the id for two different contributions of that hospital: its breast cancer cases and controls in the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC, COHO:0000020), and its BRCA1/2 mutation carriers in CIMBA (COHO:0000901). In both, the papers name the sample only after the hospital ('HCSC Hospital Clinico San Carlos'; 'Hospital Clinico San Carlos (HCSC)') and describe no study design, recruitment period or study name, so the id is an institution label, as the review decided for the other institution-named CIMBA sites (BIDMC, UPENN, MSKCC, Chicago). If the curator ever mints BCAC or CIMBA site samples, this id would need two terms, one per consortium. No COHO term uses HCSC or the hospital's name. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001847
name: obsolete High Density SNP Association Analysis of Melanoma
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. HDAAM is the dbGaP study 'High Density SNP Association Analysis of Melanoma: Case-Control and Outcomes Investigation' (phs000187), under which the MD Anderson melanoma GWAS deposited its data (PMID:21926416). Replaced by COHO:0000875 (MD Anderson Cancer Center melanoma study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000875

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001848
name: Health2 Study
def: "A population-based cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study (KoGES), set up by the Center for Genome Science of the Korea National Institute of Health, made up of community-based cohorts of adults aged 40–69 in five rural areas of South Korea (Wonju, Pyeongchang, Gangneung, Geumsan and Naju), and later counted as part of the KoGES Cardiovascular Disease Association Study (CAVAS). It served as a replication and case-control sample in Korean genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes, blood pressure, lipids and blood cell traits." [] {IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25705162", IAO:0000119="PMID:33374401", IAO:0000119="PMID:28154504", IAO:0000119="PMID:39050255", IAO:0000119="PMID:25349825"}
