[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001855
name: Hertfordshire Cohort Study
def: "A population-based cohort of men and women born in 1931–1939 in Hertfordshire, United Kingdom, who still lived there in 1998–2004, when they completed a home interview and a clinic visit for a detailed health assessment, and some of whom were followed up in later waves, recruited initially to investigate the relationship between growth in infancy and the risk of adult diseases and since used to study musculoskeletal and general health in older age." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41754086", IAO:0000119="PMID:39751886"}
synonym: "HCS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "HerCS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
