[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001856
name: Health, Risk Factors, Training and Genetics Family Study
def: "A family study, run by a consortium of universities in the United States and Canada, of sedentary white and Black families (both parents and adult offspring aged 17 to 65) who were tested, put through the same 20-week graded aerobic exercise training programme and re-tested, designed to document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic and hormonal responses to regular exercise." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35995766", IAO:0000119="PMID:7674877"}
