[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001858
name: Health Habits and Opinions study
def: "A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia's vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24569950", IAO:0000119="PMID:24860199"}
synonym: "HHO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
instance_of: coho:COHO_0000000 ! cohort
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Northern_America
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_States {xref="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038932/", comment="United States Health Habits and Opinions study (HHO) 1990"}
relationship: coho:isSubCohortOf coho:COHO_0002034 {xref="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038932/", comment="The sample is a follow up of the 1988 MATR study above."}
property_value: coho:numberOfParticipants "4119" xsd:integer {IAO:0000116="twins aged 40-93 who took part in the follow-up survey about two years after the Health and Life Styles questionnaire (1990)", xref="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4031194/", comment="In addition, 4,119 of the twins, comprised of 744 female MZ twin pairs, 421 female DZ twin pairs, 195 male MZ pairs, 93 male DZ pairs, and 339 female-male twin pairs, aged 40–93 (μ=64, σ=7.9), took part in a follow-up two years later."}
property_value: IAO:0000112 "PMID:24860199" xsd:string {dcterms:title="The Influence of Major Life Events on Economic Attitudes in a World of Gene-Environment Interplay.", xref="PMID:24860199", xref="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4031194/", comment="This Health Habits and Opinions study (HHO) assessed many of the same political attitudes in the HLQ."}

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001859
name: obsolete Hussman Institute of Human Genomics
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. HIHG is the Hussman Institute for Human Genomics of the University of Miami (formerly the Miami Institute for Human Genomics). In the PGS Catalog's source paper the id labels the institute's Parkinson's disease GWAS sample, a genotyping set of unrelated cases gathered by the 13 ascertainment centres of the PD Genetics Collaboration and the Udall Parkinson Disease Center of Excellence core, with spouse and friend controls (PMID:20070850, PMC2853717). It is a GWAS sample assembled from those collections under the institute's name, not a collection with a name of its own. If a term is ever wanted, the named collection behind it would be the PD Genetics Collaboration (Scott et al. 2001) or the Udall center's collection, not HIHG. No COHO term or review name matches; the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium (COHO:0001108) and the Ashkenazi Jewish Dataset (COHO:0001283) are separate datasets of the same meta-analysis. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001860
name: Hispanic/Latino Anthropometry Consortium
def: "A consortium of studies and consortia of adults of Hispanic/Latino heritage, or of Native American heritage, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru and the United States, among them the CANDELA consortium, that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results in discovery and replication stages to find and fine-map genetic loci for anthropometric traits such as body mass index, height and waist-to-hip ratio." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35399580"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
synonym: "HISLA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
