[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001861
name: Hannover-Jena Endometrial Cancer Study
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Germany, whose cases were women aged 31–89 recruited at the Friedrich Schiller University of Jena or at Hannover Medical School after a diagnosis of histologically confirmed primary incident endometrial carcinoma between 2004 and 2010, who were interviewed there and gave peripheral blood for DNA, with epidemiological data from questionnaires and tumour stage and histology from pathology and clinical reports. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30093612", IAO:0000119="PMID:27135401"}
synonym: "HJECS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
