[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001864
name: Hong Kong Study
def: "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer among ethnic Chinese in Hong Kong, whose cases were lung cancer patients aged 18 to 80 years who underwent tumour resection at Queen Mary Hospital and Grantham Hospital and whose controls were patients of comparable age with non-cancer diagnoses at Queen Mary Hospital; its never-smoking women were genotyped in the genome-wide association study of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23143601"}
