[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001876
name: Oxford Family Blood Pressure Study
def: "A family cohort of white British nuclear and extended families from Oxford, United Kingdom, recruited from 1993 through a proband with essential hypertension in the upper 5% of the blood pressure distribution, with other family members collected regardless of their blood pressure, for quantitative genetic study of hypertension, left ventricular mass and other cardiovascular risk factors; families were recalled for further cardiovascular phenotyping, including electrocardiography, echocardiography and cardiac magnetic resonance imaging." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:31537879", IAO:0000119="PMID:23372812", IAO:0000119="PMID:30224653"}
synonym: "HTO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Oxford Family Blood Pressure cohort" RELATED []
