[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001878
name: Hebrew University Genetic Resource
def: "A repository of DNA samples from Ashkenazi Jewish people, collected and held at the Hebrew University in Israel, that includes patients with schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder recruited from hospitalised inpatients at seven medical centres in Israel, patients with diabetes and healthy volunteers, among them controls collected through the Israeli Blood Bank; its schizophrenia cases and controls form a case-control sample used in genome-wide association studies of schizophrenia." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:22277159", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21533139", IAO:0000119="PMID:24253340", IAO:0000119="PMID:24943592"}
