id: coho:COHO_0001882
name: HYPERGENES–European Network for Genetic-Epidemiological Studies
def: "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project on the genetics of essential hypertension, coordinated from the University of Milan, that assembled hypertensive cases, normotensive controls and population samples from extensively characterised cohorts in different European regions (northern Europe, continental Italy and Sardinia), among them the FLEMENGHO/EPOGH cohort, the Wandsworth Heart and Stroke Study, the Milano-Sassari cohort and the SOPHIA cohort, for a two-stage genome-wide association study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature11401/MediaObjects/41586_2012_BFnature11401_MOESM14_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
synonym: "European Network for Genetic-Epidemiological Studies" RELATED []
synonym: "HYPERGENES" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Hypergenes" RELATED []
synonym: "Hypergenes - European Network for Genetic-Epidemiological Studies" RELATED []
synonym: "Hypergenes - European Network for Genetic-Epidemological Studies" RELATED []
synonym: "HYPERGENES–European Network for Genetic-Epidemiological Studies: building a method to dissect complex genetic traits, using essential hypertension as a disease model" RELATED []
