id: coho:COHO_0001900
name: Study to investigate the genetics of in situ carcinoma of the ductal subtype
def: "A UK case-control study of genetic predisposition to ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS) of the breast, which between 2007 and 2012 recruited women aged 60 or under with a current or past diagnosis of DCIS, identified from local pathology reports at more than 100 hospitals throughout the United Kingdom, and healthy controls without a family history of breast cancer (often friends or non-blood relatives of cases), with a blood sample and a questionnaire on reproductive, medical and family history and hormone use." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41028956", IAO:0000119="PMID:26884359"}
