[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001901
name: obsolete Institut Català d'Oncologia
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. ICO is the Institut Català d'Oncologia (Catalan Institute of Oncology), a cancer centre in Catalonia, Spain. In the PGS Catalog it labels unnamed site samples: in every CIMBA paper (PMID:28448241, 32665703, 34320204 and the source GWAS PMID:28346442, 29058716) it is the ICO Hereditary Cancer Program's BRCA1/2 pathogenic-variant carriers contributed to CIMBA (COHO:0000901), and in PMID:37321833 it is the ICO's series of Lynch syndrome carriers plus Spanish controls ('Patients were recruited based on the fulfilment of Bethesda or Amsterdam criteria or via an EC and CRC-based LS screening programme (since 2016 at the ICO).'). Neither sample has a study name of its own. This follows the review's decisions for other institution-named CIMBA sites (MSKCC, UPENN, BRICOH, Chicago, FCCC, OUH): not a cohort. Not the HVH, PBCS, kConFab or deCODE terms the automatic matching suggested (those are other CIMBA/BCAC ids in the same tables). The ICO Breast Cancer Cohort (PMID:40282542) is a separate clinical cohort that the PGS Catalog does not record. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

