id: coho:COHO_0001902
name: International Collaborative Study on Hypertension in Blacks
def: "A population-based survey of blood pressure, hypertension and associated risk factors such as obesity among adults of West African origin living in societies at different stages of social and economic development, which examined age-stratified samples at seven sites in Nigeria, Cameroon, Jamaica, St. Lucia, Barbados and metropolitan Chicago in the United States under a standardized protocol with centrally trained field staff; its Nigerian base sample, recruited in Ibadan and Igbo-Ora in Oyo State, later provided the sampling frame for genotyped cohorts." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:8793366", IAO:0000119="PMID:41908051", IAO:0000119="PMID:8581794", IAO:0000119="PMID:9103091"}
synonym: "ICSHIB" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
