relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Iceland {xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4551564/fullTextXML", comment="Patients with confirmed recurrent clinical stone disease were recruited from two sources, the Kidney Stone Prevention Clinic at Landspitali – The National University Hospital of Iceland (LUH) in Reykjavik and the Icelandic Kidney Stone Registry (IKSR) which was established in 2008 in conjunction with a nationwide study on kidney stone disease [2]."}
property_value: IAO:0000112 "PMID:20686651" xsd:string {dcterms:title="Association of variants at UMOD with chronic kidney disease and kidney stones-role of age and comorbid diseases.", xref="PMID:20686651", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2912386/fullTextXML", comment="The Icelandic kidney stone cases consisted of patients with confirmed radiopaque kidney stones from the Icelandic Kidney Stone Disease Registry at LUH."}

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001912
name: obsolete Infanta Leonor University Hospital (Madrid, Spain)
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog's full name for ILUH, 'Infanta Leonor University Hospital (Madrid, Spain)', is wrong: in the CIMBA papers the Catalog curated, ILUH is Iceland's Landspitali University Hospital. ILUH is the PGS Catalog's id for the BRCA1/BRCA2 pathogenic-variant carriers contributed to CIMBA (COHO:0000901) by Landspitali University Hospital in Reykjavik, Iceland (PMID:28448241, 34320204, 32665703, 36203093); the Catalog's expansion 'Infanta Leonor University Hospital (Madrid, Spain)' is an error. The sample has no name of its own beyond the hospital, so, like the other institution-named CIMBA sites the review decided (MSKCC, UPENN, BRICOH, Chicago, FCCC, OUH, and E522 ICO in this batch), it is not a cohort. It is not the deCODE genetics Icelandic cohort (COHO:0000428): CIMBA lists it as a clinic-based site sample of mutation carriers. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001913
name: obsolete Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. IMM labels the Tohoku Medical Megabank cohort data (the Community-Based Cohort and the Birth and Three-Generation Cohort) analysed by the Iwate group in the papers the PGS Catalog records the id in (PMID:39174808, PMID:40695273). Replaced by COHO:0000533 (Tohoku Medical Megabank Project), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000533

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001914
name: Carotid Intima-Media Thickness (IMT) and IMT-Progression as Predictors of Vascular Events in a High-Risk European Population
def: "A multicentre prospective cohort study of European adults aged 54 to 79 years with at least three vascular risk factors but no previous cardiovascular or cerebrovascular events, enrolled at seven centres in Finland, France, Italy, the Netherlands and Sweden and followed for vascular events by visits at 15 and 30 months and a final telephone interview, to assess carotid intima-media thickness and its progression as predictors of vascular events." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:28602434", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19952003"}
