[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001917
name: obsolete French National Cancer Institute
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. INCa is the Institut national du cancer (French National Cancer Institute), France's national cancer agency, which funds, coordinates and publishes cancer data but is not itself a recruited study sample ('The pilot program IMPULSION, launched by the French National Cancer Institute (INCa)...', PMID:41820119, E542.16). The PGS Catalog lists the id among its cohorts but links it to no score or sample set, so there is no paper in which it denotes a sample; nothing names an 'INCa' cohort. Not a cohort. If the Catalog later links it to a sample, it will most likely be an INCa-funded study that should be identified by its own name. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001918
name: obsolete Indiana cohort
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. Indiana cohort is how multi-cohort GWAS (PMID:20541252, PMID:28724990) name the Indiana University sample of premenopausal sister pairs, the Indiana Sisters Study. Replaced by COHO:0000099 (Indiana Sisters Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000099

