[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001920
name: Industrial Cohorts Research Group
def: "A Danish and Dutch occupational research group whose pooled surveys of occupational asthma, drawn from population-based or prospective cohort studies of workers exposed to allergens and irritants (agricultural dust or animals in the Danish SUS study, the Dutch Omega study and the Veterinarian’s Health Study; wheat flour and amylase in the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project; wood dust in the Danish Wood Dust Cohort of furniture workers; isocyanates in Dutch industrial spray painters), provided prevalent asthma cases and industry-, sex- and age-matched controls, as the INDUSTRIAL subgroup of the GABRIEL Consortium, to the genome-wide meta-analysis of asthma of the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29273806"}
synonym: "INDUSTRIAL" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
