[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001924
name: India–Scotland Partnership for Precision Medicine in Diabetes
def: "A research partnership funded by the UK National Institute for Health Research between the University of Dundee, Scotland, and Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre and Madras Diabetes Research Foundation, Chennai, India, that brings together diabetes data resources from India and Scotland, chiefly a cohort of Asian Indians with type 2 diabetes from the electronic medical records of Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre (DMDSC) and the East Scotland Diabetes Cohort (ESDC) of white Europeans with type 2 diabetes from Tayside and Fife, for precision-medicine studies comparing type 2 diabetes in Asian Indians and white Europeans." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7437708/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="PMID:35247066"}
