[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001926
name: Interplay Between Genetic Susceptibility and External Factors
def: "A population-based prospective cohort of the INTERGENE research programme, set up to study the interplay between genetic and environmental risk factors for chronic disease, in which a random sample of adults aged 24 to 77 drawn from the population registers of an urban-rural area of western Sweden (Västra Götaland County, about half of them living in Gothenburg) was examined in 2001-2004 and re-examined in 2014-2016, with follow-up of health outcomes through linkage to the Swedish national registers." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38983451", IAO:0000119="PMID:38809556", IAO:0000119="PMID:41741164"}
