[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001929
name: Lymphoma Specialized Program of Research Excellence Molecular Epidemiology Resource Cohort Study
def: "An observational epidemiology cohort of consecutive patients with newly diagnosed lymphoma (including Hodgkin lymphoma and chronic lymphocytic leukaemia), US residents aged 18 or over enrolled within 9 months of diagnosis at the Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and the University of Iowa in Iowa City from September 2002 to June 2015 as part of the University of Iowa/Mayo Clinic Lymphoma Specialized Program of Research Excellence (SPORE), set up to identify clinical, epidemiological, germline genetic, tumour and treatment factors that affect lymphoma outcomes and survivorship." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29025017"}
