[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001940
name: Italian Gene-Environment Interactions in Lymphoma Etiology
def: "A multicentre case-control study of lymphoma of any subtype carried out in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres (Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia), whose cases are incident lymphoma patients and whose controls, frequency-matched to cases by age and sex, are cancer-free hospital patients in most centres and a random sample of the general population in Cagliari and Nuoro, interviewed about lifetime occupational history and other exposures to study gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33910586"}
