[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001941
name: Jamaican Adolescent Asthma Study
def: "A cross-sectional study of the prevalence of asthma and allergies in Jamaican adolescents whose mothers had been recruited into the Jamaica Perinatal Mortality Survey of 1986, which included all children born in Jamaica in September–October 1986; children from Kingston, St Andrew and St Catherine were contacted at ages 11 and 16 in a child development study and again at 18, and asthma was ascertained with a modified International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) questionnaire validated in the Jamaican population and, for adults followed in clinic since birth, from medical records. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA)." [] {IAO:0000119="https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23554133", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf"}
synonym: "JAAS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
