[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001949
name: Japanese Female Lung Cancer Collaborative Study
def: "A collaborative hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in ethnic Japanese that enrolled patients with no history of cancer who were histologically diagnosed with lung cancer, and age- and sex-matched first-visit outpatients of the same period confirmed to have no cancer or history of neoplasia, at the Aichi Cancer Center Research Institute and the National Cancer Center Hospital; its never-smoking female cases and controls form the Japanese study of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28025329", IAO:0000119="PMID:23143601"}
