[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001950
name: Jerusalem Lipid Research Clinic Study
def: "A population-based cohort study in Jerusalem, Israel, begun in 1976–1979 as a cardiovascular prevalence study that followed the protocols of the North American Lipid Research Clinics prevalence studies, examining full age cohorts of 17-year-old Jewish residents of Jerusalem and many of their parents to describe plasma lipids and lipoproteins; samples of both generations were re-examined in later phases, the young participants at about 30 and 43 years of age in its longitudinal study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:7161042", IAO:0000119="PMID:21220750", IAO:0000119="PMID:26406330", IAO:0000119="PMID:22237065"}
