[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001951
name: Japanese Millennium Genome Project
def: "A Japanese collaborative sample, assembled within the nationally based cooperative Millennium Genome Project for genetic studies of hypertension, that combines seven independent cohorts for studies of cardiovascular diseases and related risk factors: the Ohasama, Shigaraki, Takashima, Suita and Nomura studies, general-population studies of community residents recruited through medical check-ups, and the Yokohama and Matsuyama cohorts of employees of large manufacturing industries." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21909115", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26390057", IAO:0000119="PMID:20921432"}
