[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001952
name: Human genetic determinants of severe malaria in North East Tanzania
def: "A matched case-control study of severe malaria in children aged 3 months to 10 years in Muheza, Tanga region, north-eastern Tanzania, carried out in 2006–2008 by the Joint Malaria Programme (Kilimanjaro Christian Medical Centre, Moshi) with the London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine. Its cases were children admitted to Teule Hospital with severe malaria, recruited within a study of severe febrile illness, and its controls were healthy children from the community individually matched on parental tribal origin, ward of residence and age; its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and used in candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of severe malaria." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29381699", IAO:0000119="PMID:23144702", IAO:0000119="https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/"}
