name: Kawasaki Aging and Wellbeing Project
def: "A prospective longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling residents of Kawasaki City in the Greater Tokyo Area, Japan, aged 85 to 89 and without limitations in basic activities of daily living at baseline, enrolled at hospitals in the city between March 2017 and December 2018, to study the trajectories of functional decline, frailty and cognitive impairment at advanced age and the genetic, biological, behavioural and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify them." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML"}
