[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001957
name: obsolete National Institute of Health launched the Korea Biobank Array project
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: KBA is strictly the name of a genotyping array and project; the sample it denotes is KoGES participants genotyped on it, not a separately recruited cohort. In PMID:32499647 KBA and KARE (Ansan and Ansung Study, COHO:0000530, a KoGES cohort genotyped earlier on another array) appear as separate study groups, so 'KBA' there is the KBA-genotyped part of KoGES; KoGES (COHO:0000411) is still the term it belongs to. If the curator prefers not to attach an array's name to a cohort, the alternative verdict is 'not a cohort' (a genotyping project on KoGES samples). The PGS name is a garbled fragment of the sentence 'The Korea National Institute of Health launched the Korea Biobank Array (KBA) project in 2014' (PMID:36333282). The KBA is the Korean genotyping array used on the KoGES cohorts' samples held at the National Biobank of Korea, and PMID:40778152 calls the sample 'Korean Biobank Array from the Korean Genome and Epidemiology (KoGES) Consortium (KBA)'. So the id denotes KoGES participants genotyped on the KBA: the existing aggregation KoGES (COHO:0000411). Add KBA as an acronym and the array/project names (including the catalog's name) as synonyms; obsolete placeholder COHO:0001957 in favour of COHO:0000411. Replaced by COHO:0000411 (Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000411

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001958
name: Validation Cohort of Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of AD
def: "The independent, nationwide validation cohort of the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer's disease (KBASE), which recruited cognitively normal people and people with subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer's disease dementia at nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016 under the same criteria as KBASE, and followed them annually for three years, to reconfirm biomarkers identified in KBASE and to find risk and prognostic factors for Alzheimer's disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML"}
