[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001966
name: obsolete Kentucky Lung Cancer Research Initiative
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. KLCRI is the Kentucky Lung Cancer Research Initiative, the population-based case-control study of lung cancer in Appalachian Kentucky that the lung cancer OncoArray study table lists as LCRI-DOD (PMID:28604730); a 2019 paper gives the id with the name (PMID:30059977). Replaced by COHO:0001992 (LCRI-DOD), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0001992

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001967
name: obsolete Korean Metabolic Syndrome Research Initiative
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The Korean Metabolic Syndrome Research Initiative is the programme under which the Korean Cancer Prevention Study-II Biobank recruited its health examinees; papers use the two names for the same people (PMID:25113383, PMID:27632197). Replaced by COHO:0000486 (Korean Cancer Prevention Study-II Biobank), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000486

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001968
name: obsolete Korean National Health Insurance
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. Korean National Health Insurance is South Korea's national health insurance programme and its claims database, a data source used by many unrelated studies, not a study sample; no score in the PGS Catalog uses the id. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001969
name: Human genetic determinants of severe malaria in Kumasi, Ghana
def: "A prospective, unmatched case-control study of severe malaria conducted in August 2006 – December 2008 in the Kumasi Metropolitan District, Ashanti Region, Ghana, with ethics approval from Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology. Its cases were children aged 3 months to 12 years with severe malaria admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, its controls were cord-blood samples collected in the same hospital's labour ward, and blood was also taken from the biological parents of cases (family trios); its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25261933", IAO:0000119="https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/"}
synonym: "KNUST" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology" RELATED []
