[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001973
name: Korean Hereditary Breast Cancer Study
def: "A prospective, nationwide study of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer in Korea, established in May 2007, that enrols, at many hospitals across the country, breast cancer patients at high risk of carrying a BRCA1/2 mutation (those with a family history of breast or ovarian cancer, or diagnosed at 40 or younger, with bilateral breast cancer or another BRCA-related primary cancer, or male) and family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, all of whom receive genetic counselling and BRCA testing. Its first phase (2007–2010) estimated the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations, and its second (2010–2013) studied the clinical characteristics, prognosis and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA-related breast cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24155753"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
