[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001985
name: Leiden 85-plus Study
def: "A population-based prospective cohort study of the oldest old in the city of Leiden, the Netherlands, which enrolled all inhabitants who turned 85 between September 1997 and September 1999 in the month of their 85th birthday and examined them with interviews and clinical examinations at baseline and yearly for five years, to study health, functioning and well-being in very old age; an earlier survey under the same name studied the prevalence of morbidity in the whole population of Leiden aged 85 and over, living independently or in institutions." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10732458/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9074345/fullTextXML", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:15374369"}
synonym: "L85PLUS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Leiden 85-Plus Study" RELATED []
synonym: "Leiden 85-plus study" RELATED []
