id: coho:COHO_0001995
name: Mayo-Perlegen Linked Efforts to Accelerate Parkinson's Solutions Collaboration
def: "A two-tiered case-control study of Parkinson disease at the Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, genotyped genome-wide on a Perlegen platform, whose cases were enrolled prospectively from the clinical practice of the Mayo Clinic's Department of Neurology from June 1996 to May 2004 among residents of Minnesota and the four surrounding states and assessed by a movement-disorders neurologist, and whose controls were unaffected siblings of cases (tier 1) or unrelated population controls matched on sex and age (tier 2), all screened for parkinsonism." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16252231", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000048.v1.p1"}
