comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Leeds is a city: the PGS Catalog cohort id Leeds is a kidney cancer case-control sample listed by city in the renal cell carcinoma genome-wide association study behind PGS000076, PGS000161 and PGS000722, with no study name. Found by the review of 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001997
name: Leuven Endometrial Cancer Study
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer at the Leuven University Hospital in Belgium, whose cases were white women aged 27–80 diagnosed with endometrial cancer, identified by active surveillance of the hospital's electronic patient files, with clinical data recorded at interview at diagnosis and from pathology reports. In genetic analyses its cases were compared with controls from blood donors of the Leuven Multidisciplinary Breast Centre study, and they were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30093612", IAO:0000119="PMID:27135401", IAO:0000119="PMID:40101186"}
