[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0001998
name: Lung Health Study
def: "A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:2048803", IAO:0000119="PMID:41527371", dcterms:contributor="Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
