[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002011
name: Leukotriene Modifier Or Corticosteroid or Corticosteroid-Salmeterol Trial
def: "A randomised, double-blind trial of the American Lung Association Asthma Clinical Research Centers, run at centres in the United States from 2003 to 2006, in which people whose asthma was well controlled on twice-daily low-dose inhaled fluticasone were assigned to continue it or to switch to once-daily montelukast or once-daily fluticasone plus salmeterol for 16 weeks, to test whether treatment could be stepped down without loss of asthma control." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:17507702", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00156819", IAO:0000119="PMID:26083242"}
