[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002017
name: Leukaemia Research Fund CLL4 trial
def: "The patients of the Leukaemia Research Fund CLL4 trial, a UK randomised phase III trial that between 1999 and 2004 assigned previously untreated patients with chronic lymphocytic leukaemia requiring treatment (Binet stage progressive A, B or C) to first-line chlorambucil, fludarabine, or fludarabine plus cyclophosphamide. Markers measured at trial entry were used to study prognosis, and blood samples from a subset of its patients were genotyped for the UK genome-wide association studies of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia and for studies of germline variants and patient outcome." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26457986", IAO:0000119="PMID:26964624", IAO:0000119="PMID:28112199", IAO:0000119="PMID:17658394", IAO:0000119="PMID:20511662", IAO:0000119="PMID:28165464"}
