[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002020
name: Lung Cancer in the Young study
def: "A German multicentre study of lung cancer diagnosed at the age of 50 or younger, run by the Institute of Epidemiology of the Helmholtz Zentrum München and the Department of Genetic Epidemiology of the University of Göttingen with 31 recruiting clinics across Germany from 2000, which collected a nationwide family sample (young patients with their parents, siblings, children and spouses) and a case–control sample with population controls from the KORA surveys, with epidemiological data on medical history, education, occupation, family history of cancer and smoking, and blood samples from which DNA and lymphoblastoid cell lines were prepared." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:18433484", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24704916", IAO:0000119="PMID:25644374", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
