[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002030
name: obsolete Mid-America Heart Institute
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog id has no score, development sample or evaluation sample set in the Catalog today (REST /cohort/MAHI and the full cohort list return nothing; it appears only in the Catalog's cohort table), so the paper that gave rise to it cannot be identified from the Catalog. MAHI is the Mid-America Heart Institute (Saint Luke's Health System, Kansas City), a cardiovascular hospital (E660.14). The PGS Catalog records no sample for the id. Where the name labels a genetic study sample (MIGen, PMID:19198609), it is a case-control set assembled at the institute: acute coronary syndrome survivors drawn from the institute's 'successive prospective cohort studies' plus outpatient controls, with no study name of its own. The underlying outcome registries have their own names in their own papers, but nothing ties the PGS id to any one of them, so the id denotes the site, not a named cohort. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002031
name: Malignant Ovarian Cancer Study
def: "A Danish population-based case-control study of the Danish Cancer Society, in which women aged 35 to 79 diagnosed in 1994 to 1999 with ovarian cancer or a borderline ovarian tumour in the municipalities of Copenhagen and Frederiksberg and the surrounding counties, and controls drawn at random from the female population of the same area through the Central Population Register, gave questionnaire data, blood and tumour tissue, to identify risk factors and prognostic factors for ovarian cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3108970/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2645422/fullTextXML", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2361465/fullTextXML"}
