[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002033
name: Sydney Memory and Ageing Study
def: "A longitudinal cohort of non-demented, community-dwelling people aged 70 to 90, recruited by random approach from the electoral roll in two areas of Sydney, Australia, and begun in 2005 to examine the clinical characteristics and prevalence of mild cognitive impairment and related syndromes and the rate of change in cognitive function over time, with annual telephone reviews and periodic detailed neuropsychiatric and medical assessments." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20637138"}
