id: coho:COHO_0002036
name: Mayo lung cancer GWAS
def: "A case-control sample of lung cancer patients who had never smoked, identified and recruited at Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, between 1997 and 2008, and never-smoking community residents matched to them by age, sex and ethnic background, genotyped for a genome-wide association study of lung cancer in never smokers." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20304703"}
