[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002041
name: Mexico City Childhood Asthma Study
def: "A case–parent trio study of childhood asthma in Mexico City, supported by the Intramural Research Program of the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, which recruited children aged 5 to 17 with asthma, diagnosed by a paediatric allergist from clinical symptoms and response to treatment, together with their biological parents, between June 1998 and November 2003 at the paediatric allergy clinic of the Hospital Infantil de México Federico Gómez, a large public hospital in central Mexico City; parents completed questionnaires on the children's asthma symptoms and risk factors, including environmental tobacco smoke, the children had skin prick tests and lung function tests, and blood was taken from children and parents for DNA, from which the trios were genotyped genome-wide." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19714205", IAO:0000119="PMID:26635092", IAO:0000119="PMID:21804549", IAO:0000119="PMID:21696813"}
