[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002048
name: MD Anderson Renal Cell Cancer Study
def: "A population-based case-control study of renal cell carcinoma run from the University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center in Houston since 2002, whose cases are Texas residents with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma identified from the appointment schedules of MD Anderson's urology and genitourinary oncology departments, and whose controls are cancer-free Texas residents found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age, sex, ethnicity and county of residence, with an in-person interview and a blood sample from each participant." [] {IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22010048"}
