[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002053
name: obsolete Massachussetts Eye and Ear Infirmary
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. In NEIGHBORHOOD (PMID:26752265) the MEEI dataset is the Genetic Etiologies of POAG project based at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, one of the three GLAUGEN studies. Replaced by COHO:0001793 (Genetic Etiologies of Primary-Open angle Glaucoma Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0001793

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002054
name: Melbourne Epidemiological Study of Childhood Asthma
def: "A population-based prospective study of childhood asthma, also known as the Melbourne Asthma Study, initiated in 1964 by Howard Williams of the Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, Australia, which recruited four asthma or wheeze groups and a control group of children aged 7 and has followed them into their seventh decade, providing the first prospective evidence linking childhood asthma to the development of COPD; its participants contributed to the Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium’s genome-wide association study." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21907864", dcterms:contributor="Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41849083"}
synonym: "Melbourne Asthma Study" RELATED []
synonym: "MESCA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
instance_of: coho:COHO_0000000 ! cohort
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia {xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13331842/fullTextXML", comment="Introduction The study set-up The Melbourne Epidemiological Study of Childhood Asthma (MESCA) also known as the Melbourne Asthma Study, was initiated in 1964 by the late Howard Williams of the Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, with the initial aim of determining the prevalence and describing the natural history of childhood asthma and wheezy bronchitis."}
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania
property_value: coho:numberOfParticipants "484" xsd:integer {IAO:0000116="combined sample: 401 recruited at age 7 in 1964 plus 83 severe asthmatics added at age 10 (1967)", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13331842/fullTextXML", comment="†The percentages from ages 14 to 50 follow-ups are based on the combined sample of 484 participants (401 original at age 7 + 83 SA added at age 10)"}
property_value: IAO:0000112 "PMID:21907864" xsd:string {dcterms:title="Identification of IL6R and chromosome 11q13.5 as risk loci for asthma.", xref="PMID:21907864", xref="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3517659/", comment="Phenotype and genotype collection for MESCA: C.H., M.R., P.LeS., C.R."}

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002055
name: Metabolic Syndrome Berlin Potsdam Study
def: "A cross-sectional study of the metabolic syndrome in Germany whose participants, randomly recruited from Berlin, Potsdam and their surroundings, underwent a 75 g oral glucose tolerance test with insulin measurements and nutritional assessment, and included people with normal glucose metabolism as well as people with impaired glucose metabolism or type 2 diabetes; part of it was later re-examined in a follow-up study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28257453", IAO:0000119="PMID:19052638", IAO:0000119="PMID:28835639"}
