id: coho:COHO_0002063
name: Massachusetts General Hospital Stroke Study
def: "The stroke genetics studies of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States, analysed together under this name: the Genetics of Cerebral Hemorrhage on Anticoagulation (GOCHA) study of people over 55 with acute primary haemorrhagic stroke and controls from ambulatory clinics, and the Genes Affecting Stroke Risk and Outcome Study (GASROS), a single-centre prospective cohort of adults with acute ischaemic stroke who presented to the hospital from 2003 to 2011, with controls matched on age, sex and race or ethnicity." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29892015"}
