name: Michigan, Mayo, AREDS, Pennsylvania Cohort Study
def: "A case-control collection for a joint genome-wide association study of age-related macular degeneration, assembled by researchers from the University of Michigan, the Mayo Clinic, the University of Pennsylvania and the Age-Related Eye Disease Study group with National Eye Institute intramural investigators, who contributed patients with advanced macular degeneration (geographic atrophy, neovascularisation or large drusen) and examined unaffected controls enrolled from 1998 through ophthalmology clinics in Michigan, Pennsylvania, Minnesota and Texas and through the Age-Related Eye Disease Study, genotyped together at the Center for Inherited Disease Research." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20385819", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000182.v3.p1"}
