id: coho:COHO_0002086
name: Max Planck Institute of Psychiatry Study
def: "A case-control sample for major depressive disorder at the Max Planck Institute of Psychiatry in Munich, Germany, whose cases were patients admitted to the institute's hospital for treatment of major depressive disorder and diagnosed by psychiatrists according to DSM-IV criteria, and whose controls were drawn at random from Munich community registries and screened for the absence of any lifetime axis I disorder; it contributed genotypes to the major depressive disorder analyses of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22472876"}
