[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002096
name: Mid-South Tobacco Family
def: "A family-based genetic study of nicotine dependence in which African American and European American smoker probands (aged at least 21, smoking at least 20 cigarettes a day for the preceding year and for at least five years) were recruited in the Mid-South states of the United States, primarily Tennessee, Mississippi and Arkansas, in 1999–2004, together with their biological parents and full siblings, with nicotine dependence assessed by smoking quantity, the Heaviness of Smoking Index and the Fagerström Test for Nicotine Dependence, for linkage and association studies of nicotine dependence." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17164261", IAO:0000119="PMID:16960812", IAO:0000119="PMID:17579606", IAO:0000119="PMID:19763258"}
