[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002100
name: obsolete Medical University of Vienna
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. MUV is the PGS Catalog's id for the BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers that the Medical University of Vienna (Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, General Hospital Vienna) contributed to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA, COHO:0000901). CIMBA itself names this study only 'General Hospital Vienna' (PMID:28346442 Supplementary Table 1; PMID:32665703 supplement), so it is a centre's unnamed set of carriers, not a named cohort. It is a site of CIMBA, like OUH and OSUCCG, which the review already marked as not cohorts. Not to be confused with DNMUV (COHO:0001672, Department of Neurology, Medical University of Vienna). Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002101
name: obsolete MXB
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. MXB is the Mexican Biobank (MXBB), the training sample of the PGS Catalog score it is recorded in (PMID:37148359). Replaced by COHO:0000114 (Mexican Biobank), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000114

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002102
name: Myopia Genomics Study of Hong Kong
def: "A genetic study of myopia at the Hong Kong Polytechnic University, which recruited unrelated adults of Chinese descent aged 18 to 45 years through the university's Optometry Clinic, excluding people with signs of ocular disorders or of inherited disorders associated with myopia, measured their refraction by cycloplegic autorefraction together with corneal curvature, lens thickness and axial length, and genotyped them genome-wide; it is a member study of the Consortium for Refractive Error and Myopia (CREAM)." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:24144296"}
synonym: "MyGS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Myopia Genomics Study" RELATED []
synonym: "Myopia Genomics Study (Hong Kong HTI)" RELATED []
synonym: "The Myopia Genomics Study" RELATED []
