[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002107
name: Nagano Breast Cancer Study
def: "A multicentre hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer in Nagano, Japan, enrolling a consecutive series of women aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed invasive breast cancer at four hospitals and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees matched by age and residential area, designed to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors and, with a parallel study in São Paulo, Brazil, to compare Japanese, Japanese Brazilian and non-Japanese Brazilian women." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3050759/fullTextXML"}
