[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002111
name: Women's College Research Institute Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Study
def: "A long-term study, started in 1995 at Women's College Hospital in Toronto, Canada, of women aged 18 or over carrying a BRCA1 or BRCA2 (later also PALB2) mutation, whatever their cancer history, recruited from Canada, the United States, Europe, Asia, the Caribbean and Latin America and followed by questionnaires every two years, to study hormonal, reproductive and lifestyle factors in the prevention and treatment of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; it contributes carriers to CIMBA." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx", IAO:0000119="https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/"}
