[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002121
name: North Cumbria Community Genetics Project
def: "A prospective, unselected, population-based birth cohort in West Cumbria, England, set up by the University of Newcastle and the Westlakes Research Institute, which from January 1996 to 2003 collected umbilical cord blood and tissue, with maternal consent and a short maternal lifestyle questionnaire, from babies born at the West Cumberland Hospital maternity unit in Whitehaven, storing DNA, plasma and viable cells as a resource for genetic and epidemiological studies of gene–environment interaction and health, with some children followed up in childhood." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22479380", IAO:0000119="PMID:9610806", IAO:0000119="PMID:24098518", IAO:0000119="PMID:19681860"}
synonym: "NCCGP" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
