[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002134
name: Netherlands Mental Health Survey and Incidence Study
def: "A psychiatric epidemiological population study of non-institutionalised Dutch adults, conducted by the Trimbos Institute in Utrecht, that interviews representative samples drawn by multistage, stratified random sampling (NEMESIS-1 from 1996 and NEMESIS-2 from 2007, aged 18-64, the latter with DNA from saliva, and NEMESIS-3 from 2019, aged 18-75) with the Composite International Diagnostic Interview and follows them up to determine the prevalence, incidence, course and consequences of mental disorders." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:9555130", IAO:0000119="PMID:20641046", IAO:0000119="PMID:35913550", IAO:0000119="PMID:42687372", IAO:0000119="PMID:9857790"}
synonym: "NEMESIS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "NEMESIS-Study" RELATED []
