id: coho:COHO_0002141
name: obsolete Australian NHMRC program
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. NHMRC is Australia's National Health and Medical Research Council, and the Australian NHMRC program a funding programme: the bipolar disorder GWAS of PMID:21353194 credits it with the recruitment of its Australian sample. A funder, not a cohort. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002142
name: obsolete Nurses Health Study III
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. NHS3 is the third Nurses' Health Study case-control set of the colorectal cancer GWAS of PMID:29917119, beside HPFS3, not the Nurses' Health Study 3 cohort begun in 2010, which could not have supplied its cases. The Catalog's name for it, Nurses Health Study III, names that other cohort and is not carried over. Replaced by COHO:0000456 (Nurses' Health Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000456

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002143
name: 1998 Singapore National Health Survey
def: "A population-based, cross-sectional survey conducted between September and November 1998 of Chinese, Malay and Asian Indian Singapore residents aged 18-69, based on the World Health Organization model for field surveys of diabetes and other noncommunicable diseases and the WHO MONICA protocol, with interviewer-administered questionnaires, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and fasting blood samples." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19252135", IAO:0000119="PMID:18599522"}
synonym: "1998 Singapore National Health Study" RELATED []
