[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002145
name: obsolete NHS-egems
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. NHS-egems is the Catalog's misspelling of NHS-cgems, the label the age-at-menopause GWAS of PMID:22267201 gives the Nurses' Health Study's breast cancer GWAS set, genotyped by the CGEMS project; that paper lists the Nurses' Health Study as exactly two sets, NHS-cgems and NHS-Hu. Replaced by COHO:0000456 (Nurses' Health Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000456

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002146
name: obsolete NHS-Hu
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. NHS-Hu is the label the age-at-menopause GWAS of PMID:22267201 gives the Nurses' Health Study's type 2 diabetes GWAS set. Replaced by COHO:0000456 (Nurses' Health Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000456

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002147
name: obsolete National Institute on Aging
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. NIA is the PGS Catalog's name for the US National Institute on Aging, an NIH research funding institute, and no PGS Catalog score or sample set uses the id, so no study sample stands behind it. Every Europe PMC hit is about the institute (grant mechanisms, workshops), not a cohort. Cohorts the institute sponsors already have their own terms (the NIA Late Onset Alzheimer's Disease Family Study COHO:0000669, the NIA Long Life Family Study in COHO:0000513), but nothing links this id to either one. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002148
name: obsolete Norfolk Island Cohort
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The Norfolk Island Cohort is what the Norfolk Island Health Study's papers call its sample (PMID:26628212, PMID:37886940). Replaced by COHO:0002153 (Norfolk Island Health Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0002153

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002149
name: obsolete National Israeli Cancer Control Center
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-25. The Clalit National Israeli Cancer Control Center is an institution that runs several separate studies, not a cohort; found when the IHCC Cohort Atlas's entry NICCC was checked (see src/curation/ihcc_atlas_review.tsv). Found by the IHCC Cohort Atlas review, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002150
name: Clalit National Israeli Cancer Control Center lung cancer study
def: "An ongoing population-based case-control study of lung cancer in Israel, run since 2005 by the Clalit National Israeli Cancer Control Center with Carmel Medical Center and the Technion, of newly diagnosed lung cancer cases of any histology and controls matched to them on age, sex and ethnicity, all interviewed face to face and giving a blood sample, with histology, tumour blocks and clinical follow-up available for most cases." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25924736", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28604730", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
