[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002151
name: obsolete Northern Institute for Cancer Research
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. NICR is the PGS Catalog's id for 23 childhood B-cell precursor acute lymphoblastic leukaemia cases, with no study name, from the Northern Institute for Cancer Research (Leukaemia Research Group, Newcastle University, UK). They were included in the UK-GWAS of PMID:27694927 ('23 cases from the Northern Institute for Cancer Research (16 males)'). This is an institute's unnamed handful of cases, not a named cohort. The other UK-GWAS samples already have COHO terms or are other catalog ids: UK Childhood Cancer Study COHO:0000178, 1958 British Birth Cohort COHO:0000207, WTCCC COHO:0000182. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002152
name: obsolete Nigerian cohort
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The PGS Catalog id Nigerian (Nigerian cohort) names only a nationality: no score uses it, and every paper found by the name uses the phrase for an unrelated, unnamed sample. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002153
name: Norfolk Island Health Study
def: "A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41751589", IAO:0000119="PMID:26628212"}
synonym: "NIC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "NIHS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Norfolk Island Cohort" RELATED []
synonym: "Norfolk Island cohort" RELATED []
synonym: "Norfolk Island Health study" RELATED []
instance_of: coho:COHO_0000000 ! cohort
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Australia {xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4667444/fullTextXML", comment="Located in the Pacific Ocean between Australia and New Zealand, the unique population isolate of Norfolk Island has been shown to exhibit increased prevalence of metabolic disorders (type-2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease) compared to mainland Australia."}
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oceania
property_value: coho:numberOfParticipants "1199" xsd:integer {IAO:0000116="Norfolk Islanders with data and samples collected by 2015", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4667444/fullTextXML", comment="To date the Norfolk Island Health Study (NIHS) has collected data and samples for 1199 Norfolk Islanders, 52 % (N = 624) of whom were found to have direct links to the original founders."}
property_value: IAO:0000112 "PMID:41751589" xsd:string {dcterms:title="An <i>ACOT4</i> Multi-Nucleotide Variant Is Associated with Cardiovascular Risk in Norfolk Island and UK Biobank Cohorts.", xref="PMID:41751589", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41751589+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core", comment="We leveraged the population genetic features of the Norfolk Island Health Study (NIHS, n = 601), to identify candidate functional variants which were analysed for association with CVD and metabolic syndrome traits."}

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002154
name: obsolete Nijmegen
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Nijmegen is a city: the PGS Catalog cohort id Nijmegen is a prostate cancer sample listed by city (alongside the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, NBS, as its controls) in the deCODE replication sets behind PGS000082 and PGS000793, with no study name. Found by the review of 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002155
name: obsolete NIMH Intramural Research Program
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The NIMH Intramural Research Program is the in-house research division of the US National Institute of Mental Health, which papers name as an affiliation, a funder or the host of several distinct collections; no score in the PGS Catalog uses the id. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002156
name: Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium
def: "A case–control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder in the United States, assembled by the Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium: its cases, of non-Ashkenazi European origin with bipolar I disorder, came from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative repository, selected where possible as pairs of affected siblings from families collected in its multicentre bipolar family study, and from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository; its controls came from the NIMH repository and reported no diagnosis of or treatment for bipolar disorder or schizophrenia and said they had not heard voices that others could not hear, with suspected major depression excluded. It is one of the bipolar disorder samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29906448", IAO:0000119="PMID:21926972", IAO:0000119="PMID:19416921"}
synonym: "NIMH RGR Bipolar Study 2 (Pritzker)" RELATED []
synonym: "NIMH/Pritzker" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "PNDRC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
