[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002167
name: Nashville Men's Health Study
def: "A clinic-based study of men aged 40 or older with no previous prostate cancer diagnosis who were scheduled for a diagnostic prostate biopsy at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, the Tennessee Valley Veterans Administration hospital or a large private urology practice in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, recruited from 2002 under a multicentre rapid-recruitment protocol that collects clinical, biological, behavioural and body-measurement data and blood and urine, to study risk factors for prostate cancer, prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia and benign prostatic enlargement." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:26158673", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21541018", IAO:0000119="PMID:19286210"}
