[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002173
name: Nordic Diltiazem Study
def: "A prospective, randomised, open, blinded-endpoint multicentre trial started in 1992 that enrolled patients aged 50-74 with primary hypertension and a diastolic blood pressure of 100 mm Hg or more at primary health care centres and hospital hypertension units in Norway and Sweden, and randomly assigned them to diltiazem or to conventional treatment with diuretics, beta-blockers or both, to compare their effects on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:10972367", IAO:0000119="PMID:8173702"}
