[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002176
name: Nottingham Smokers
def: "An ongoing collection, in Nottingham and funded by the University of Nottingham, of smokers of European ancestry over 40 years of age with a smoking history of more than 10 pack-years, whose lung function (FEV1 and FVC) was measured by spirometry at enrolment, before and after bronchodilation, and from which people with asthma were excluded; divided by spirometry into COPD cases and smoking controls, it has served as a follow-up sample in genetic association studies of lung function and COPD." [] {IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26952864", IAO:0000119="PMID:24786987", IAO:0000119="PMID:21965014"}
