[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002178
name: NPC Genes, Environment, and EBV study
def: "A population-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in southern China, in which incident cases aged 20–74 years were recruited from March 2010 to December 2013, and randomly selected population controls from November 2010 to November 2014, among residents of 13 cities and counties of Guangdong Province and Guangxi Autonomous Region, with questionnaires and biospecimens collected to study the independent and interactive roles of genes, environmental exposures and Epstein–Barr virus infection in the disease; it was conducted by Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center, Karolinska Institutet, Guangxi Medical University and collaborating institutions." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29152064"}
