[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002179
name: obsolete NPHS
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. NPHS, the National Physicians Health Study of PMID:26590902, is the Physicians' Health Study. Replaced by COHO:0000626 (Physicians' Health Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000626

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002180
name: obsolete Novel Risk Factors and Potential Early Detection Markers for Ovarian Cancer
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. Novel Risk Factors and Potential Early Detection Markers for Ovarian Cancer is the name several Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium tables give its study HOP (PMID:23535730, PMID:27698005), which the consortium elsewhere names Hormones and Ovarian Cancer Prediction. Replaced by COHO:0001872 (Hormones and Ovarian Cancer Prediction Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0001872

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002181
name: obsolete NRG Oncology
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. NRG Oncology is a clinical trials group. In the CIMBA papers the PGS Catalog records the id in (PMID:29058716), it labels the group's contribution of BRCA1 and BRCA2 carriers, with no study name of its own; the carriers are covered by CIMBA (COHO:0000901). Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002182
name: Nambour Skin Cancer Study
def: "A prospective community-based cohort of adults aged 20–69 years randomly selected from the electoral roll of the township of Nambour in subtropical Queensland, Australia, begun in 1986 with a survey of skin cancer prevalence and dermatologists' skin examinations; from 1992 to 1996 most participants took part in a randomised trial of daily sunscreen use and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention, and the cohort has since been followed for skin cancers, diet and mortality." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:35505292", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38680071"}
