[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002183
name: National Study of Endometrial Cancer Genetics
def: "A UK study of women with histologically confirmed endometrial cancer, identified through collaborating clinicians throughout the United Kingdom, with the help of the National Cancer Research Network, from 2008 to 2013 (avoiding centres that recruited to the SEARCH study) and coordinated from the University of Oxford, to find inherited genetic variants that influence endometrial cancer risk; its cases have been compared with controls from other UK studies, such as the CORGI study and the 1958 Birth Cohort." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:27135401"}
