relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/United_Kingdom {xref="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fejhg.2010.38/MediaObjects/41431_2010_BFejhg201038_MOESM31_ESM.pdf", comment="United Kingdom: Asthmatic subjects and controls were selected from the Nottingham area from 3 study cohorts recruited over the period 1995-2008."}
property_value: IAO:0000112 "PMID:20372189" xsd:string {dcterms:title="A sequence variant on 17q21 is associated with age at onset and severity of asthma.", xref="PMID:20372189", xref="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fejhg.2010.38/MediaObjects/41431_2010_BFejhg201038_MOESM31_ESM.pdf", comment="Childhood asthma cases (n=57) were included by using index cases from the Nottingham sib pair asthma study12 and additional adult asthma cases were recruited from an ongoing study of asthma severity (N=141)."}

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002186
name: obsolete North Shore University Health System
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The one id is used for two unrelated samples from the same health system, a CIMBA contributing centre and an active-surveillance prostate cancer series, neither with a study name. NSUHS is the PGS Catalog's id for NorthShore University HealthSystem, Evanston, Illinois, USA, as a site, used for two unrelated samples: (1) the BRCA1/BRCA2 pathogenic-variant carriers NorthShore contributed to CIMBA (CIMBA's code NORTHSHORE; PMID:32665703, 28346442), and (2) 432 prostate cancer patients of European ancestry on active surveillance at NorthShore, evaluated for a prostate cancer PRS together with Johns Hopkins patients (PMID:33956350, PSS001140). Neither sample has a study name or a design of its own beyond the institution ('separate active surveillance studies conducted at ... NorthShore University HealthSystem'), so the id denotes an institution, not a named cohort. The CIMBA carriers are covered by CIMBA (COHO:0000901). It is not the Polish Breast Cancer Study (COHO:0000930), which the triage matched only through a shared line of the ethics list. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

