[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002191
name: Neocodex–Murcia study
def: "A Spanish case-control sample for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease, assembled by the genomics company Neocodex in Seville, whose patients with sporadic Alzheimer's disease were diagnosed with possible or probable disease under NINCDS–ADRDA criteria by neurologists at the Virgen de la Arrixaca University Hospital in Murcia, and whose controls, of unknown cognitive status, came from the Spanish general population." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35379992", IAO:0000119="PMID:21627779"}
