[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002196
name: Ohio Colorectal Cancer Prevention Initiative
def: "A prospective statewide study of adults who underwent surgical resection for primary invasive colorectal cancer at 51 hospitals across Ohio, United States, enrolled from 2013 to 2016, in which every tumour was screened for mismatch-repair deficiency and those meeting high-risk criteria (mismatch-repair deficiency, diagnosis before 50, multiple primary tumours or an affected first-degree relative) had multigene germline panel testing, to identify Lynch syndrome and other hereditary cancer syndromes." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:34250417", IAO:0000119="PMID:42435229"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
synonym: "OCCPI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
