[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002199
name: obsolete Oncology Department of Zaragoza Hospital
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. ODZH is the PGS Catalog's id for the Spanish case-control material that deCODE genetics' multi-population cancer GWAS used as a replication group: cancer patients (lung, ovarian and thyroid cancer in the papers read) recruited from the Oncology Department of Zaragoza Hospital, with controls who attended the University Hospital in Zaragoza for other conditions (PMID:21303977, 28195142, 21964575). The papers call it only 'the Spanish study population' or 'Zaragoza, Spain', with case recruitment differing by cancer; it has no study name and no design of its own beyond the hospital, so the id denotes a site, not a named cohort (like LUHR, E651, the Landspitali material in the same deCODE papers). No COHO term covers it. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002200
name: Ontario Familial Colorectal Cancer Registry
def: "A population-based familial colorectal cancer registry in Ontario, Canada, one of the sites of the US National Cancer Institute's Colon Cancer Family Registry, which recruited people aged 20 to 74 with colorectal cancer diagnosed from July 1997 to June 2000, identified through the Ontario Cancer Registry, and population controls randomly sampled from Ontario residents and frequency-matched to the cases by sex and five-year age group, who completed family-history, epidemiologic and food questionnaires and gave blood samples." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17618283"}
