id: coho:COHO_0002202
name: Ottawa Heart Genomics Study
def: "A case-control study of coronary artery disease at the University of Ottawa Heart Institute, Ottawa, Canada, that recruited people of European ancestry without diabetes, with cases defined by more than 50% stenosis of a major coronary artery at angiography, myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation, and controls who were either angiographically free of coronary disease or elderly and asymptomatic, genotyped in several phases for genome-wide association studies of coronary artery disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28209224", IAO:0000119="PMID:23202125", IAO:0000119="PMID:25180781", IAO:0000119="PMID:21378990"}
