[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002203
name: obsolete Ohio State University
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The Columbus-area HNPCC study, one of the named studies behind this id, has no COHO term and no PGS Catalog id of its own; the curator may want to consider it separately if a catalog or resource names it. Ohio_SU is the PGS Catalog's id for the Ohio State University's combined contribution to the colorectal cancer GWAS of Huyghe et al. 2019 (PMID:30510241): cases from two separate named studies, the Columbus-area HNPCC study and the Ohio Colorectal Cancer Prevention Initiative, matched to controls from the OSUMC Human Genetics Sample Bank (Columbus Area Controls Sample Bank). The id names the university, not a study; the combined set has no name or design of its own, and its parts are distinct studies that the Catalog also lists separately (OCCPI, E836, COHO:0002196; OSUMC, E857, judged not a cohort; OSU, E855, the Stefanie Spielman Breast Bank and the Columbus Area Control Sample Bank). So it is not a cohort, and it should not be a synonym of any of those. None of the COHO terms the triage matched (BioVU, TGEN2, York, CRC, etc.) is related. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002204
