[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002213
name: Oregon Sudden Unexpected Death Study
def: "An ongoing prospective community-based study of out-of-hospital sudden cardiac arrest and sudden cardiac death in the Portland, Oregon metropolitan area (including Multnomah County), United States, running since 2002, which ascertains cases through first responders, emergency medical services, area hospitals and the county medical examiner, reviews their medical records, and compares them with geographically matched controls, including people with coronary artery disease, some of them with blood samples for genetic studies." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16731473", IAO:0000119="PMID:16545646", IAO:0000119="PMID:25227407", IAO:0000119="PMID:20360844"}
