[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002224
name: Oxford Endometriosis Gene Study
def: "A United Kingdom-based international genetic study of endometriosis, run from the University of Oxford, that from 1995 to 2006 recruited women with surgically confirmed endometriosis, both families with two or more affected sisters and single cases, through collaborating clinicians in Britain, Ireland and the United States, advertisements and its website, to identify susceptibility genes by linkage analysis and positional cloning; with the Australian Genes Behind Endometriosis Study it forms the International Endogene Study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.731/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng731_MOESM17_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:16080113", IAO:0000119="PMID:17498711", IAO:0000119="PMID:10206402"}
