id: coho:COHO_0002225
name: Progression to insulin deficiency: South West England cohort
def: "A cross-sectional cohort of white European adults from Devon and Cornwall in South West England who were diagnosed with diabetes between the ages of 20 and 40 and had had it for more than three years, excluding known monogenic and secondary diabetes, assembled by researchers at the University of Exeter to test whether a type 1 diabetes genetic risk score predicts progression to severe insulin deficiency (continuous insulin treatment within three years of diagnosis with low C-peptide)." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26577414"}
