[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002228
name: obsolete Princess Alexandra Hospital
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: Borderline: the PAH cases are a defined collection (histopathologically confirmed invasive primary melanoma, 1994–2007, recruited at the hospital's Multidisciplinary Melanoma Clinic and related clinics, with its own funding and 'cohort management'), but no source gives it a name other than the hospital's ('PAH', 'the PAH dataset'). If the curator prefers to treat it like the Melanoma Institute Australia cohort (COHO:0001103), which comes from the same paper, it would need a descriptive label such as 'Princess Alexandra Hospital melanoma case series', which no source uses. PAH is the PGS Catalog's id for Princess Alexandra Hospital, Brisbane, Australia, as the source of 236 unrelated melanoma cases recruited at its Multidisciplinary Melanoma Clinic (primary melanoma confirmed 1994–2007) and genotyped with the Melanoma Institute Australia cases for melanoma GWAS and PRS work (PMID:32716505, 32341527). The papers call this sample only 'PAH' or 'the PAH dataset'; it has no study name, so the id denotes a hospital's case series, not a named cohort. It is not the Melanoma Institute Australia cohort (COHO:0001103), a separate Sydney collection, nor the Queensland Study of Melanoma (COHO:0001031) or the old Queensland Melanoma Project registry. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

