id: coho:COHO_0002231
name: Pharmacogenomics and Risk of Cardiovascular Disease Study
def: "A pharmacogenomic study of the response to statins that combines two clinical populations of white adults in the United States given a statin for a fixed period: participants of the Cholesterol and Atherosclerosis Pharmacogenetics (CAP) study, recruited at two clinical sites in Los Angeles and San Francisco and treated with simvastatin for six weeks, and participants of the Pravastatin Inflammation CRP Evaluation (PRINCE) trial, enrolled at sites across the country and treated with pravastatin for twelve weeks." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf"}
