[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002232
name: Parkinson's, Genes, and Environment Study
def: "A case-control study of Parkinson's disease nested in the NIH-AARP Diet and Health Study, the prospective cohort established by the National Cancer Institute in 1995–1996, whose cases are cohort members who reported Parkinson's disease in the cohort's 2004–2006 follow-up survey and were confirmed by their treating physicians or by medical record review, and whose controls are randomly selected cohort members who did not report Parkinson's disease, frequency-matched to the cases on year of birth, sex and ethnicity, with DNA collected from saliva." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21912625", IAO:0000119="PMID:21741729"}
