property_value: IAO:0000112 "PMID:22999729" xsd:string {dcterms:title="Mortality and cardiovascular events are best predicted by low central/peripheral pulse pressure amplification but not by high blood pressure levels in elderly nursing home subjects: the PARTAGE (Predictive Values of Blood Pressure and Arterial Stiffness in Institutionalized Very Aged Population) study.", xref="PMID:22999729", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22999729+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core", comment="The aim of the longitudinal PARTAGE study was to determine the predictive value of blood pressure (BP) and pulse pressure amplification, a marker of arterial function, for overall mortality (primary endpoint) and major cardiovascular (CV) events, in subjects older than 80 years of age living in a nursing home."}

