id: coho:COHO_0002241
name: Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial
def: "A phase 3 randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, in which generally healthy men aged 55 or older with a normal digital rectal examination and a PSA level of 3 ng/mL or less, recruited at sites across the United States and Canada from 1994 to 1997, were assigned to finasteride (5 mg a day) or placebo for seven years and offered an end-of-study prostate biopsy, to test whether finasteride prevents prostate cancer." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:21149329", IAO:0000119="PMID:21667068", dcterms:contributor="GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22810146"}
