[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002257
name: Portuguese Island Collection
def: "A collection of individuals and multiplex families with schizophrenia and/or bipolar disorder, with psychiatrically screened controls, sampled from the founder population of the Azores and Madeira archipelagos of Portugal through all the islands' psychiatric and general hospitals, taking families only if the proband's parents and four grandparents were native to the islands, with further families from mainland Portugal identified through the University of Coimbra and participants from the first- and second-generation Portuguese immigrant population of the United States; it was used in linkage and association studies of psychosis and became part of the Genomic Psychiatry Cohort." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:23650244", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:15704217", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:24123842"}
synonym: "PIC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Portuguese island collection" RELATED []
