name: obsolete Pittsburgh 3D Facial Norms
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. PITT is how facial genetics consortia name the 3D Facial Norms sample: 'Pittsburgh 3D Facial Norms study (PITT)' is the 3D Facial Norms dataset (PMID:31763980, PMID:30405702). Replaced by COHO:0001139 (3D Facial Norms cohort), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0001139

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002262
name: Pittsburgh Lung Screening Study
def: "A prospective, Pittsburgh-based cohort of current and former cigarette smokers aged 50-79 (at least half a pack a day for 25 years and, for former smokers, quit within the last 10 years), enrolled in 2002-2005 for computed-tomography lung cancer screening and long-term follow-up." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", dcterms:contributor="Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26352532"}
