[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002268
name: obsolete Primary Open Angle Glaucoma
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. POAG names a disease, primary open-angle glaucoma, not a study; no score in the PGS Catalog uses the id. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002269
name: obsolete Poland
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Poland is a country: the PGS Catalog cohort id Poland is the PRACTICAL consortium’s label for a prostate cancer case-control sample from the University Hospital in Szczecin (The Poland Group) and, in a breast cancer score, another Polish sample, neither a cohort with a name of its own. Found by the review of 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002270
name: obsolete Nijmegen Polygene Study & Nijmegen Biomedical Study
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. POLYGENE is the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium's Nijmegen study NTH ('Nijmegen Polygene Study & Nijmegen Biomedical Study POLYGENE NTH Netherlands', PMID:21639959), which the consortium's later tables call the Nijmegen Ovarian Cancer Study. Replaced by COHO:0002170 (Nijmegen Ovarian Cancer Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0002170

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002271
name: Prospective study of Outcomes in Sporadic versus Hereditary breast cancer
def: "A prospective cohort of women in the United Kingdom diagnosed with a first primary breast cancer at age 40 or younger, recruited between June 2001 and December 2007 (with an additional category of BRCA1 or BRCA2 carriers diagnosed at 41 to 50), with family history, epidemiological and clinical data and blood collected and annual follow-up, to establish whether genetic status influences breast cancer prognosis independently of known prognostic factors." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17697367", IAO:0000119="PMID:20453838"}
