id: coho:COHO_0002276
name: Molecular Reclassification to Find Clinically Useful Biomarkers for Systemic Autoimmune Diseases
def: "A European multicentre observational study of the PRECISESADS project that recruited adults with systemic autoimmune diseases (rheumatoid arthritis, systemic sclerosis, primary Sjögren's syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus, primary antiphospholipid syndrome, mixed connective tissue disease and undifferentiated connective tissue disease) and healthy controls at 19 institutions in nine countries between December 2014 and December 2018, in a cross-sectional cohort and a prospective inception cohort, to reclassify these diseases into molecular clusters using omics profiles." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:32665668", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02890134?fields=IdentificationModule,DescriptionModule,DesignModule,ContactsLocationsModule,StatusModule"}
