[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002279
name: Pravastatin Inflammation/CRP Evaluation
def: "An investigator-initiated, multicentre, community-based trial in office-based practices in the United States that from February to December 2000 evaluated the effect of pravastatin 40 mg/d on C-reactive protein: men and women with no prior cardiovascular disease (the primary prevention cohort) were randomly assigned, double-blind, to pravastatin or placebo for 24 weeks, and patients with known cardiovascular disease (the secondary prevention cohort) received open-label pravastatin, with lipid profiles and high-sensitivity C-reactive protein measured at baseline, 12 and 24 weeks. DNA collected from participants was later used in genome-wide studies of the lipid-lowering response to statins." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:11376301", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20339536", IAO:0000119="PMID:11434828"}
