id: coho:COHO_0002283
name: Parkinson's Research: The Organized Genetics Initiative
def: "A genetic study of familial Parkinson's disease, run through the Parkinson Study Group, that ascertains multiplex families through a pair of living siblings who both have Parkinson's disease and has the affected family members examined by movement disorder specialists at Parkinson Study Group clinical centres throughout North America, to identify genes contributing to susceptibility to Parkinson's disease." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:26595808", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18987351", IAO:0000119="PMID:19279319"}
