id: coho:COHO_0002285
name: Progression Risk of Glaucoma: Relevant SNPs With Significant Association
def: "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30517101", IAO:0000119="PMID:36246177", IAO:0000119="PMID:36249683"}
