id: coho:COHO_0002287
name: Prospective Athletic Heart Study
def: "An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35368514"}
