[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002288
name: Sea Islands Genetic African American Registry
def: "A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25279862", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19783527", IAO:0000119="PMID:18835935"}
