[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002291
name: Prostate testing for cancer and Treatment study
def: "A randomised phase 3 trial in the United Kingdom in which men aged 50–69 registered at primary care centres in nine UK cities were invited for PSA testing (a pilot from 1999, the main phase from 2001 to 2009), men with a raised PSA were offered prostate biopsy, and those with clinically localised prostate cancer were randomly assigned to active monitoring, radical prostatectomy or radiotherapy, to investigate the effectiveness of treatments for localised prostate cancer." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25163905", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
