[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002292
name: Prostate Cancer and Environment Study
def: "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, in which men aged 75 or under with histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed in 2005–2009 were ascertained across Montreal's French-language hospitals and controls were randomly selected from the provincial electoral list of French-speaking men, frequency-matched on age, and interviewed in person on sociodemographic, lifestyle, environmental and medical factors, with a genetic component." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24655933", IAO:0000119="PMID:30233396", IAO:0000119="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1"}
