[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002299
name: Prospective Urban Rural Epidemiology study
def: "A large international prospective epidemiological cohort study, funded by the Population Health Research Institute (Hamilton, Canada) with Canadian research funders, that has recruited since 2002 adults aged 35 to 70 years, with their household members, from representative samples of urban and rural communities in low-, middle- and high-income countries on five continents (17 countries at first, 27 later), to examine how societal influences and social, behavioural, genetic and environmental factors relate to lifestyle, cardiovascular risk factors and chronic non-communicable diseases, above all cardiovascular disease. Participants give medical history, lifestyle, anthropometric and electrocardiogram data and blood stored for biochemistry and genetic analysis, and are followed up for at least 10 years for events and death." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:34910150", IAO:0000119="PMID:24093842", IAO:0000119="PMID:19540385", IAO:0000119="PMID:40519856"}
