[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002300
name: Puerto Rico Familial Colorectal Cancer Registry
def: "A familial cancer registry established in 2006 at the University of Puerto Rico Comprehensive Cancer Center, the first familial cancer registry in Puerto Rico, which enrols Hispanic individuals with a clinical or genetic diagnosis of a hereditary colorectal cancer or polyposis syndrome (familial adenomatous polyposis, attenuated FAP, hamartomatous polyposis syndromes or Lynch syndrome), referred with a personal or family history of possible familial colorectal cancer or polyposis by gastroenterologists, oncologists and colorectal surgeons. Consenting probands complete questionnaires on medical history, environmental exposures and cancer family history, their pedigrees are traced, and the registry offers affected families education, genetic testing and surveillance." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23460355", IAO:0000119="PMID:25389437"}
synonym: "Puerto Rico Familial Cancer Registry" RELATED []
synonym: "PURIFICAR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "The Puerto Rico Familial Colorectal Cancer Registry" RELATED []
