[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002302
name: Queensland Familial Melanoma Project
def: "A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases' relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:8791274", IAO:0000119="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
