[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002303
name: Quebec Family Study
def: "An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:24533236", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
synonym: "QFS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
