[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002308
name: Radiogenomics: Assessment of Polymorphisms for Predicting the Effects of Radiotherapy
def: "A UK multicentre sample collection study, opened in 2005, that collects blood samples and prospectively recorded radiotherapy toxicity data from cancer patients, among them breast and prostate cancer patients, enrolled in radiotherapy clinical trials (such as RT01 and CHHiP) and other studies, to identify genetic variants that predict the adverse effects of radiotherapy on normal tissue." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29892016", IAO:0000119="PMID:22767148", IAO:0000119="PMID:27070714"}
