[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002315
name: Reykjavik Eye Study
def: "A population-based epidemiological study of eye disease, run by Icelandic and Japanese study groups, in which citizens of Reykjavik, Iceland, aged 50 years and older, randomly selected from the national population census, were given ophthalmological examinations to determine the prevalence of lens opacities, refractive error and visual acuity, and open-angle glaucoma." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:11054002", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:11167223", IAO:0000119="PMID:12928689"}
