id: coho:COHO_0002341
name: Salzburg Atherosclerosis Prevention Program in subjects at High Individual Risk
def: "A prospective study begun in 1999 in Salzburg, Austria, to investigate genetic and environmental factors contributing to atherosclerotic vascular diseases, whose participants, healthy unrelated adults aged 39–67 years, were recruited through health screening programmes in large companies in and around the city of Salzburg and examined with carotid ultrasonography and laboratory measurements." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25273948", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:15715680"}
