[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002346
name: Sheffield Breast Cancer Study
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer in Sheffield, United Kingdom, that recruited women with histologically confirmed breast cancer from the surgical outpatient clinics of the Royal Hallamshire Hospital, Sheffield, and Rotherham District Hospital from 1998 to 2005, and as controls women aged 50 to 60 attending the Sheffield mammography screening service in 2000–2004 whose mammograms showed no breast lesions, all resident in the Sheffield area and of northern European ancestry, for studies of genetic susceptibility to and survival from breast cancer." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:20520800", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:23844225"}
