[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002355
name: South Carolina Prostate Cancer Study
def: "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:29117387", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:15280622", IAO:0000119="PMID:16912087", IAO:0000119="PMID:15150583"}
