[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002368
name: San Francisco Prostate Cancer Study
def: "A population-based case-control study of advanced prostate cancer among non-Hispanic White and African American men aged 40-79 in the San Francisco Bay Area, California, United States, whose cases were diagnosed from 1997 to 2000 and identified through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry and whose controls, men without a history of prostate cancer, were found by random-digit dialling and from Health Care Financing Administration rosters and frequency matched to cases on race and age; participants were interviewed about lifetime sun exposure and other risk factors and gave biospecimens." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:15958597", IAO:0000119="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5448553/supplementaryFiles"}
