property_value: IAO:0000112 "PMID:42664632" xsd:string {dcterms:title="Multidimensional sleep health and all-cause mortality: Counterfactual risk estimation and component-specific contributions in the sleep heart health study.", xref="PMID:42664632", xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42664632+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core", comment="We included 4382 adults from the Sleep Heart Health Study with baseline polysomnography, questionnaire-based sleep assessments, covariates, and mortality follow-up."}

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002377
name: obsolete Sheba Medical Centre
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. SHMC is the PGS Catalog's id for the Chaim Sheba Medical Center (Tel Hashomer, Ramat Gan, Israel) as a CIMBA contributing site: the BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic-variant carriers from its oncogenetics unit that entered the OCAC/CIMBA ovarian cancer GWAS (PMID:28346442) and CIMBA's PRS analyses (PMID:32665703). CIMBA's own lists name the study only after the hospital ('Sheba Medical Centre', 'SMC-CIMBA'), and no source gives it a name, design or recruitment of its own. This is the same case as LUHR (E651, Landspitali), so it is not a cohort. No COHO term covers it; CIMBA is COHO:0000901. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002378
name: Singapore Indian Chinese Cohort
def: "A population-based eye study of ethnic Indian and ethnic Chinese adults aged 40 years and older living in south-western Singapore, sampled by age-stratified random sampling from name lists provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs and examined with standardised interviews, eye examinations and laboratory investigations, with blood, tear and urine samples stored for genetic and proteomic studies, to quantify ethnic differences in the prevalence, risk factors and impact of major eye diseases; its Indian component is the Singapore Indian Eye Study, and together with the Singapore Malay Eye Study it covers Singapore's three main ethnic groups." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:19995197", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:39051044", IAO:0000119="PMID:23964661"}
