id: coho:COHO_0002379
name: Shanghai Institute of Hypertension GWAS
def: "A hospital-based case-control genome-wide association study of hypertension among Han Chinese adults aged 37–84 living in the Shanghai metropolitan area, approved by the ethics committee of Ruijin Hospital. Its cases had hypertension diagnosed after age 30 and at least two family members with hypertension, and its controls were normotensive adults over 40; both groups had a BMI under 27 kg/m2 and cases had no diabetes." [] {IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
