[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002380
name: obsolete Sikh GWAS
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. Sikh GWAS is the Punjabi Sikh type 2 diabetes GWAS sample of PMID:23300278, drawn from the Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study, which the paper says is also named the Sikh Diabetes Study. The Catalog's name describes that analysis and is not carried over. Replaced by COHO:0001116 (Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study/Sikh Diabetes Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0001116

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002381
name: Silk Road
def: "A collection of genetic and phenotypic data, gathered in 2010 by the scientific expedition Marco Polo (Marcopolo 2010), from healthy people in communities of the Terra Madre network along the Silk Road in Georgia, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan and Tajikistan (rural communities, and also cities in Uzbekistan and Kazakhstan), with ethics approval from the IRCCS Burlo Garofolo hospital in Trieste, Italy. It was used to study the genetics of the senses, such as taste, food preferences, hearing and vision, in these isolated populations." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25476266", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26188009", IAO:0000119="PMID:24626196"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
