[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002393
name: Study of Myocardial Infarctions Leiden
def: "A population-based case-control study from Leiden, the Netherlands, of men born in the Netherlands, comparing men younger than 70 years who had a first myocardial infarction between 1990 and 1996 with control men without a history of myocardial infarction, frequency-matched on 10-year age groups, used to study coagulation and fibrinolytic factors, their genetic variants and cardiovascular risk factors as risk factors for myocardial infarction." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:19377074", IAO:0000119="PMID:16931632", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:17053057", IAO:0000119="PMID:28393470"}
