[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002395
name: SNP Prostate Ghent
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of prostate cancer at Ghent University Hospital, Belgium, whose cases are men treated with intensity-modulated radiotherapy as primary or postoperative treatment for prostate cancer at the hospital between 2000 and 2010, first genotyped to study genetic markers of radiation toxicity, and whose controls are employees of the hospital and members of social activity clubs without a history of any cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="PMID:22658438"}
