[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002396
name: Southern Ostrobothnia isolate GWAS
def: "A Finnish case-control sample of multiple sclerosis patients with both parents, or one parent and a family history of multiple sclerosis, from Southern Ostrobothnia, the internal isolate on the western coast of Finland with an increased prevalence and familial clustering of multiple sclerosis, and population-based controls, drawn from the Health 2000 project, matched to them by genome-wide identity-by-state sharing and parental birthplace, that formed the genome-wide association stage of a 2010 study of multiple sclerosis in that isolate." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20159113"}
synonym: "SO" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
