[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002403
name: obsolete The Spanish study (University Hospital of Bellvitge, Hospital of Leon)
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The paper's supplement (the likely source of the Catalog's full name) could not be downloaded, even through the watcher; the identification rests on the hospitals named, the paper's acknowledgement and the Catalog's cohort list. The PGS Catalog's 'Spain' ('The Spanish study (University Hospital of Bellvitge, Hospital of Leon)') is the colorectal cancer case-control study that COHO already has as CRCGEN (COHO:0000585, Colorectal Cancer Genetics & Genomics). CRCGEN's own paper (PMC8574048) says its second component 'was conducted in parallel in the University Hospital of Bellvitge and in the Hospital of León, León, during 2007–2015', exactly the two hospitals the Catalog names, and the PGS Catalog paper PMID:31866242 acknowledges 'CRCGEN: Colorectal Cancer Genetics & Genomics, Spanish study' (COHO:0000585 already carries that phrase as a synonym). The other Spanish sample in that score (EPICOLON, Hospital Clínic Barcelona) has its own Catalog id. Add the Catalog name as a synonym and 'Spain' as an acronym of COHO:0000585 (no other COHO term uses 'Spain' as an acronym, so no editor note is needed); obsolete placeholder COHO:0002403 in its favour. Replaced by COHO:0000585 (Colorectal Cancer Genetics & Genomics), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000585

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002404
name: Determining the Molecular Pathways and Genetic Predisposition of the Acute Inflammatory Process Caused by SARS-CoV-2
def: "A Spanish study of the molecular pathways and genetic predisposition behind the acute inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2, run from the GENYO Centre for Genomics and Oncological Research in Granada, whose participants, patients with laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection whose blood was sampled on arrival at the emergency ward of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid (from March 2020) or the Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga (from August 2020), together with SARS-CoV-2 PCR-negative individuals, were genotyped on the Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array and profiled for whole-blood DNA methylation; it contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33846372", IAO:0000119="PMID:34237774", IAO:0000119="PMID:35933486"}
