[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002410
name: Genomic epidemiology of SARS-Cov-2 and host genetics in Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19)
def: "A COVID-19 pandemic-tracking study at Stanford Health Care in northern California that, from March to July 2020, collected the residual nasopharyngeal swab media of clinical SARS-CoV-2 tests from approximately consecutive SARS-CoV-2-positive and -negative patients, linked them to electronic health record data, and sequenced the patients' genomes at low coverage together with viral genomes and transcriptomes, to study host genetic, viral and clinical correlates of COVID-19 severity; it contributed its host genetic data to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:34237774", IAO:0000119="PMID:36042219"}
synonym: "Stanford" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
