id: coho:COHO_0002411
name: Strabismus, Amblyopia and Refractive Error Study in Singaporean Chinese Preschoolers
def: "A population-based study of Chinese children aged 6 to 72 months living in south-western and western Singapore, recruited door to door from 2006 to 2008 with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month age bands, who had parental questionnaires and eye examinations including visual acuity, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and retinal photography, to study strabismus, amblyopia and refractive error in preschool children; a family study in 2008-2010 added parents and siblings." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:19426960", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19933197", IAO:0000119="PMID:23860760", IAO:0000119="PMID:22064996", IAO:0000119="PMID:34319387"}
