[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002412
name: Singapore Translational and Clinical Research in Psychosis
def: "A five-year national flagship research programme on psychosis in Singapore, based at the Institute of Mental Health, made up of three linked studies: a genome-wide association and copy-number study of schizophrenia and its cognitive phenotypes, a prospective study of people at ultra-high risk of psychosis, and a randomized controlled trial to improve neurocognition in schizophrenia. Its schizophrenia study recruited outpatients and inpatients of Chinese ethnicity aged 21 to 55 with DSM-IV schizophrenia at the Institute of Mental Health from 2008 to 2011." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:36831758", IAO:0000119="PMID:22032547"}
