[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002414
name: obsolete Stollery Children’s Hospital Coeliac Clinic
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. STOLLERY_CC is the PGS Catalog's id for the pilot clinical sample of PMID:32790217: about 128 children referred to the coeliac clinic of the Stollery Children's Hospital (Edmonton, Alberta, Canada) with suspected coeliac disease, plus paediatric gastroenterology controls, used once to evaluate a coeliac genetic risk score (PSS000381). The paper and the Catalog describe it only as a 'pilot clinical cohort' at a tertiary paediatric clinic; it has no study name, design or recruitment beyond that one paper, so it is a clinic's patient sample, not a cohort. No COHO term matches. Recommend obsoleting placeholder COHO:0002414. If the curator prefers to keep one-paper clinical samples, reading the closed full text would be needed for recruitment dates. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002415
name: Special Turku Coronary Risk Factor Intervention Project
def: "A randomised controlled trial in Turku, Finland, that enrolled infants and their parents at well-baby clinics between 1989 and 1992 and gave the intervention group individualised dietary counselling from age 7 months to 20 years, aimed at improving dietary fat quality to prevent cardiovascular disease, while the control group received routine care; participants have been followed into adulthood." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16250721", IAO:0000119="PMID:42011282"}
