[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002427
name: Southampton Women's Survey
def: "A prospective mother-offspring cohort of non-pregnant women aged 20 to 34 years from the general population of Southampton, UK, recruited through their general practitioners between 1998 and 2002 and characterised before pregnancy; the women who later became pregnant were followed through pregnancy, and their children through infancy and childhood, to study how maternal characteristics and the children's prenatal and postnatal growth affect their development and their risk factors for chronic diseases." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35689423", IAO:0000119="PMID:16195252"}
synonym: "Southampton Womens Survey" RELATED []
