[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002433
name: TAiwan Coronary and Transcatheter intervention
def: "A hospital-based cohort of patients with angina pectoris and objective documentation of myocardial ischaemia who underwent diagnostic coronary angiography or revascularisation at National Taiwan University Hospital at any time after October 2000, with questionnaire data including cardiovascular medication, electronic medical records and fasting blood samples taken before cardiac catheterisation. Collected independently of the similar TCAGEN study at the same hospital, it is one of the seven Taiwan-based cohorts of the TAICHI consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-020-2263-3/MediaObjects/41586_2020_2263_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
