[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002437
name: Comparative Evaluation of Novel Screening Strategies for Colorectal Cancer Screening
def: "A multicentre randomised controlled trial of colorectal cancer screening at six study centres in five Chinese provinces (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan and Yunnan), which from May 2018 recruited adults aged 50–74 years from community-based screening programmes and randomised them to one-time colonoscopy, annual faecal immunochemical testing or a risk-adapted strategy (colonoscopy for high-risk and faecal immunochemical testing for low-risk participants), over four annual screening rounds completed in 2023." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:41851747", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09"}
