[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002438
name: Tasmanian Study of Cognition and Gait
def: "A population-based longitudinal cohort of community-dwelling people aged 60 to 85 randomly selected from the Southern Tasmanian electoral roll in Australia, examined in three phases between 2005 and 2012 with questionnaires, objective gait, cognitive and sensorimotor testing and brain magnetic resonance imaging, to study gait, cognition and brain structure in older people." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:31956917", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:30618725", IAO:0000119="PMID:35363862"}
