id: coho:COHO_0002439
name: TASPRAC Study
def: "The prostate cancer resource of the Menzies Institute for Medical Research, University of Tasmania, in Hobart, made up of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study, begun in the late 1990s, of prostate cancer families of Northern European descent identified through the Menzies Genealogical database, the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and local clinicians, and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study, whose cases were ascertained through the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and whose male controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33436325", IAO:0000119="PMID:39001544"}
