[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002447
name: Tennessee Colorectal Polyp Study
def: "A colonoscopy-based case-control study of colorectal polyps conducted by Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, from 2003 to 2010, which enrolled patients undergoing colonoscopy at the Vanderbilt gastroenterology clinic and the Nashville Veterans Affairs medical centre, taking those found to have adenomatous or hyperplastic polyps as cases and polyp-free patients as controls, to study dietary, lifestyle and genetic risk factors for colorectal polyps." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:39977302", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:39812514", IAO:0000119="PMID:17354224"}
