id: coho:COHO_0002450
name: Twins Eye Study in Tasmania
def: "A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19803772"}
