id: coho:COHO_0002456
name: Tianjin Study
def: "A hospital-based case–control study of breast cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were women with histopathologically diagnosed primary breast cancer recruited consecutively from the Department of Breast Surgery of Tianjin Cancer Institute and Hospital, Tianjin Medical University, and whose controls were women without evidence of cancer who attended health screening at the same hospital, frequency-matched to the cases on age; all participants were unrelated ethnic Han Chinese women who were permanent residents of urban Tianjin. Its study period was 2004 to 2008, and it is one of the participating studies of the Asia Breast Cancer Consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:18629629", IAO:0000119="PMID:21908515"}
