[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002457
name: Trial of Intensified versus standard Medical therapy in Elderly patients with Congestive Heart Failure
def: "A prospective, single-blinded, multicentre randomised trial, run at centres in Switzerland and Germany from 2003 to 2008, in which patients aged 60 years or over with symptomatic congestive heart failure, a heart-failure hospitalisation within the previous year and raised NT-proBNP were randomised to NT-proBNP-guided (intensified) or symptom-guided (standard) medical therapy, to compare the two strategies in patients aged 75 or over and aged 60 to 74, with reduced or preserved ejection fraction." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16644310", IAO:0000119="PMID:33012170"}
