[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002464
name: obsolete Toronto Ovarian Cancer Study
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. Toronto Ovarian Cancer Study is the name the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium's GWAS supplement of PMID:23535730 gives its study TOR, which the consortium's other tables name the Familial Ovarian Tumour Study (PMID:20852632, PMID:21639959). Replaced by COHO:0001738 (Familial Ovarian Tumor Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a search for the cohorts behind placeholder names with no known paper, 2026-09-27.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0001738

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002465
name: Tomsk Study
def: "A family study of asthma conducted from 1998 onwards by the Research Institute of Medical Genetics and Siberian State Medical University in Tomsk, Russia, which recruited nuclear families and extended pedigrees of Russian or mixed East Slavonic origin through probands with atopic bronchial asthma at hospitals in Tomsk and Irkutsk, with probands and relatives clinically examined for asthma and atopy." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
