comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The women of the UK Collaborative Trial of Ovarian Cancer Screening, whose samples the only paper the PGS Catalog records the id in uses (PMID:29730597), are the UKCTOCS Longitudinal Women's Cohort. Replaced by COHO:0002688 (UKCTOCS Longitudinal Women's Cohort), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0002688

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002502
name: UKCVD
def: "A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24795349"}
instance_of: coho:COHO_0000001 ! cohort aggregation
