[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002512
name: UK Prospective Diabetes Study
def: "A multicentre randomised intervention trial in the United Kingdom, begun in 1977 and expanded to 23 centres by 1987, of patients aged 25–65 years with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes, who after initial diet treatment were randomly allocated to intensive blood-glucose control (with a sulphonylurea or insulin, or metformin for overweight patients) or to conventional diet-based treatment, with the Hypertension in Diabetes Study nested in a factorial design comparing tight with less tight blood-pressure control; its participants were followed for diabetic complications and death for decades after the intervention ended." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:40485651", IAO:0000119="PMID:1778353", IAO:0000119="PMID:9742976"}
synonym: "UKPDS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "United Kingdom Prospective Diabetes Study" RELATED []
