[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002518
name: obsolete University of Munich
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The id is ambiguous in PGS005391: there the Catalog lists UM among ADGC datasets (next to UPITT, NIA-LOAD, TARCC, GENADA), and the source paper (PMID:42237039) uses 'UM' only for the University of Miami ('the University of Miami (UM)/Case Western Reserve University (CWRU)/Mt. Sinai School of Medicine (MSSM)'). That paper's own Munich sample is called 'The PAGES study', never UM. So in PGS005391 UM may be the Catalog's reuse of its Munich id for PAGES, or a mis-tag of UM/CWRU/MSSM (placeholder COHO:0002521). This could not be settled from the paper. UM ('University of Munich') is not the university but, in PGS000823's source GWAS (Jonsson et al. 2013, TREM2), the Munich sample of Alzheimer's disease patients from the memory clinic of the Department of Psychiatry, University of Munich (LMU), with population controls randomly selected from Munich. The 2026 consensus meta-analysis supplement describes exactly this sample, in the same sentences, as 'The PAGES study'. COHO already has PAGES as COHO:0000720 'Phenomics and Genomics Sample', whose definition already includes 'Alzheimer's disease patients from the psychiatric memory clinic' and Munich controls. So UM should become an acronym of COHO:0000720. 'University of Munich' is not added as a synonym: it is the institution's name. No other COHO term carries the acronym UM. PAGES is already shared with COHO:0000721 (Paediatric Asthma Gene Environment Study), which is unaffected. See problems for the PGS005391 ambiguity: if the curator reads that use as the University of Miami datasets, the UM tag there belongs with UM/VU/MSSM (COHO:0002521), with a shared-acronym note on both terms. Replaced by COHO:0000720 (Phenomics and Genomics Sample), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000720

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002519
name: obsolete University Medical Center Utrecht
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UMC ('University Medical Center Utrecht') is the PGS Catalog's id for samples that came from UMC Utrecht without a study name, and it covers at least two different sets. In the bladder cancer GWAS it is a pooled Dutch control group: companions of neurology outpatients and controls from a schizophrenia GWAS. In the intracranial aneurysm scores it is the Utrecht intracranial aneurysm patients (UMC Utrecht biobank data). Neither is a cohort with a name or recruitment of its own; the id is the hospital, so it is not a cohort. None of the COHO matches in the evidence is this sample: ALS Utrecht (COHO:0000506) is a 158-person MRI sample, and the Nijmegen Biomedical Study (COHO:0000128, acronym NBS) is the other Dutch control set in the bladder GWAS, which the UMC controls extended but are not part of. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002520
name: obsolete University of Minnesota study
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UMN is the PGS Catalog's id for the systemic lupus erythematosus cases and controls that the University of Minnesota contributed to the multi-ancestry LLAS2 sample of PMID:22523428. The paper's Supplementary Table S1 gives the source only as "UMN (University of Minnesota, USA)" (https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S000349672418630X-mmc1.pdf), with no study name, design or recruitment of its own; it is one institution among some twenty sample sources. The two Europe PMC hits for 'University of Minnesota study' (a 1978 surgical follow-up and the Colon Cancer Control Study) have nothing to do with the id. Not a cohort; no COHO term matches. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

