id: coho:COHO_0002521
name: University of Miami/Vanderbilt University/Mt. Sinai School of Medicine
def: "A case-control collection of late-onset Alzheimer's disease, whose cases met NINCDS-ADRDA criteria for probable or definite Alzheimer's disease with onset after age 60 and whose controls are cognitively healthy, unrelated people from the same catchment areas frequency-matched by age and sex, ascertained at the University of Miami, Vanderbilt University (later Case Western Reserve University) and Mount Sinai School of Medicine, including autopsy-confirmed cases and controls mainly from Mount Sinai; it is one of the datasets of the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium." [] {IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02838-5/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2838_MOESM1_ESM.pdf", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2802/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2802_MOESM27_ESM.pdf"}
