[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002523
name: obsolete University of Noth Carolina Rectal Cancer Study
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UNC-Rectal is the North Carolina Rectal Cancer Study. This is phase II of the North Carolina Colon Cancer Study (NCCCS-II), which COHO already has as COHO:0000597. That term's definition covers phase II: sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer cases, May 2001 to September 2006. The two descriptions match point for point. NCCCS-II (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode): "The North Carolina Colon Cancer Study-Phase II (NCCCS-II) was a population-based case-control study of incident distal large bowel cancer (rectal, recto-sigmoid, or sigmoid cancer) in 33 counties in the central and eastern part of North Carolina.", with cases "identified through the rapid case ascertainment system of the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry between May 2001 and September 2006". UNC-Rectal (E1177.17-E1177.18): the same 33-county area, the same three tumour sites, the same registry, the same dates, and controls from motor-vehicle and Medicare records. Add the catalog's name (typo 'Noth' included, as the catalog tags it) and the study's own names as synonyms, and UNC-Rectal as an acronym. PMID:26683305 also abbreviates this study as 'UNC'. That abbreviation is a paper's shorthand, not the study's acronym or a catalog tag, and COHO:0001179 already carries it, so it is not proposed. The placeholder COHO:0002523 is then a duplicate of COHO:0000597. Replaced by COHO:0000597 (North Carolina Colon Cancer Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: coho:COHO_0000597

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002524
name: Prognostic Modelling in Ischaemic Stroke study
def: "A cohort study of patients with non-disabling cerebral ischaemia of arterial origin referred to the University Medical Center Utrecht, the Netherlands, and included between 1994 and 2009 in the SMART study or the Utrecht Stroke Database, whose patients were genotyped with the Illumina Immunochip and followed up for new vascular events in order to test whether genetic information improves prognostic models for new ischaemic and haemorrhagic events. Its genotyped patients were also the Utrecht Immunochip case sample of genetic association studies of ischaemic stroke." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25906364", IAO:0000119="PMID:26708676", IAO:0000119="PMID:25031287", IAO:0000119="PMID:18264013"}
