[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002525
name: obsolete University of Florida
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UOF is the PGS Catalog's id for 145 African-ancestry DNA samples (61 with type 1 diabetes, 54 controls, 30 with type 2 diabetes) from the University of Florida Diabetes Institute. PMID:30659077 used them as its independent replication group, and PGS sample set PSS000031 carries only this id. The paper names the source only as the University of Florida (E1179.7, E1179.13) and gives no study name, design or recruitment period. The paper's named collections (T1DGC, SEARCH, GoKinD, Barbara Davis Center) are separate sources. Not a cohort. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002526
name: Uppsala Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm Cohort Study
def: "A prospective population-based case-control study of abdominal aortic aneurysm in Uppsala, Sweden, in which all 65-year-old men identified through the National Population Registry were invited to an ultrasound examination; it aims to find biomarkers for the cause and progression of abdominal aortic aneurysm and to investigate how people with and without an aneurysm experience their health." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01510-y/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1510_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
