[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002527
name: URWCI study
def: "A prospective, multicentre observational study of late radiotherapy toxicity that recruited men with prostate cancer without distant metastases who were scheduled for curative-intent radiotherapy (external beam radiotherapy with or without a brachytherapy boost, or brachytherapy alone) between April 2016 and March 2019 at two hospitals in the United States, the University of Rochester Wilmot Cancer Institute and the Medical College of Wisconsin; participants were enrolled before or in the first week of radiotherapy, followed with patient-reported outcomes (the Expanded Prostate Index Composite with added radiation-related questions) at the end of radiotherapy, at 6 months and yearly for up to four years, and genotyped genome-wide, to validate predictive models and biomarkers of toxicity such as hematuria." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35077710", IAO:0000119="PMID:40029246"}
synonym: "RGC-URWCI cohort" RELATED []
synonym: "URWCI" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
