[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002537
name: Val Gardena COVID-19 study
def: "A population-based SARS-CoV-2 study in the Gardena valley (Val Gardena/Gröden) of South Tyrol, Italy, one of the areas most afflicted early in the COVID-19 pandemic, that invited a random sample of the inhabitants of its main municipalities (Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva), stratified by municipality, sex and age group, to answer a questionnaire and undergo a nasopharyngeal swab test and a serological antibody test between 26 May and 8 June 2020, towards the end of the first wave, and stored their biological samples at the Eurac Research Biobank; funded by the Healthcare System of the Autonomous Province of Bolzano/Bozen, it later contributed genotyped participants to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative and participants with confirmed infection to a whole-genome sequencing study of COVID-19 host genetics built on the German COVID-19 Omics Initiative." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:39715278", IAO:0000119="PMID:34237774", IAO:0000119="PMID:34645534"}
synonym: "TOPMed_Gardena" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "topmed_gardena" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "Val Gardena" RELATED []
synonym: "Val Gardena cohort" RELATED []
synonym: "Val Gardena/Gröden study" RELATED []
synonym: "Val_Gardena" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
