[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002539
name: obsolete Van Andel Research Institute
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. VARI is the PGS Catalog's id for a case series in the renal cell carcinoma GWAS of PMID:28598434. It holds about 1,050 kidney cancer patients treated at Spectrum Health Hospital in Grand Rapids, Michigan, and at hospitals of the Cooperative Human Tissue Network, with germline DNA extracted from normal kidney tissue next to the tumour. The supplement calls it only a 'Van Andel Research Institute Case series' (E1193.7), with no study name, recruitment period or design beyond that. Not a cohort. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002540
name: Viborg Aneurysm Screening Study
def: "A single-centre randomised controlled trial of screening for abdominal aortic aneurysm in Viborg County, Denmark, which randomised all men born in 1921–29 who lived in the county in 1994, and those who turned 65 in 1995–98, either to an invitation to abdominal ultrasound screening or to a control group; men found to have an aneurysm of 30–49 mm were offered annual surveillance." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:15757960", IAO:0000119="PMID:32158272"}
synonym: "VCAAA" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
