[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002547
name: Vioxx in Colorectal Cancer Therapy: Definition of Optimal Regime
def: "A phase III, placebo-controlled randomized trial of the COX-2 inhibitor rofecoxib (Vioxx) in patients from throughout the United Kingdom who had undergone potentially curative surgery and completed adjuvant therapy for stage II or III colorectal cancer, testing whether rofecoxib reduced recurrence and improved survival; it was terminated early by the worldwide withdrawal of rofecoxib. Its patients, together with those of the QUASAR2 trial, form the VQ58 case series of colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22634755", IAO:0000119="PMID:20972440", IAO:0000119="PMID:20837956", IAO:0000119="PMID:24062397"}
subset: coho1:PGS_subset
synonym: "VICTOR" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "VICTOR trial" RELATED []
