property_value: IAO:0000112 "PMID:22634755" xsd:string {dcterms:title="Common variation near CDKN1A, POLD3 and SHROOM2 influences colorectal cancer risk.", xref="PMID:22634755", xref="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4747430/", comment="The VQ58 GWAS comprised 1,800 CRC cases from the UK-based VICTOR and QUASAR2 adjuvant chemotherapy clinical trials."}

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002548
name: obsolete Valencia Institute of Oncology
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The id is on the PGS Catalog's cohort reference list but has no released score, sample set or publication (REST record empty, no papers in cohort_papers.json), so there is no PGS paper to read. VIO is the PGS Catalog's reference-list entry for the Valencia Institute of Oncology (Fundación Instituto Valenciano de Oncología, Valencia, Spain), a cancer hospital. No released PGS score, sample set or publication uses it. The only literature under this name is clinical case series and affiliations of the institute's clinicians. Its melanoma patients appear in consortium genetics papers as part of the MelaNostrum Consortium ('Spain (Valencia, Barcelona)'), not as a named study. Nothing shows a defined, named collection behind the id, so the name denotes only the institution. Not a cohort. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002549
name: Västerbotten Intervention Project
def: "An ongoing population-based cohort study initiated in 1985 in which all residents of Västerbotten County, Sweden, are invited to a health examination at ages 40, 50 and 60, with blood drawn for cryopreservation; one of the three sub-surveys of the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, used for nested case–control studies of cancer and cardiovascular disease and for evaluating polygenic risk scores." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:41419686", dcterms:contributor="Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35396534"}
