[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002556
name: Women's Circle of Health Study
def: "A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:29073238", IAO:0000119="PMID:19865486", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:24113797", IAO:0000119="PMID:33024820"}
