[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002557
name: obsolete Womens Cancer Program at the Samuel Oschin Comprehensive Cancer Institute
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. WCPSOCCI is the PGS Catalog's id for OCAC's study LAX: ovarian cancer patients of the Women's Cancer Program at the Samuel Oschin Comprehensive Cancer Institute, Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, collected since 1989 with data taken from medical records (PMC5625672 Table 1; PMID:28346442). OCAC names it only by the programme and the acronym LAX. It has no study name, design or defined recruitment of its own beyond being the programme's patients, so it is an unnamed institutional collection. Not a cohort. The CIMBA group from the same programme is E1212 (WCRI). Cedars-Sinai's MIRIAD IBD biobank (COHO:0000716) is unrelated. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002558
name: obsolete Womens Cancer Research Institute - Cedars-Sinai Medical Center
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. WCRI is the PGS Catalog's id for CIMBA's group WCP: BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers from the Women's Cancer Program at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles (PMID:32665703 supplement; PMID:28346442; PMID:29058716). CIMBA names the group only by the clinical programme, with no study name or recruitment protocol of its own. That matches how other CIMBA institution groups in this review were decided (UPENN, UCSF, MSKCC, FCCC, KUMC and OUH are all 'not a cohort'). Not a cohort. The same programme's OCAC contribution is E1211 (WCPSOCCI). Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002559
name: Wuhan Diabetes Study
def: "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:20862305", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22109280", IAO:0000119="https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008"}
synonym: "WDS" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
