[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002562
name: Wessex family study
def: "A UK family-based collection of white families recruited from the Southampton area, each with at least two biological siblings aged 5 to 21 years with a current physician's diagnosis of asthma who were taking asthma medication regularly, originally recruited in collaboration with Genome Therapeutics Corporation and Schering-Plough for the study that identified ADAM33 as an asthma gene, and later used to test asthma genetic associations by transmission disequilibrium tests." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:12728163", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:21696813"}
