[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002566
name: Women's Health Initiative Clinical Trial
def: "The randomised clinical trial component of the Women's Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:36797788", IAO:0000119="PMID:9492970"}
