[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002568
name: Women's Health Initiative Hormone Therapy Trials
def: "The hormone therapy component of the Women's Health Initiative: two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years were enrolled between 1993 and 1998 at 40 clinical centers across the United States and randomized to estrogen alone (women without a uterus) or estrogen plus progestin versus placebo; the estrogen plus progestin and estrogen-alone trials were stopped early in 2002 and 2004, and participants were then followed without intervention." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:31676865", IAO:0000119="PMID:21036692"}
