[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002569
name: Women's Health Initiative Long Life Study
def: "An ancillary study of the Women's Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:32680817", IAO:0000119="PMID:35522983", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
