[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002570
name: Wheezing Illnesses Study Leidsche Rijn
def: "A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio)." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37713433", IAO:0000119="PMID:15499901"}
