id: coho:COHO_0002571
name: Whitehall II Study
def: "A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28642251", IAO:0000119="PMID:22223828", IAO:0000119="PMID:23843750"}
