[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002572
name: Wuhan-Zhuhai Cohort
def: "A community-based prospective cohort of residents aged 18 to 80 of sampled communities in Wuhan (Hubei province) and Zhuhai (Guangdong province), China, who had lived there for more than five years, recruited in April–May 2011 in Wuhan and May 2012 in Zhuhai with questionnaires, physical examination, spirometry and blood and urine samples, and followed up every three years to study how exposure to air particulate matter and other environmental pollutants affects the respiratory and cardiovascular systems." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:25252923"}
