[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002573
name: obsolete Westmead Institute for Cancer Research
comment: Obsoleted 2026-09-24. WICR is the PGS Catalog's id for the Westmead Institute for Cancer Research, a research institute of the University of Sydney at Westmead (Sydney, Australia). The Catalog records no score or sample set for it, no GWAS Catalog study uses it, and in the literature 'WICR' labels the institute itself: an author affiliation in breast and ovarian cancer genetics papers, and the code of the Sydney/Westmead melanoma-family group in GenoMEL (PMID:18394881). No study or collection is named after it, so it denotes an institution, not a cohort. Samples from Westmead enter named cohorts that COHO already has, such as the Australian Ovarian Cancer Study (COHO:0000014), the Australian Melanoma Family Study (COHO:0001277) and GenoMEL (COHO:0001335), but no source ties the id WICR to any one of them. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24.
is_obsolete: true

[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002574
name: Women's Insights and Shared Experiences Study
def: "A population-based pair of case-control studies, one of endometrial cancer and one of breast cancer, among white and African American women aged 50 to 79 in the Philadelphia area of Pennsylvania and New Jersey, United States, examining exogenous hormone use, parity and estrogen-related genes: cases diagnosed between July 1999 and June 2002 were identified through hospitals and the Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, and controls from the same area by random-digit dialling. Its endometrial cancer study is one of the studies of the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19124504", IAO:0000119="PMID:19028704", IAO:0000119="PMID:18757329"}
