[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002576
name: Wuhan Lung Cancer Study
def: "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Wuhan, China, whose cases were consecutive patients with lung cancer at Wuhan Zhongnan Hospital, without restriction on age, sex or histology but excluding those with a previous cancer or an unknown history of radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were cancer-free outpatients of other clinics of the same hospital in the same period, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and urban or rural residence; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:20700438", IAO:0000119="PMID:23143601"}
