[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002588
name: Young Adult Hodgkin's Disease Case-Control Study
def: "A UK population-based case-control study of Hodgkin's disease in young adults aged 16 to 24 years, whose cases were those newly diagnosed between October 1991 and May 1995 in the Yorkshire, Wessex and South West Family Health Service Authority areas and parts of Cumbria and Lancashire, ascertained by the methods of the Leukaemia Research Fund Data Collection Study, and whose controls, two per case, were randomly selected from people registered with general practitioners in the study area and matched on sex, year of birth and area of residence. It was set up to test the late host response model of young adult Hodgkin's disease and whether it differs between Epstein-Barr virus-positive and -negative disease, and its cases were later genotyped for genome-wide association studies of classical Hodgkin lymphoma, among them the European Collaborative Study." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:22286212", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:10737396", IAO:0000119="PMID:24920014", IAO:0000119="PMID:20308568"}
