[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002591
name: Academia Sinica Multicentered Young-Onset Hypertension Genetic Study
def: "A multicentre study run from Academia Sinica, Taiwan, of Han Chinese patients with young-onset essential hypertension, first diagnosed between the ages of 20 and 51, with secondary hypertension, diabetes and a body mass index of 35 kg/m2 or more excluded. Lymphoblastoid cell lines were established for its patients, who, with normotensive controls from other Taiwanese studies, have been used in genome-wide association, gene-expression and candidate-gene studies of hypertension, blood pressure, adiponectin and ACE activity." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:19421330", IAO:0000119="PMID:21771975", IAO:0000119="PMID:23469169", IAO:0000119="PMID:29379041"}
