id: coho:COHO_0002596
name: Cardiovascular Effects of Air Pollution and Noise in Stockholm
def: "A pooling of four population-based cohorts from Stockholm County, Sweden (the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Programme, a random sample of 60-year-olds known as SIXTY, the Stockholm-resident participants of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study, and the Swedish National Study on Aging and Care in Kungsholmen), recruited between 1992 and 2004 and analysed together to study long-term exposure to ambient air pollution and noise as risk factors for cardiovascular disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:29016987", IAO:0000119="PMID:34497075", IAO:0000119="PMID:35270332"}
