[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002600
name: Dutch Famine Birth Cohort
def: "A historical birth cohort of singletons born alive and at term in the Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, around the time of the 1944–1945 Dutch famine (1943–1947), traced and studied by Amsterdam UMC since 1994 through repeated interviews, examinations, biological samples, imaging and registry linkage, to investigate the effects of acute maternal undernutrition during specific stages of gestation on later health, particularly cardiovascular and metabolic disease, ageing and mental health." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33664071", IAO:0000119="https://www.hongerwinter.nl/"}
subset: coho1:GEC_subset
