[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002606
name: Rhea Study
def: "A population-based mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the prefecture of Heraklion, Crete, Greece, recruited at their first major ultrasound examination around week 12 of gestation at four prenatal clinics in Heraklion from February 2007 to February 2008, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy towards young adulthood to study how environmental, dietary and other early-life exposures affect the health of mothers and children, with a focus on childhood obesity." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33407552", IAO:0000119="https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/RHEA", IAO:0000119="PMID:25970502"}
