[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002627
name: Central European Longitudinal Studies of Parents and Children: Young Adults
def: "A follow-up study, begun in 2019 at Masaryk University in Brno, Czech Republic, of the young adults born in 1991 and 1992 who took part in the Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood, joined by their siblings and partners and by others born in those years, who are examined clinically, give blood, urine and buccal samples and answer questionnaires, to study how lifestyle, social and environmental factors relate to early signs of chronic disease." [] {IAO:0000119="https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:38820320"}
