[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002638
name: Rome Longitudinal Study
def: "An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:35641005", IAO:0000119="PMID:37944432", IAO:0000119="https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS"}
