[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002641
name: International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements Project-DYAD-Malawi
def: "The participants of a randomised, single-blind controlled trial in rural Malawi (Mangochi, University of Malawi College of Medicine with Tampere University), part of the International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements (iLiNS) Project: pregnant women enrolled from 2011, and later their infants. The women received small-quantity lipid-based nutrient supplements, multiple micronutrients or iron-folic acid during pregnancy and lactation, and the infants were followed to test effects on birth size, child growth and development, with a later follow-up of the children at 9 years." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:25646337", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD", IAO:0000119="https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01239693"}
