[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002652
name: Infants' Environmental Health Study
def: "A prospective community-based birth cohort of pregnant women aged 15 or over living in 40 villages of Matina County, Limón, Costa Rica, within 5 km of large-scale banana plantations where the fungicide mancozeb is sprayed from the air, enrolled from March 2010 to June 2011 by the Central American Institute for Studies on Toxic Substances (IRET) of the Universidad Nacional, and their children, followed to study the effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children's growth, neurodevelopment and respiratory health and on the mothers' health." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119=" PMID:29847083 ", IAO:0000119=" https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ISA", IAO:0000119="PMID:25198283 "}
subset: coho1:GEC_subset
