[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002655
name: Maule Cohort
def: "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 38 to 74 years living in the agricultural county of Molina, in the Maule Region of central Chile, identified through a household census and enrolled from December 2014 by the Advanced Center for Chronic Diseases (ACCDiS) of the Universidad de Chile and the Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile, with questionnaires, physical examinations, ultrasound and a biobank of blood, urine and saliva, and followed with repeat visits and surveillance of hospital events to study the natural history and environmental, lifestyle and social determinants of chronic diseases such as cardiometabolic diseases and cancer." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119=" https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAUCO", IAO:0000119="PMID:26847446 "}
