[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002658
name: Cohorts Consortium of Latin America and the Caribbean
def: "A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:32888015", IAO:0000119="PMID:39687239"}
subset: coho1:GEC_subset
synonym: "CC-LAC" RELATED OMO:0003000 []
synonym: "The Cohorts Consortium of Latin America and the Caribbean (CC-LAC)" RELATED []
xref: https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CC-LAC
instance_of: coho:COHO_0000001 ! cohort aggregation
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Argentina
relationship: coho:has_data_collection_location http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brazil {xref="https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML", comment="The aforementioned 7 cohorts that have not been pooled because cardiovascular outcomes are not yet available include: CRONICAS Cohort Study (Peru),27 Mexican Health & Aging Study (Mexico),28 Puerto Rican Elderly Health Conditions (Puerto Rico),29 Costa Rican Longevity and Healthy Aging Study (CRELES) 1945–1955 Retirement Cohort (Costa Rica),30 Influence of Biopsychosocial Factors on the Survival of the Elderly in Northeast Brazil—A Prospective Study (Brazil),31 Baependi Heart Study (Brazil)32 and MONICA-VITÓRIA study (Brazil)."}
