[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002680
name: Iganga-Mayuge Health and Demographic Surveillance Site
def: "A health and demographic surveillance system following the largely rural population of villages in the Iganga and Mayuge districts of eastern Uganda, established in the mid-2000s by Makerere University with the two districts and Karolinska Institutet and run by the Makerere University Centre for Health and Population Research, which records pregnancies, births, deaths and other events in census rounds and links household data with health facility records, as a platform for population health research and research training." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:28799450", IAO:0000119="PMID:35427403", IAO:0000119="PMID:40018598"}
