[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002686
name: Personalized Environment and Genes Study
def: "A cohort of demographically diverse adults recruited in North Carolina since 2002 by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, first as the Environmental Polymorphisms Registry, who complete surveys on health, exposures, diet and lifestyle, give biological samples and are genotyped, with geocoded residential data, to study how environment, lifestyle and genes act together on disease." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:41927563"}
