[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002687
name: Newfoundland and Labrador Genome Project
def: "A general population cohort of adults in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada, established by the company Sequence Bioinformatics (Sequence Bio) of St. John's and recruiting from 2019, whose participants, aged 18 and over with a valid provincial health card, were recruited at random from general practice clinics across the province and gave medical history and saliva samples for genotyping, to characterise the genetics of the province's founder population and find genetic causes of disease." [] {IAO:0000119="https://atlas.ihccglobal.org/", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:37117635"}
subset: coho1:IHCC_subset
