id: coho:COHO_0002691
name: Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes Cohort
def: "A collaborative cohort study funded in 2016 by the US National Institutes of Health within the Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes (ECHO) Program, bringing together existing and new pregnancy and paediatric cohorts across the United States and Puerto Rico under a common data collection protocol to study how early-life environmental exposures affect pre-, peri- and postnatal outcomes, airway health, obesity, neurodevelopment and positive health in children." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:36963379", dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="https://echochildren.org/"}
