[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002693
name: China Patient-centered Evaluative Assessment of Cardiac Events Million Persons Project
def: "A government-funded, population-based cardiovascular screening cohort run by the National Center for Cardiovascular Diseases (Fuwai Hospital, Beijing) that, after a pilot in four provinces, enrolled community-dwelling residents aged 35 to 75 years at urban districts and rural counties in all 31 provinces of mainland China from 2014, with blood pressure, anthropometric and lipid measurements and a health questionnaire, and gave further assessment, counselling and follow-up to those at high risk, to identify people at high risk of cardiovascular disease and support research on its prevention." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:26729395", IAO:0000119="PMID:33038086"}
