[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002694
name: Africa Centre Demographic Information System
def: "An open population cohort of all resident and non-resident members of households in a demographic and health surveillance area in the uMkhanyakude district of rural KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, established in 2000 by the Africa Centre for Health and Population Studies (now the Africa Health Research Institute) and expanded and renamed the Population Intervention Platform in 2017, with repeated household surveillance and population-based HIV surveys, to describe the demographic, social and health impact of the HIV epidemic, and later of tuberculosis and non-communicable diseases, and to evaluate interventions." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:33437994"}
