[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002697
name: South African Population Research Infrastructure Network
def: "A national network, established in 2016 by South Africa's Department of Science and Innovation and hosted by the South African Medical Research Council, that harmonises the longitudinal population surveillance of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa, starting from the rural Agincourt, DIMAMO and Africa Health Research Institute HDSSs and extending to urban nodes, to provide up-to-date longitudinal health, demographic and socioeconomic data for research and national policy." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="http://saprin.mrc.ac.za/", IAO:0000119="PMID:34966919"}
subset: coho1:IHCC_subset
