[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002699
name: Vorarlberg Health Monitoring and Prevention Programme
def: "A population-based cohort of adult residents of Vorarlberg, the westernmost province of Austria, enrolled from 1985 through a routine risk-factor surveillance and prevention programme run by the Agency for Social and Preventive Medicine, in which local physicians carried out a physical examination, blood test and consultation, and followed by linkage to the Vorarlberg cancer registry and death index to study metabolic and other risk factors for cancer, cardiovascular disease and mortality." [] {dcterms:contributor="Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:16234822", IAO:0000119="PMID:19380371"}
