[Instance]
id: coho:COHO_0002705
name: Phenotyping Young-Onset Atrial Fibrillation Patients study
def: "An observational cohort of adults with atrial fibrillation first diagnosed before age 60, recruited at the outpatient clinic of the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, in 2012–2013, combining retrospective information near the first diagnosis with prospective follow-up to characterize their clinical and familial profile, atrial fibrillation progression and cardiovascular outcomes." [] {dcterms:contributor="GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:31890859", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
