id: coho:COHO_0002707
name: Glycometabolic Intervention as adjunct to Primary percutaneous intervention in ST elevation myocardial infarction (GIPS)-III trial
def: "A single-centre, double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled trial at the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, that recruited patients without diabetes undergoing primary percutaneous coronary intervention for ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction in 2011–2013, to test whether four months of metformin treatment preserved left ventricular function." [] {IAO:0000119="PMID:24687169", dcterms:contributor="GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09", IAO:0000119="PMID:22968678", IAO:0000119="https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf"}
